1
00:00:00,590 --> 00:00:07,780
欢迎来到 AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner 考试（代码为 CLF-C02）的完整课程。
Welcome to the complete course for the AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner Exam exam code CLF-C02.

2
00:00:08,654 --> 00:00:15,972
在接下来的几个小时里，我们将涵盖考试大纲中提到的每一个领域，以及一些没被明确列出但会考到的内容。
Over the next several hours, we will cover every domain the exam guide names and a few things it does not name but does test.

3
00:00:16,910 --> 00:00:19,396
让我们先从你即将面临的考试情况开始。
Let us start with what you are actually walking into.

4
00:00:21,102 --> 00:00:24,772
在开始之前，有一件最重要的事情需要你理解。
Here is the single most useful thing to understand before you begin.

5
00:00:25,134 --> 00:00:29,060
几乎没有人是因为没听说过某个服务而挂掉这个考试的。
Almost nobody fails this exam because they have never heard of a service.

6
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:33,348
他们失败的原因是四个选项听起来都像正确答案，而且时间一直在流逝。
They fail because four options all sound plausible and the clock is running.

7
00:00:33,870 --> 00:00:36,388
本课程中的每个模块都是围绕这一点构建的。
Every module in this course is built around that.

8
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:43,940
我们不仅讲解一个服务的功能，还会说明它容易被混淆成什么，以及题目中哪个词能把它们区分开来。
We do not just say what a service does, we say what it is confused with and what word in the question separates them.

9
00:00:45,646 --> 00:00:46,852
先说考试形式。
The format first.

10
00:00:47,930 --> 00:00:49,850
在 90 分钟内完成 65 道题。
65 questions in 90 minutes.

11
00:00:50,574 --> 00:00:53,732
其中只有 50 道计入你的分数。
Only 50 of those count towards your score.

12
00:00:55,790 --> 00:00:58,308
剩下的 15 道是试题。
The other 15 are trial questions.

13
00:00:58,640 --> 00:01:05,924
AWS 在测试未来的考试内容，而且这些题目不会被标出，所以请把每一道题都当作计分题来对待。
AWS is testing for future exams and they are not identified, so treat every question as if it counts.

14
00:01:06,542 --> 00:01:08,560
你需要在 1000 分中拿到 700 分。
You need 700 out of 1000.

15
00:01:09,742 --> 00:01:12,996
这是一个比例计分，而不是简单的百分比。
That is a scaled score, not a raw percentage.

16
00:01:13,294 --> 00:01:16,580
所以不要去计算你可以错答多少题。
So do not try to compute how many you can afford to miss.

17
00:01:18,094 --> 00:01:19,972
这里有两个非常重要的点。
Two things matter enormously here.

18
00:01:20,334 --> 00:01:23,876
猜测没有扣分，而且评分是补偿性的。
There is no penalty for guessing, and the scoring is compensatory.

19
00:01:24,270 --> 00:01:28,708
补偿性意味着某个较弱的领域不会导致你直接挂科。
Compensatory means a weak domain cannot fail you on its own.

20
00:01:29,902 --> 00:01:30,980
共有四个领域。
Four domains.

21
00:01:31,360 --> 00:01:36,000
云概念占 24%，安全性与合规性占 30%。
Cloud concepts at 24%, security and compliance at 30%.

22
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:39,200
云技术与服务占 34%。
Cloud technology and services at 34%.

23
00:01:40,110 --> 00:01:42,560
计费、定价和支持占 12%。
Billing, pricing, and support at 12%.

24
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:46,052
注意，安全性几乎占据了考试的三分之一。
Notice that security is nearly a third of the exam.

25
00:01:46,894 --> 00:01:51,040
有技术背景的人往往会略过这一部分，因为觉得它像是些繁琐的文书工作。
People coming from a technical background often skim it because it feels like paperwork.

26
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:54,640
这是这个考试中最常见且可以避免的错误。
That is the most common preventable mistake in this exam.

27
00:01:56,174 --> 00:01:59,844
关于本课程构建方式的一点说明，因为它决定了你该如何使用它。
A word on how this was built because it changes how you should use it.

28
00:02:00,558 --> 00:02:06,212
我们分析了 918 道练习题，以找出这个考试反复出现的决策点。
918 practice questions were analyzed to work out which decisions this exam keeps coming back to.

29
00:02:06,720 --> 00:02:08,804
这些题目不会在这里重复出现。
Those questions are not reproduced here.

30
00:02:09,741 --> 00:02:17,828
简单地重复练习题只会让你学会识别那些特定的题目，而当正式考卷的措辞不同时，这种做法几乎没有意义。
Reproducing a bank trains you to recognize those exact questions, which is worth very little when the real paper phrases things differently.

31
00:02:18,254 --> 00:02:24,708
相反，本课程中的每个案例都是原创的，是根据分析出的决策点编写的。
Instead, every scenario in this course is original, written around the decision the analysis found.

32
00:02:25,102 --> 00:02:29,316
每一项解释都追溯到当前的 AWS 文档。
Every explanation traces back to current AWS documentation.

33
00:02:31,054 --> 00:02:35,396
现在有一件你需要在开头就听到的事情，而不是等到第 15 模块才发现。
Now for something you need to hear at the start rather than discover in module 15.

34
00:02:36,078 --> 00:02:40,772
认证内容的更新往往滞后于 AWS 目录，有时甚至超过一年。
Certification content lags the AWS catalog, sometimes by more than a year.

35
00:02:41,040 --> 00:02:47,524
考试中有些服务虽然是正确答案，但对于新客户来说可能已经非常接近新产品、被重命名或计划停用。
There are services on this exam that are correct answers and are also close to new customers, renamed or scheduled for shutdown.

36
00:02:48,240 --> 00:02:53,444
如果你只根据当前的 AWS 文档来学习，你可能会在这些题目上出错。
If you study from current AWS documentation alone, you will get some of these wrong.

37
00:02:53,760 --> 00:02:59,236
如果你只从旧的题库中学习，你会相信一些不再成立的事实。
If you study only from an old question bank, you will believe things that are no longer true.

38
00:03:00,430 --> 00:03:10,372
这是简短版本，稍后的一个完整模块会详细讲解。Snow 系列非常接近新客户，且 Snowball 的支持将于今年年底结束。
Here is the short version and a whole module later covers it properly. The Snow family is close to new customers and snowball support ends at the end of this year.

39
00:03:11,320 --> 00:03:13,092
QuickSight 已经被重命名过两次。
QuickSight has been renamed twice.

40
00:03:13,646 --> 00:03:17,124
整个 AWS 支持计划系列正在被更换。
The entire AWS support plan lineup is being replaced.

41
00:03:17,934 --> 00:03:22,052
Code Catalyst 和 Code Commit 都非常接近新客户。
Code Catalyst and Code Commit are both close to new customers.

42
00:03:22,542 --> 00:03:25,250
SageMaker 现在被称为 SageMaker。
SageMaker is now called SageMaker.

43
00:03:25,646 --> 00:03:27,480
考试指南中的 AI 部分。
AI in the exam guide.

44
00:03:28,494 --> 00:03:30,660
在所有情况下，规则都是一样的。
In every case, the rule is the same.

45
00:03:31,374 --> 00:03:37,860
根据记录的考试目录来回答问题，并了解实际情况，这样你在打开控制台时才不会感到困惑。
Answer from the documented exam catalog and know the reality so you are not confused when you open the console.

46
00:03:39,502 --> 00:03:41,348
这是接下来的内容结构。
Here is the shape of what is ahead.

47
00:03:41,614 --> 00:03:43,620
四个关于云概念的模块。
Four modules on cloud concepts.

48
00:03:43,950 --> 00:03:46,980
五个关于安全性和合规性的模块，这是最大的领域。
Five on security and compliance, which is the largest domain.

49
00:03:47,520 --> 00:03:51,908
八个关于云技术和服务的模块，因为那个部分涵盖的内容最广。
Eight on cloud technology and services, because that section covers the most ground.

50
00:03:52,160 --> 00:03:54,436
三个关于账单、定价和支持的模块。
3 on billing, pricing, and support.

51
00:03:55,182 --> 00:04:03,204
然后是 3 个关于易混淆对、考试内容变化以及考试技巧本身的跨领域模块。
Then 3 cross-cutting modules on confusion pairs, on what has changed under the exam, and on exam technique itself.

52
00:04:03,630 --> 00:04:07,520
最后，是 3 套每套 20 道题的模拟考试。
Finally, 3 practice exams of 20 questions each.

53
00:04:07,680 --> 00:04:14,240
总共大约是 7 个多一点小时。这些模块并非刻意设计成等长的。
That is roughly 7 and a quarter hours in total. The modules are deliberately not equal lengths.

54
00:04:14,830 --> 00:04:18,244
每个模块的大小都是根据考试实际考查内容的多少来确定的。
Each one is sized by how much the exam actually tests it.

55
00:04:19,790 --> 00:04:22,320
这是一个学习路径，而不是简单的内容列表。
A study route rather than a contents list.

56
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:26,820
请按顺序观看，因为后面的模块会用到前面模块提到的词汇。
Watch in order because later modules assume vocabulary from earlier ones.

57
00:04:27,374 --> 00:04:31,012
当场景幻灯片暂停时，请真的停下来并确定一个答案。
When a scenario slide pauses, actually pause and commit to an answer.

58
00:04:31,470 --> 00:04:35,428
在不先回答的情况下只看讲解，几乎学不到任何东西。
Watching a walkthrough without answering first teaches you almost nothing.

59
00:04:36,430 --> 00:04:39,844
因为你同意了每一个步骤，所以你会觉得自己在学习。
It feels like learning because you agree with every step.

60
00:04:40,320 --> 00:04:46,320
在完成教学模块后进行模拟考试 1，并按领域而非总分来计算得分。
Take practice exam 1 after the teaching modules and score it by domain rather than by total.

61
00:04:46,574 --> 00:04:48,676
只重温你最弱的领域。
Rewatch only your weakest domain.

62
00:04:49,040 --> 00:04:50,308
然后再做模拟题 2。
Then exam 2.

63
00:04:50,798 --> 00:04:52,900
然后在考试前留出几天时间。
Then leave several days before exam.

64
00:04:53,582 --> 00:04:54,000
3。
3.

65
00:04:54,926 --> 00:04:56,420
这个间隔是关键。
That gap is the point.

66
00:04:57,358 --> 00:05:01,476
复习你已经掌握的内容虽然让人舒服，但毫无进展。
Revising what you already know is comfortable and moves nothing.

67
00:05:03,310 --> 00:05:04,560
一些惯例。
Some conventions.

68
00:05:05,422 --> 00:05:11,492
幻灯片底部的橙色条是考试要点。如果你每张幻灯片只记一个笔记，就记那个。
The amber bar at the bottom of a slide is the exam takeaway. If you take one note per slide, take that one.

69
00:05:12,590 --> 00:05:15,972
左侧边缘的标记按领域权重划分。
The marker running down the left edge is split by domain weight.

70
00:05:16,654 --> 00:05:21,668
顶部的片段告诉你当前位置，这样你就能在不死记硬背的情况下掌握权重分配。
The lid segment tells you where you are, so you absorb the weighting without memorizing it.

71
00:05:22,318 --> 00:05:24,292
绿色点表示正确或建议的做法。
Green points are true or advisable.

72
00:05:24,686 --> 00:05:26,052
红色点是陷阱。
Red points are traps.

73
00:05:26,542 --> 00:05:31,268
而且在每个案例中，错误选项的解释和正确答案一样详尽。
And in every work scenario, the wrong answers get explained as carefully as the right one.

74
00:05:31,982 --> 00:05:37,700
这是刻意为之的，因为理解为什么干扰项错误，可以帮助你应对从未见过的题目。
That is deliberate because understanding why a distractor fails transfers to questions you have never seen.

75
00:05:39,310 --> 00:05:40,644
最后一次校准。
One last calibration.

76
00:05:41,120 --> 00:05:47,012
AWS 将目标考生描述为有最多六个月 AWS 云经验的人。
AWS describes the target candidate as someone with up to six months of exposure to the AWS cloud.

77
00:05:48,078 --> 00:05:57,636
考试指南明确列出编码、设计云架构、故障排除、实施和负载测试均属于超出范围。
The exam guide explicitly lists coding, designing cloud architecture, troubleshooting, implementation, and load testing as out of scope.

78
00:05:58,542 --> 00:06:05,252
如果你在担心手动编写策略文档或计算实例系列的规模，那你考的内容就超纲了。
If you are worrying about writing policy documents by hand or sizing instance families, you are studying above the level.

79
00:06:05,614 --> 00:06:08,324
在这里，广度永远比深度更重要。
Breadth beats depth here every time.

80
00:06:10,158 --> 00:06:11,588
那么，什么样的状态才算准备好了呢？
So what does ready look like?

81
00:06:12,942 --> 00:06:17,280
你能用一句话说明每个在范围内的服务是用来做什么的。
You can say in one sentence what each in-scope service is for.

82
00:06:17,440 --> 00:06:25,680
你能区分两个听起来很像的服务，并注意到限定词，比如“成本效益最高”和“运维开销最低”这些点
You can separate two services that sound alike and you notice the qualifier words because most cost-effective and least operational overhead point

83
00:06:25,840 --> 00:06:27,760
指向截然不同的答案。
at genuinely different answers.

84
00:06:28,238 --> 00:06:33,252
不属于准备好的状态是死记硬背实例系列或价格表。
What ready does not look like is memorized instance families or pricing tables.

85
00:06:33,614 --> 00:06:35,300
这些内容在考试中都不会考到。
None of that is on this exam.

86
00:06:35,886 --> 00:06:36,676
让我们开始吧。
Let us begin.

87
00:06:39,630 --> 00:06:42,560
本模块涵盖领域一的前半部分。
This module covers the first half of domain one.

88
00:06:43,022 --> 00:06:47,492
为什么组织转向云端，以及这样做后他们的成本会发生什么变化。
Why organizations move to the cloud and what happens to their costs when they do.

89
00:06:48,078 --> 00:06:50,148
这看起来像是考试中比较简单的部分。
It looks like the soft part of the exam.

90
00:06:50,480 --> 00:06:51,300
但并不是。
It is not.

91
00:06:52,142 --> 00:06:58,756
这里的题目由一个词汇决定，如果你选错了对应的优势名称，就拿不到分数，
Questions here are decided by one vocabulary word, and if you pick the wrong benefit name, you lose the mark,

92
00:06:59,598 --> 00:07:01,348
哪怕你的逻辑推导是正确的。
even though your reasoning was fine.

93
00:07:02,894 --> 00:07:04,420
这是这个领域的考点分布。
Here is the shape of this domain.

94
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:10,756
题目会描述公司发生了一些好的变化，你得把对应的 AWS 优势名称匹配上去。
A scenario describes something good happening to a company, and you have to attach the correct AWS benefit name to it.

95
00:07:11,120 --> 00:07:12,868
启动更快就是敏捷性。
Faster launches is agility.

96
00:07:13,294 --> 00:07:15,204
能够从故障中恢复就是弹性。
Surviving of failure is resilience.

97
00:07:15,950 --> 00:07:20,356
因为 AWS 规模巨大，所以单价更低就是规模经济。
Lower unit prices, because AWS is enormous, is economies of scale.

98
00:07:20,878 --> 00:07:22,756
这些场景的变化是无穷无尽的。
The scenarios vary endlessly.

99
00:07:23,502 --> 00:07:30,500
如果你不精确记住这些名称，这个领域就会变成纯粹靠机械记忆。
The list of names does not learn the names precisely, and this domain becomes almost mechanical.

100
00:07:32,174 --> 00:07:36,580
这是标准的六大优势列表，值得作为一个整体来记忆。
This is the canonical list of six advantages, and it is worth memorizing as a set.

101
00:07:36,960 --> 00:07:39,428
用可变支出代替资本支出。
Trade capital expense for variable expense.

102
00:07:39,760 --> 00:07:41,956
受益于巨大的规模经济。
Benefit from massive economies of scale.

103
00:07:42,320 --> 00:07:43,680
不再猜测容量。
Stop guessing capacity.

104
00:07:43,886 --> 00:07:45,572
提高速度和敏捷性。
Increase speed and agility.

105
00:07:45,920 --> 00:07:48,868
不再花钱去运行和维护数据中心。
Stop spending money running and maintaining data centers.

106
00:07:49,838 --> 00:07:51,492
并且在几分钟内走向全球。
And go global in minutes.

107
00:07:51,886 --> 00:08:00,644
注意其中一些听起来很像。不再猜测容量，以及提高速度和敏捷性。这两者都描述了灵活性带来的良好结果。
Notice how similar some of them sound. Stop guessing capacity and increase speed and agility. Both describe good outcomes from flexibility.

108
00:08:00,880 --> 00:08:02,980
考试会要求你把它们区分开来。
The exam will make you separate them.

109
00:08:04,270 --> 00:08:06,864
资本支出对比可变支出。
Capital expense against variable expense.

110
00:08:07,104 --> 00:08:16,356
在本地部署时，你在任何东西运行之前就要支付一大笔费用。至于容量，你是靠猜测的，而且无论你用不用，这些硬件都在贬值。
On premises, you pay a large sum before anything runs. For capacity, you guessed at, and that hardware depreciates whether you use it or not.

111
00:08:16,974 --> 00:08:19,556
而在 AWS 上，你只需为实际消耗的内容付费。
On AWS, you pay for what you consume.

112
00:08:19,984 --> 00:08:22,788
当资源停止运行时，计费也就停止了。
And when the resource stops, the charge stops.

113
00:08:23,630 --> 00:08:25,796
注意这里的特定干扰项。
Watch for a specific distractor here.

114
00:08:26,304 --> 00:08:34,340
那些说云端消除了成本，或者同时消除了固定成本和可变成本的选项永远是错误的。
Options that say the cloud eliminates expense or eliminates both fixed and variable costs are always wrong.

115
00:08:35,278 --> 00:08:39,140
你只是在用一种形式的成本替换另一种形式，而不是消除它。
You are trading one shape of cost for another, not removing it.

116
00:08:40,813 --> 00:08:44,324
规模经济值得专门拿出一页来讲，因为它经常出现。
Economies of scale deserves its own slide because it appears constantly.

117
00:08:44,846 --> 00:08:46,372
其机制是聚合。
The mechanism is aggregation.

118
00:08:47,104 --> 00:08:57,732
大量的客户汇聚在一起，形成了单个组织无法达到的采购量。这降低了 AWS 的单价，而 AWS 再通过降低价格将其传递给用户。
Enormous numbers of customers combine into purchasing volume no single organization could reach. That lowers what AWS pays per unit and AWS passes it on as lower prices.

119
00:08:58,704 --> 00:09:00,612
这些干扰项是固定的。
The distractors are consistent.

120
00:09:00,864 --> 00:09:04,036
与竞争对手匹配价格并不属于规模经济。
Price matching a competitor is not economies of scale.

121
00:09:04,686 --> 00:09:06,884
免费套餐不属于规模经济。
The free tier is not economies of scale.

122
00:09:07,438 --> 00:09:09,732
无限资源根本不是真实存在的东西。
Unlimited resources is not a real thing at all.

123
00:09:10,350 --> 00:09:16,164
如果题干提到汇总多个客户的使用情况，那么答案就是规模经济。
If the STEM mentions aggregating usage across customers, the answer is economies of scale.

124
00:09:17,870 --> 00:09:23,076
敏捷性和弹性是这个领域里最让考生丢分的两个概念。
Agility and elasticity are the pair that cost people the most marks in this domain.

125
00:09:23,504 --> 00:09:26,116
敏捷性是指开展新业务的速度。
Agility is about speed of doing something new.

126
00:09:27,502 --> 00:09:31,424
比如一个营销活动以前需要三周，现在只需要三天。
A marketing campaign that used to take three weeks now takes three days.

127
00:09:31,630 --> 00:09:32,868
这就是敏捷性。
That is agility.

128
00:09:33,646 --> 00:09:36,388
弹性是指容量随着需求而变化。
Elasticity is about capacity following demand.

129
00:09:37,358 --> 00:09:41,824
比如周五流量翻了三倍，服务器集群随之扩大，然后在周日缩减回去。
Traffic triples on Friday and the fleet grows, then shrinks again on Sunday.

130
00:09:41,984 --> 00:09:46,276
这就是弹性。题目通常会给出相关线索。
That is elasticity. The question usually hands you the clue.

131
00:09:47,022 --> 00:09:49,796
如果提到启动时间，选敏捷性。
If it mentions time to launch, choose agility.

132
00:09:50,862 --> 00:09:54,820
如果提到需求上涨和下降，选弹性。
If it mentions demand rising and falling, choose elasticity.

133
00:09:56,544 --> 00:09:59,984
这个表格就是你在考试中实际使用的反向查询表。
This table is the reverse lookup you actually use in the exam.

134
00:10:00,224 --> 00:10:04,228
与其从收益出发，不如从场景中的关键词入手。
Rather than starting from the benefit, start from the phrase in the scenario.

135
00:10:04,544 --> 00:10:07,876
更快的启动和廉价的实验意味着敏捷性。
Faster launches and cheap experiments means agility.

136
00:10:10,062 --> 00:10:12,612
容量随负载变化意味着弹性。
Capacity tracking load means elasticity.

137
00:10:13,774 --> 00:10:18,276
在故障中幸存并改善安全态势意味着运维韧性。
Surviving failure and improving security posture means operational resilience.

138
00:10:18,862 --> 00:10:22,788
员工不再从事无差异的繁重工作意味着提高员工生产力。
Staff no longer doing undifferentiated heavy lifting means staff productivity.

139
00:10:23,662 --> 00:10:25,988
汇总的需求意味着规模经济。
Aggregated demand means economies of scale.

140
00:10:26,734 --> 00:10:29,284
部署到新区域意味着全球覆盖。
Deploying into a new region means global reach.

141
00:10:30,190 --> 00:10:36,932
而且没有大额前期采购，意味着用可变支出代替资本支出。
And no big upfront purchase means trading capital expense for variable expense.

142
00:10:38,638 --> 00:10:42,788
有两个收益名称容易与成本节约混淆，所以我们把它们明确一下。
Two benefit names get confused with cost savings, so let us pin them down.

143
00:10:43,504 --> 00:10:52,388
运维韧性将可用性、容错性、容灾以及改进的安全性控制整合在一个概念中。
Operational resilience bundles, availability, fault tolerance, disaster recovery, and improved security controls into one name.

144
00:10:52,814 --> 00:10:59,236
如果一家公司为了更高的在线时间和更强的安全性而迁移，那就是运维韧性。
If a company migrates for higher uptime and stronger security, that is operational resilience.

145
00:10:59,694 --> 00:11:04,704
员工生产力意味着你的员工不再从事无差异的繁重工作。
Staff productivity means your people stop doing undifferentiated heavy lifting.

146
00:11:05,180 --> 00:11:14,628
安装硬件、更换故障磁盘、修补虚拟机管理程序，这些通常都能省钱，这正是为什么“成本节约”常作为干扰项出现的原因。
Racking hardware, swapping failed disks, patching hypervisors, both of these do usually save money, which is exactly why cost savings appears as a distractor.

147
00:11:15,246 --> 00:11:19,972
只有当场景明确涉及账单时，才选择成本节约。
Choose cost savings only when the scenario is explicitly about the bill.

148
00:11:21,422 --> 00:11:25,316
了解本地部署中钱花在了哪里，能让很多题目变得简单。
Understanding where on premises money goes makes several questions easy.

149
00:11:25,744 --> 00:11:27,908
有硬件的更新周期。
There is hardware with its refresh cycle.

150
00:11:28,224 --> 00:11:32,100
设施意味着空间、电力、冷却和物理安全。
Facilities meaning space, power, cooling, and physical security.

151
00:11:32,464 --> 00:11:35,396
许可费用，通常按插槽或核心计费。
Licensing, often charged per socket or per core.

152
00:11:36,544 --> 00:11:38,468
安装和布线所需的员工成本。
Staffing to rack and patch it all.

153
00:11:39,406 --> 00:11:44,644
还有闲置容量，即为了极少数出现的峰值而购买的冗余空间。
And idle capacity, the headroom bought for a peak that rarely arrives.

154
00:11:49,870 --> 00:11:51,216
现在来看考题。
Now, the exam question.

155
00:11:51,456 --> 00:11:53,856
迁移消除了哪些成本？
Which costs does migration eliminate?

156
00:11:54,158 --> 00:11:56,612
数据中心成本和硬件，是的。
Data center costs and hardware, yes.

157
00:11:56,896 --> 00:12:03,652
但你仍需支付安全工作、监控以及员工培训的费用。这些是转移，而不是消失。
But you still pay for security work, for monitoring, and for training your people. Those move, they do not vanish.

158
00:12:05,006 --> 00:12:09,616
考试指南中明确提到了许可，所以要掌握这两种策略。
Licensing appears in the exam guide explicitly, so know both strategies.

159
00:12:09,966 --> 00:12:13,540
「自带许可」意味着你可以继续使用现有的协议。
Bring your own license means you reuse an agreement you already hold.

160
00:12:14,030 --> 00:12:21,252
这通常需要专用主机，因为基于插槽和核心的许可条款需要识别物理服务器。
That often requires dedicated hosts because socket-based and core-based license terms need visibility of the physical server.

161
00:12:21,934 --> 00:12:33,056
「包含许可」意味着 AWS 将成本计入每小时费率。这种方式更简单，但每小时费用通常更高，不过当你停止实例时就不再收费了。
License included means AWS builds the cost into the hourly rate. That is simpler and usually dearer per hour, but it stops charging when you stop the instance.

162
00:12:33,376 --> 00:12:41,732
值得记住的考点是：与物理硬件挂钩的许可条款是使用专用主机的典型理由。
The exam link worth remembering is that license terms tied to physical hardware are the classic justification for dedicated hosts.

163
00:12:43,118 --> 00:12:44,656
还有两个特定的概念。
Two more named concepts.

164
00:12:44,976 --> 00:12:51,268
「规格优化」意味着根据测得的使用情况来匹配实例大小，并且不断重复这个过程，而不是只在启动时做一次。
Right sizing means matching instance size to measured usage and doing it repeatedly rather than once at launch.

165
00:12:51,616 --> 00:12:58,628
对应的工具是 AWS Compute Optimizer 以及成本管理器中的规格优化建议。
The tools named for this are AWS Compute Optimizer and the write sizing recommendations inside Cost Explorer.

166
00:12:59,406 --> 00:13:05,092
自动化通过减少人工操作以及在没人需要时关闭功能来降低成本。
Automation reduces cost by removing manual effort and by turning things off when nobody needs them.

167
00:13:06,414 --> 00:13:08,736
这里有一个常考的区别点。
Here is the distinction that gets tested.

168
00:13:09,056 --> 00:13:14,336
「规格优化」改变的是实例的大小。而「自动扩容」改变的是实例的数量。
Right sizing changes the size of an instance. Autoscaling changes the number of instances.

169
00:13:14,656 --> 00:13:16,336
是尺寸还是数量。
Size versus count.

170
00:13:17,774 --> 00:13:18,916
案例分析。
Worked scenario.

171
00:13:19,536 --> 00:13:19,972
1。
1.

172
00:13:21,422 --> 00:13:23,556
一家零售商运营自己的数据中心。
A retailer runs its own data center.

173
00:13:24,430 --> 00:13:32,336
每年 11 月，他们都会为圣诞节高峰购买额外的服务器，而在其他 11 个月里，大约 60% 的硬件处于闲置状态。
Every November it buys extra servers for the Christmas peak, and for the other 11 months, about 60% of that hardware sits idle.

174
00:13:32,910 --> 00:13:39,536
迁移到 AWS 后，财务总监注意到每到秋天就不再有大规模的硬件采购了。
After migrating to AWS, the finance director notices there is no longer a large hardware purchase each autumn.

175
00:13:39,696 --> 00:13:43,972
相反，每月的账单在 11 月升高，并在 1 月再次下降。
Instead, the monthly bill rises through November and falls again in January.

176
00:13:44,496 --> 00:13:48,420
这最直接描述了云计算的哪种优势？
Which advantage of cloud computing does this most directly describe?

177
00:13:48,976 --> 00:13:52,656
A。受益于大规模的规模经济。
a benefit from massive economies of scale.

178
00:13:53,166 --> 00:13:53,520
B。
B.

179
00:13:53,902 --> 00:13:56,484
用可变支出代替资本支出。
Trade capital expense for variable expense.

180
00:13:56,816 --> 00:13:57,056
C。
C.

181
00:13:57,582 --> 00:13:59,296
提高速度和敏捷性。
Increase speed and agility.

182
00:13:59,616 --> 00:13:59,856
D。
D.

183
00:14:00,256 --> 00:14:01,732
在几分钟内走向全球。
Go global in minutes.

184
00:14:02,094 --> 00:14:03,108
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

185
00:14:09,166 --> 00:14:10,308
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

186
00:14:10,798 --> 00:14:13,508
用可变支出代替资本支出。
Trade capital expense for variable expense.

187
00:14:14,830 --> 00:14:23,044
关键句是：秋季的硬件采购消失了，取而代之的是根据需求产生的账单。这就是它的定义。
The deciding sentence is that the autumn hardware purchase disappeared and was replaced by a bill that follows demand. That is the definition.

188
00:14:24,398 --> 00:14:26,948
现在来看看为什么 C 选项看起来很有诱惑力。
Now look at why C is genuinely tempting.

189
00:14:27,886 --> 00:14:32,900
弹性显然在后台发生，而且弹性感觉就像是敏捷性。
Elasticity is clearly happening in the background, and elasticity feels like agility.

190
00:14:33,296 --> 00:14:35,396
但在这种情况下，没有任何东西变快了。
But nothing in this scenario got faster.

191
00:14:35,854 --> 00:14:40,676
圣诞高峰还是在往常的时间到来。改变的只是付费的形式。
The Christmas peak arrives at the same time it always did. Only the shape of the payment changed.

192
00:14:40,976 --> 00:14:46,564
A 对 AWS 来说是正确的，但在这里没有证据支持；而 D 完全没提到地理位置。
A is true of AWS but unsupported here, and D has no geography in it at all.

193
00:14:47,854 --> 00:14:48,836
工作场景。
Work scenario.

194
00:14:49,774 --> 00:14:50,116
2。
2.

195
00:14:50,990 --> 00:14:58,692
一家媒体公司过去需要 6 周时间来审批、订购、交付并安装服务器，才能测试新的视频格式。
A media company used to need 6 weeks to get servers approved, ordered, delivered, and racked before it could test a new video format.

196
00:14:59,310 --> 00:15:02,180
在最后三种格式中，有两项在测试后被放弃了。
Two of the last three formats were abandoned after testing.

197
00:15:02,896 --> 00:15:10,820
在 AWS 上，同样的测试现在只需两天就能搭建完成，而且团队每季度能进行四次实验，而不是一次。
On AWS, the same test now takes two days to set up and the team runs four experiments a quarter instead of one.

198
00:15:11,278 --> 00:15:15,556
这个场景展示了 AWS 云的哪种优势？
Which benefit of the AWS cloud does this scenario demonstrate?

199
00:15:16,016 --> 00:15:24,900
A 弹性，B 运维韧性，C 提高业务敏捷性，D 高可用性。
a Elasticity, B Operational Resilience, C Increase Business Agility, D. High Availability.

200
00:15:25,518 --> 00:15:26,724
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

201
00:15:33,006 --> 00:15:34,304
答案是 C。
The answer is C.

202
00:15:34,926 --> 00:15:36,772
提高业务敏捷性。
Increase business agility.

203
00:15:38,638 --> 00:15:48,544
故意将此与场景 1 进行对比。在场景 1 中，支付形式变了，但时间线没变；而在这里，时间线变了，且没提到钱的问题。
Compare this deliberately with scenario 1. There, the payment shape changed and the timeline did not. Here, the timeline changed and nothing was said about money.

204
00:15:48,784 --> 00:15:53,316
属于同一个领域，只是名称不同的优势，而区别就在于题干中的一句话。
Same domain, different name benefit, and the difference is one sentence in the stem.

205
00:15:54,254 --> 00:15:58,884
这就是为什么寻找关键细节比死记硬背定义更重要。
That is why reading for the deciding detail matters more than knowing the definitions.

206
00:15:59,504 --> 00:16:02,564
A 是错误的，因为并没有容量随着需求变动。
A is wrong because no capacity moves with demand.

207
00:16:03,182 --> 00:16:07,940
B 和 D 都需要某些东西发生故障或停机，但这里什么都没出问题。
B and D both need something to have failed or gone down, and nothing did.

208
00:16:09,800 --> 00:16:14,372
工作场景 3。而且这是一个多选题。
Worked scenario 3. And this one is a multiple response.

209
00:16:14,704 --> 00:16:21,220
一家物流公司正在构建其迁移的业务案例，并想知道哪些成本项将真正消失。
A logistics firm is building its migration business case and wants to know which cost lines will actually disappear.

210
00:16:21,742 --> 00:16:31,876
清单包括数据中心租赁、服务器硬件更新、安全运营团队、监控工具订阅以及存储阵列的前期采购。
The list includes the data center lease, server hardware refresh, its security operations team, its monitoring tooling subscription, and the upfront purchase of storage arrays.

211
00:16:33,230 --> 00:16:36,228
迁移到 AWS 后，哪两项成本会被消除？
Which two costs will migrating to AWS eliminate?

212
00:16:37,774 --> 00:16:39,588
A 数据中心成本。
A data center costs.

213
00:16:40,224 --> 00:16:40,464
B
B

214
00:16:41,518 --> 00:16:43,044
数据安全成本。
Data security costs.

215
00:16:44,110 --> 00:16:46,340
C 固定硬件成本。
C Fixed hardware costs.

216
00:16:46,864 --> 00:16:47,104
D
D

217
00:16:48,494 --> 00:16:49,796
监控成本。
monitoring costs.

218
00:16:50,144 --> 00:16:50,304
E。
E.

219
00:16:50,704 --> 00:16:52,064
员工培训成本。
Staff training costs.

220
00:16:52,462 --> 00:16:54,660
暂停一下，做个决定。
Choose to pause and decide.

221
00:17:00,814 --> 00:17:02,276
答案是 A 和 C。
The answers are A and C.

222
00:17:02,544 --> 00:17:08,324
这道题中的关键词是「消除」，而不是减少或转移，是彻底消除。
The word doing the work in this question is eliminate, not reduce, not shift, eliminate.

223
00:17:08,624 --> 00:17:12,624
数据中心成本会完全消失，因为 AWS 负责建筑维护。
Data center costs go entirely because AWS owns the buildings.

224
00:17:12,864 --> 00:17:16,420
固定硬件成本也会消失，因为购买变成了按需消费。
Fixed hardware costs go because purchase becomes consumption.

225
00:17:16,814 --> 00:17:18,948
其他所有项目都会改变形式但依然存在。
Everything else changes shape and stays.

226
00:17:19,854 --> 00:17:29,540
根据责任共担模型，安全性仍然由你负责。监控仍是构建服务，而培训在迁移过程中通常会增加，而不是减少。
Security is explicitly still yours under the shared responsibility module. Monitoring is still a build service and training usually goes up during a migration, not down.

227
00:17:30,094 --> 00:17:34,180
当题目使用「消除」这个词时，要判断每个选项是否是彻底消失。
When a question users eliminate, test each option against gone entirely.

228
00:17:35,790 --> 00:17:37,124
来看场景 4。
Work scenario 4.

229
00:17:37,582 --> 00:17:43,940
一个财务团队在查看 AWS 账单时，发现有 12 个开发实例已经连续运行了 8 个月。
A finance team reviews its AWS bill and finds 12 development instances running continuously for 8 months.

230
00:17:45,166 --> 00:17:50,180
峰值 CPU 利用率仅为 9%，且在非工作时间没人使用它们。
Peak CPU utilization is 9% and nobody uses them outside working hours.

231
00:17:51,054 --> 00:17:56,544
开发部门表示，这些实例在工作时间内必须保持当前配置和数据。
Development says the instances must keep their current configuration and data during working hours.

232
00:17:56,784 --> 00:17:59,396
哪两个操作能最直接地解决这个问题？
Which two actions address this most directly?

233
00:18:00,064 --> 00:18:03,108
a 将实例调整为更小的类型。
a Right size the instances to a smaller type.

234
00:18:03,664 --> 00:18:07,236
B 将这些实例放入自动缩放组中。
B put the instances behind an auto-scaling group.

235
00:18:08,110 --> 00:18:08,384
C。
C.

236
00:18:08,910 --> 00:18:12,384
设置在非工作时间停止这些实例。
Schedule the instances to stop outside working hours.

237
00:18:12,942 --> 00:18:13,184
D。
D.

238
00:18:13,664 --> 00:18:16,304
为它们购买为期三年的预留实例。
Buy three year reserved instances for them.

239
00:18:16,784 --> 00:18:17,104
E。
E.

240
00:18:17,614 --> 00:18:19,876
将工作负载迁移到竞价实例。
Move the workload to spot instances.

241
00:18:20,526 --> 00:18:22,756
停下来思考一下并做决定。
Choose to pause and decide.

242
00:18:28,974 --> 00:18:30,916
答案是 A 和 C。
The answers are A and C.

243
00:18:31,344 --> 00:18:35,332
这个场景设置了两个约束条件，每个标记对应一个。
This scenario plants two constraints, one for each mark.

244
00:18:36,064 --> 00:18:39,812
9% 的峰值利用率是规格优化的信号。
9% peak utilization is the right sizing signal.

245
00:18:40,494 --> 00:18:44,164
非工作时间无人使用是调度信号。
Nobody using them outside working hours is the scheduling signal.

246
00:18:44,544 --> 00:18:46,852
现在来看看这两个最好的干扰项。
Now look at the two best distractors.

247
00:18:47,726 --> 00:18:54,052
D 是针对注重成本的考生的陷阱，因为预留实例确实能省钱。
D is the trap that catches cost conscious candidates because reserved instances do save money.

248
00:18:54,544 --> 00:19:01,188
但为尺寸不对且大部分处于闲置状态的实例承诺三年，只是在打折购买浪费。
But committing three years to instances that are the wrong size and mostly idle just buys the waste at a discount.

249
00:19:01,984 --> 00:19:04,228
先解决浪费问题，然后再做承诺。
Fix the waste first, then commit.

250
00:19:06,304 --> 00:19:09,264
而 E 违反了明确的约束条件。
And E fails on a stated constraint.

251
00:19:10,606 --> 00:19:15,588
开发人员需要他们的工作状态持续运行，而竞价实例的中断会破坏这种状态。
The developers need their working state to persist, and spot interruption destroys it.

252
00:19:17,262 --> 00:19:24,548
总结一下，这六个优势是词汇量，考试考的是名称而不是你的推理逻辑，所以要精确掌握它们。
To recap, the six advantages are vocabulary and the exam grades the name rather than your reasoning, so learn them precisely.

253
00:19:25,584 --> 00:19:29,412
敏捷性衡量时间，弹性衡量容量。
Agility measures time, elasticity measures capacity.

254
00:19:30,064 --> 00:19:33,348
规模经济意味着跨客户的聚合。
Economies of scale means aggregation across customers.

255
00:19:34,158 --> 00:19:42,788
迁移消除了设施和前期硬件投入，而安全性、监控和规划只是改变了形式而非消失。
Migration eliminates facilities and upfront hardware while security, monitoring, and planning change shape rather than disappearing.

256
00:19:43,534 --> 00:19:47,780
而且规格优化改变的是尺寸，而自动扩缩容改变的是数量。
And right sizing changes size while auto-scaling changes count.

257
00:19:49,198 --> 00:19:51,844
下一个模块，Well-Architected Framework。
Next module, the well-architected framework.

258
00:19:53,454 --> 00:20:00,836
Well-Architected Framework 在考试大纲中直接点名，相关的题目非常容易预测。
The well-architected framework is named directly in the exam guide and questions about it are unusually predictable.

259
00:20:01,646 --> 00:20:04,804
场景描述一个设计目标，你来指出对应的支柱。
A scenario describes a design goal and you name the pillar.

260
00:20:05,390 --> 00:20:08,740
把这些支柱的定义搞清楚，这些题就是送分题。
Get the pillar definitions crisp and these become fee marks.

261
00:20:10,446 --> 00:20:13,424
有一种框架让这些支柱更容易记住。
One framing that makes the pillars easier to remember.

262
00:20:13,664 --> 00:20:15,664
它们不是你一项项勾选的清单。
They are not a checklist you take off.

263
00:20:16,078 --> 00:20:19,588
它们是六个在实际操作中互相制衡的优先事项。
They are six priorities that genuinely pull against each other.

264
00:20:20,142 --> 00:20:22,144
更强的安全性会牺牲性能。
Tighter security costs performance.

265
00:20:22,384 --> 00:20:24,452
更高的可靠性会消耗成本。
Higher reliability costs money.

266
00:20:25,264 --> 00:20:34,596
这个框架之所以存在，是因为在团队讨论这些权衡之前，需要给它们命名。这也是为什么一个场景可以涉及三个支柱但仍只有一个正确答案的原因。
The framework exists because those trade-offs need naming before a team can argue about them. That is also why a scenario can touch three pillars and still have one correct answer.

267
00:20:35,024 --> 00:20:37,156
其中一个目标始终是明确表述的目标。
One goal is always the stated goal.

268
00:20:38,670 --> 00:20:39,652
六个支柱。
Six pillars.

269
00:20:40,144 --> 00:20:44,516
卓越运营考查的是你是否能日常运行并改进系统。
Operational excellence asks whether you can run and improve the system day to day.

270
00:20:45,024 --> 00:20:48,612
安全性考查的是你是否能保护数据并证明是谁做了什么。
Security asks whether you can protect data and prove who did what.

271
00:20:49,614 --> 00:20:53,668
可靠性考查的是系统是否能正常运行并从故障中恢复。
Reliability asks whether it does its job correctly and recovers from failure.

272
00:20:54,574 --> 00:20:59,940
性能效率考查的是在需求变化时，你是否在高效利用资源。
Performance efficiency asks whether you are using resources well as demand changes.

273
00:21:00,302 --> 00:21:04,804
成本优化考查的是你是否能以最低价格获得价值。
Cost optimization asks whether you are getting value at the lowest price.

274
00:21:05,344 --> 00:21:09,860
而可持续性考查的是你是否在减少对环境的影响。
And sustainability asks whether you are minimizing environmental impact.

275
00:21:11,278 --> 00:21:13,604
旧的学习资料中列出了五个支柱。
Older study material lists five pillars.

276
00:21:14,606 --> 00:21:18,980
可持续性是在 2021 年加入的，也是考试考查的内容。
Sustainability was added in 2021 and it is examinable.

277
00:21:20,398 --> 00:21:27,460
可靠性和性能效率是最容易混淆的一对，因为两者听起来都像是系统在正常运行。
Reliability and performance efficiency are the pair most often confused because both sound like the system working properly.

278
00:21:27,982 --> 00:21:30,596
区分它们的关键在于场景关注的是什么。
The separator is what the scenario worries about.

279
00:21:31,118 --> 00:21:33,028
可靠性关注的是故障。
Reliability worries about failure.

280
00:21:33,742 --> 00:21:39,364
自动恢复、多可用区部署、备份、健康检查。
Recovering automatically, multi-availability zone deployment, backups, health checks.

281
00:21:40,464 --> 00:21:43,492
性能效率关注的是效率。
Performance efficiency worries about efficiency.

282
00:21:43,904 --> 00:21:50,692
选择轻量级资源类型、采用缓存或无服务器架构、随需求变化进行调整。
Choosing the light resource type, adopting caching or serverless, adapting as demand changes.

283
00:21:51,264 --> 00:21:55,844
如果出现「恢复」或「故障」这些词，就选可靠性。
If the words recover or fail appear, choose reliability.

284
00:21:57,582 --> 00:22:01,892
另一对值得区分的是卓越运营和可靠性。
The other pair worth separating is operational excellence and reliability.

285
00:22:02,830 --> 00:22:05,892
卓越运营是关于团队如何运行系统。
Operational excellence is about how the team runs the system.

286
00:22:06,478 --> 00:22:13,412
部署流程、操作手册、可观测性、进行小的可逆更改、从失败中学习。
Deployment processes, run books, observability, making small reversible changes, learning from failures.

287
00:22:14,318 --> 00:22:17,444
可靠性是关于在没有人工干预的情况下，系统如何表现。
Reliability is about how the system behaves without you.

288
00:22:18,478 --> 00:22:19,824
它能自动恢复。
It recovers on its own.

289
00:22:20,174 --> 00:22:25,508
一个实用的测试方法是：判断句子是在讲人员和流程，还是在讲架构。
A useful test is to ask whether the sentence is about people and process or about architecture.

290
00:22:27,662 --> 00:22:29,860
「流程」指向的是卓越运营。
Process points at operational excellence.

291
00:22:31,598 --> 00:22:36,260
该框架还有一些通用的设计原则，也会出现在题目中。
The framework also has general design principles that get quoted in questions.

292
00:22:36,942 --> 00:22:38,436
不要去猜测容量。
Stop guessing capacity.

293
00:22:38,894 --> 00:22:45,184
在生产规模下测试系统，这在云端是可负担的，因为你可以在之后删除环境。
Test systems at production scale, which is affordable in the cloud because you delete the environment afterwards.

294
00:22:45,424 --> 00:22:48,612
通过自动化来让架构实验变得更容易。
Automate to make architectural experimentation easier.

295
00:22:49,550 --> 00:22:51,492
支持演进式架构。
Allow for evolutionary architectures.

296
00:22:52,250 --> 00:22:53,770
利用数据来驱动架构。
Drive architectures using data.

297
00:22:55,662 --> 00:23:01,412
并通过游戏日进行改进，这意味着有意识地演练故障，而不是等到真正发生时才去应对。
And improve through game days, meaning rehearsing failure deliberately rather than waiting to meet it.

298
00:23:02,384 --> 00:23:07,044
「游戏日」和「在生产规模下测试」是两个最常作为正确答案出现的选项。
Game days and testing at production scale are the two that turn up most as correct answers.

299
00:23:08,750 --> 00:23:13,124
这里有一个框架，还有一个工具，考试会区分这两者。
There is a framework and there is a tool, and the exam distinguishes them.

300
00:23:17,454 --> 00:23:26,660
架构设计的工具是一个免费的控制台服务，你只需回答关于工作负载的结构化问卷，就能获得改进方案。
The architected tool is a free console service where you answer a structured questionnaire about a workload and receive an improvement plan.

301
00:23:27,040 --> 00:23:28,708
这是一个你运行的审查。
It is a review you run.

302
00:23:29,680 --> 00:23:34,916
相比之下，顾问会持续且自动地检查你的实时账户。
Trusted Advisor, by contrast, inspects your live account continuously and automatically.

303
00:23:35,566 --> 00:23:37,764
这就是考试用来区分两者的点。
That is the separator the exam uses.

304
00:23:38,480 --> 00:23:41,476
“持续”和“自动”指向顾问。
Continuous and automatic points at Trusted Advisor.

305
00:23:42,574 --> 00:23:47,172
“结构化审查”，你坐下来完成它，这指向 well-architected 工具。
A structured review, you sit down and complete points at the well-architected tool.

306
00:23:48,462 --> 00:23:52,484
这种反向推导与 AWS 实际使用的措辞一致。
This reverse lookup mirrors the phrasing AWS actually uses.

307
00:23:52,800 --> 00:23:56,740
“快速恢复并持续运行”意味着可靠性。
Recover quickly and perform consistently means reliability.

308
00:23:57,040 --> 00:24:00,196
“保护数据并追踪操作”意味着安全性。
Protect data and trace actions means security.

309
00:24:00,686 --> 00:24:04,100
“日常运行和监控”意味着卓越运营。
Run and monitor day-to-day means operational excellence.

310
00:24:04,750 --> 00:24:09,252
“随需求变化高效利用资源”意味着性能效率。
Use resources efficiently as demand changes means performance efficiency.

311
00:24:10,286 --> 00:24:13,988
“以最低价格提供价值”意味着成本优化。
Deliver value at the lowest price means cost optimization.

312
00:24:14,798 --> 00:24:18,180
“减少对环境的影响”意味着可持续性。
And reduce environmental impact means sustainability.

313
00:24:19,086 --> 00:24:25,444
掌握这些措辞比记住名称更有用，因为屏幕上出现的是这些措词。
Learning the phrasings is more useful than learning the names because the phrasings are what appears on screen.

314
00:24:26,880 --> 00:24:28,324
实战案例。
Worked scenario.

315
00:24:28,880 --> 00:24:33,764
1. 一家支付公司正在重新设计其交易服务。
1. A payments company is redesigning its transaction service.

316
00:24:34,160 --> 00:24:43,652
如果整个可用区不可用，它必须继续正确处理，并且在无需工程师干预的情况下恢复到全部容量。
It must continue processing correctly if an entire availability zone becomes unavailable and must return to full capacity without an engineer intervening.

317
00:24:44,494 --> 00:24:51,524
团队正在部署到三个可用区，并配备健康检查和故障实例的自动替换。
The team is deploying across three availability zones with health checks and automatic replacement of failed instances.

318
00:24:52,334 --> 00:24:54,532
这个设计体现了哪一个支柱？
Which pillar does this design represent?

319
00:24:55,630 --> 00:24:57,295
A. 安全性
A security.

320
00:24:57,902 --> 00:24:58,310
B.
B.

321
00:24:59,010 --> 00:25:00,110
性能效率
Performance efficiency

322
00:25:00,110 --> 00:25:01,570
C.
C.

323
00:25:02,250 --> 00:25:03,330
卓越运营
Operational excellence

324
00:25:03,330 --> 00:25:04,750
D.
D.

325
00:25:05,290 --> 00:25:07,780
可靠性。停一下，做决定。
Reliability Pause and decide.

326
00:25:13,998 --> 00:25:16,580
答案是 D，可靠性。
The answer is D reliability.

327
00:25:17,040 --> 00:25:18,660
有两个短语决定了结果。
Two phrases decide it.

328
00:25:19,120 --> 00:25:24,068
“继续正确处理”以及“在无需工程师干预的情况下恢复到全部容量”。
Continue processing correctly and return to full capacity without an engineer intervening.

329
00:25:24,782 --> 00:25:26,560
这些几乎是逐字对应的。
Those are almost word for word.

330
00:25:27,790 --> 00:25:29,284
这就是可靠性的定义。
The reliability definition.

331
00:25:29,614 --> 00:25:33,860
仔细看选项 A，因为它是这组题目里最强的干扰项。
Watch option. A carefully because it is the best distractor in the set.

332
00:25:34,638 --> 00:25:39,428
「支付」这个词会让安全性看起来相关，而且在现实生活中确实是相关的。
The word payments makes security feel relevant and it would be in real life.

333
00:25:39,950 --> 00:25:46,660
但考试是根据明确要求的来评分的，这里没提到访问权限、加密或审计。
But the exam grades the stated requirement and nothing here asks about access, encryption, or audit.

334
00:25:48,270 --> 00:25:52,960
你自带的领域知识不能作为题目中的证据。
Domain knowledge you bring to the question is not evidence in the question.

335
00:25:54,158 --> 00:25:55,716
来看变体场景 2。
Worked scenario 2.

336
00:25:56,302 --> 00:26:02,660
一个研究小组在固定的一组大型通用型 EC2 实例上运行耐克模拟实验。
A research group runs Nike simulations on a fixed fleet of large general purpose EC2 instances.

337
00:26:03,440 --> 00:26:05,284
这些任务是受计算限制的。
The jobs are compute bound.

338
00:26:05,920 --> 00:26:11,044
内存占用仅为 11%，而 CPU 在数小时内一直处于 100% 的满载状态。
Memory sits at 11% while CPU pins at 100% for hours.

339
00:26:12,000 --> 00:26:20,000
团队希望在不增加支出的情况下让任务更快完成，并正在评估计算优化型实例类型和一个
The team wants the jobs to finish sooner without increasing spend and is evaluating compute optimized instance types and a cache-in

340
00:26:20,160 --> 00:26:21,860
用于共享输入数据的缓存层。
layer for shared input data.

341
00:26:22,400 --> 00:26:24,900
团队主要是在哪个维度上工作？
Which pillar is the team primarily working in?

342
00:26:25,360 --> 00:26:27,108
A. 可靠性。
A reliability.

343
00:26:27,694 --> 00:26:29,796
B. 性能效率。
B performance efficiency.

344
00:26:30,254 --> 00:26:32,196
C. 成本优化。
C Cost optimization.

345
00:26:32,560 --> 00:26:34,276
D. 可持续性。
D. Sustainability.

346
00:26:36,366 --> 00:26:37,412
停一下，做决定。
Pause and decide.

347
00:26:43,280 --> 00:26:44,560
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

348
00:26:44,800 --> 00:26:45,956
性能效率。
Performance efficiency.

349
00:26:46,320 --> 00:26:50,052
这个场景的设计是为了测试一种特定的阅读技巧。
This scenario is built to test one specific reading skill.

350
00:26:50,510 --> 00:26:54,500
它提到了支出，这会强烈引导你往成本优化上想。
It mentions spend, which pulls hard towards cost optimization.

351
00:26:54,958 --> 00:26:56,356
但再读一遍这句话。
But read the sentence again.

352
00:26:56,910 --> 00:27:00,004
「在不增加支出的情况下」是针对解决方案的一个约束条件。
Without increasing spend is a constraint on the solution.

353
00:27:00,366 --> 00:27:01,796
「更快完成」才是目标。
Finish sooner is the goal.

354
00:27:02,560 --> 00:27:05,508
目标决定了维度，而不是约束条件。
The goal picks the pillar, not the constraint.

355
00:27:05,920 --> 00:27:10,660
这种区别贯穿了整个考试，不仅仅是在优秀的架构问题中出现。
That distinction appears throughout this exam well beyond well-architected questions.

356
00:27:10,960 --> 00:27:14,820
要学会区分场景想要什么，以及它不允许什么。
Learn to separate what the scenario wants from what it will not allow.

357
00:27:16,400 --> 00:27:17,988
变体场景 3。
Warped Scenario 3.

358
00:27:18,320 --> 00:27:22,880
一名运营经理希望减少因部署导致的生产事故。
An operations manager wants to reduce production incidents caused by deployments.

359
00:27:23,120 --> 00:27:31,300
团队每月发布一次大型版本，没有回滚程序，并通过阅读单个服务器上的日志来诊断问题。
The team ships one large release a month, has no rollback procedure, and diagnoses problems by reading logs on individual servers.

360
00:27:32,110 --> 00:27:40,964
拟议的更改包括：频繁部署小变动、跳过回滚、集中化日志和指标，并在每次事故后进行审查。
The proposed changes are to deploy small changes frequently, skip the rollback, centralize logs and metrics, and hold a review after every incident.

361
00:27:41,600 --> 00:27:43,940
这些变更属于哪一个支柱？
Which pillar do these changes belong to?

362
00:27:44,560 --> 00:27:46,372
A. 卓越运营，
a Operational Excellence,

363
00:27:47,406 --> 00:27:48,900
B. 可靠性，
B reliability,

364
00:27:49,902 --> 00:27:51,460
C. 安全性，
C security,

365
00:27:52,160 --> 00:27:52,480
D.
D.

366
00:27:52,880 --> 00:27:54,212
性能效率。
Performance efficiency.

367
00:27:55,182 --> 00:27:56,388
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

368
00:28:02,670 --> 00:28:05,796
答案是 A，卓越运营。
The answer is A, operational excellence.

369
00:28:08,270 --> 00:28:11,152
故意把这个和场景一进行对比。
Compare this with scenario one deliberately.

370
00:28:11,598 --> 00:28:14,244
两个场景都是关于生产环境中的故障。
Both scenarios are about failures in production.

371
00:28:15,918 --> 00:28:24,992
在场景一中，修复方案是架构上的，即跨可用区部署并自动替换，所以答案是可靠性。
In scenario one, the fix was architectural, deploying across availability zones with automatic replacement, and the answer was reliability.

372
00:28:25,518 --> 00:28:29,060
而在这里，每一个提出的变更都是流程上的变化。
Here, every single proposed change is a process change.

373
00:28:29,454 --> 00:28:35,952
发布节奏、回滚脚本、集中式可观测性以及事故回顾。
Release cadence, a rollback script, centralized observability, and incident reviews.

374
00:28:36,112 --> 00:28:38,308
架构方面没有任何变动。
Nothing about the architecture moves.

375
00:28:38,512 --> 00:28:40,804
这就是卓越运营。
That is operational excellence.

376
00:28:41,072 --> 00:28:45,632
同样的问题，不同的支柱，因为修复方案所在的维度不同。
Same problem, different pillar, because the fix lives in a different place.

377
00:28:47,022 --> 00:28:48,324
处理场景 4。
Worked scenario 4.

378
00:28:49,518 --> 00:28:55,044
一家公司希望根据 AWS 最佳实践对其主要工作负载进行结构化审查。
A company wants a structured review of its main workload against AWS best practices.

379
00:28:56,206 --> 00:29:04,192
它希望回答有关工作负载的问题，获得一份优先排序的改进清单，并每季度重复一次审查。
It wants to answer questions about the workload, receive a prioritized list of improvements, and repeat the review quarterly.

380
00:29:04,814 --> 00:29:13,348
它还要求对运行中的账户进行自动持续检查，找出未使用的资源和开放的安全组，而不需要任何人填写问卷。
It also wants automatic ongoing checks of the live account for unused resources and open security groups without anyone completing a questionnaire.

381
00:29:13,712 --> 00:29:16,352
哪两个服务符合这些要求？
Which two services meet these requirements?

382
00:29:16,672 --> 00:29:24,672
A. AWS Well Architected Tool，B. AWS Trusted Advisor，C. Config，D.
A AWS Well Architected Tool, B AWS Trusted Advisor, C AWS Config, D.

383
00:29:25,102 --> 00:29:27,300
AWS Compute Optimizer。
AWS Compute Optimizer.

384
00:29:28,272 --> 00:29:28,512
E
E

385
00:29:29,454 --> 00:29:30,692
Amazon Inspector。
Amazon Inspector.

386
00:29:31,406 --> 00:29:32,132
选择
Choose to

387
00:29:32,782 --> 00:29:34,052
停下来思考一下。
pause and decide.

388
00:29:40,206 --> 00:29:42,436
答案是 A 和 B。
The answers are A and B.

389
00:29:43,054 --> 00:29:45,924
多选题经常会这样出题。
Multiple response questions frequently do this.

390
00:29:46,352 --> 00:29:51,428
两个不同的要求，各对应一个服务，你的任务就是注意到有两个需求。
Two distinct requirements, one service each, and your job is to notice there are two.

391
00:29:52,014 --> 00:29:56,068
基于问卷的重复性审查是“架构良好工具”。
The questionnaire-based repeatable review is the well-architected tool.

392
00:29:56,352 --> 00:30:00,420
持续自动的账户检查是“顾问”。
The continuous automatic account checks are trusted advisor.

393
00:30:01,312 --> 00:30:08,548
C、D 和 E 都是功能相近的真实服务，这就是它们成为优秀干扰项的原因。
C, D, and E are all real services that do adjacent things, which is what makes them good distractors.

394
00:30:09,152 --> 00:30:11,172
Config 记录配置。
Config records configuration.

395
00:30:11,758 --> 00:30:14,084
计算优化器负责调整合适尺寸。
Compute optimizer right sizes.

396
00:30:14,352 --> 00:30:16,352
Inspector 查找漏洞。
Inspector finds vulnerabilities.

397
00:30:16,512 --> 00:30:18,916
这些都不是运行最佳实践问卷的工具。
None of them runs a best practice questionnaire.

398
00:30:20,622 --> 00:30:25,156
总结一下，六大支柱和可持续性都是考点。
To recap, six pillars and sustainability is examinable.

399
00:30:25,678 --> 00:30:31,044
可靠性关注故障，而性能效率关注效率。
Reliability worries about failure while performance efficiency worries about efficiency.

400
00:30:31,918 --> 00:30:39,236
卓越运营存在于流程中，而可靠性存在于架构中。所以要判断提议的修复方案属于哪一类。
Operational excellence lives in process while reliability lives in architecture. So ask where the proposed fix sits.

401
00:30:40,142 --> 00:30:43,076
目标决定支柱，而不是约束条件。
The goal picks the pillar, not the constraint.

402
00:30:45,006 --> 00:30:51,844
而且“架构良好工具”是你运行的审查，而“顾问”是持续监控的。
And the well-architected tool is a review you run while trusted advisor watches continuously.

403
00:30:52,814 --> 00:31:01,188
一个小细节：AWS 用 Z 来拼写成本优化的支柱，因为它是一个产品名称。
One small note AWS spells the pillar cost optimization with a Z because it is a product name.

404
00:31:01,678 --> 00:31:06,468
下一个模块是迁移策略和云采用框架。
Next module, migration strategies and the cloud adoption framework.

405
00:31:08,142 --> 00:31:12,516
这个模块涵盖了组织如何真正进入 AWS。
This module covers how organizations actually get onto AWS.

406
00:31:13,518 --> 00:31:14,308
分为两个部分。
Two halves.

407
00:31:14,926 --> 00:31:24,192
首先是包含考试词汇的七种迁移策略。然后是 AWS 提供的用于规划和执行迁移的工具。
First, the seven migration strategies with the exam test as vocabulary. Then the tools AWS provides to plan and execute a move.

408
00:31:24,718 --> 00:31:31,268
在工具部分，一些旧的题库已经过时，所以我们会在过程中标出这些内容。
The tooling half is where several older question banks have gone out of date, so we will flag that as we go.

409
00:31:32,752 --> 00:31:37,392
这里的结构与模块 1 中的优势问题相同。
The shape here is the same as the benefits questions in module 1.

410
00:31:37,806 --> 00:31:43,428
情景描述公司对应用程序做了什么，你来匹配正确的策略名称。
A scenario describes what a company did to an application and you attach the correct strategy name.

411
00:31:43,950 --> 00:31:46,432
原封不动地移动意味着“重新托管”。
Moved it unchanged means re-host.

412
00:31:51,232 --> 00:31:51,552
抛弃
Throw

413
00:31:51,712 --> 00:31:55,076
它并购买新软件意味着“重新购买”。
it away and bought software instead means repurchase.

414
00:31:55,822 --> 00:31:57,636
准确记住这 7 个名称，
Learn the 7 names precisely,

415
00:31:58,382 --> 00:32:00,676
这样大部分内容就变成机械式的操作了。
and most of this becomes mechanical.

416
00:32:02,382 --> 00:32:04,100
这是标准列表。
Here is the canonical list.

417
00:32:04,494 --> 00:32:07,568
重新托管是“平移”，即原封不动地移动。
Re-host is lift and shift, moving it unchanged.

418
00:32:07,918 --> 00:32:14,756
重新平台化是“抬起、调整并平移”，在不改动核心应用的情况下进行微调优化。
Replatform is lift, tinker and shift, making small optimizations without touching the core application.

419
00:32:15,310 --> 00:32:21,088
重新购买是“放弃并购买”，抛弃现有产品转而购买新软件。
Repurchase is drop and shop, abandoning what you have and buying software instead.

420
00:32:21,646 --> 00:32:24,932
重构意味着重写代码以使用云原生服务。
Refactor means rewriting it to use cloud native services.

421
00:32:25,614 --> 00:32:28,484
退役是指因为没人使用而将其关闭。
Retire means switching it off because nobody used it.

422
00:32:29,006 --> 00:32:30,980
保留是指暂时保持原样不动。
Retain means leaving it alone for now.

423
00:32:31,566 --> 00:32:36,356
而重新定位是指在不改变操作方式的情况下，整体迁移基础设施。
And relocate means moving infrastructure wholesale without changing how you operate it.

424
00:32:37,934 --> 00:32:41,412
这种反向推导是你在面临时间压力时真正会用到的方法。
This reverse lookup is what you actually use under time pressure.

425
00:32:41,728 --> 00:32:43,556
针对场景提一个问题。
Ask one question of the scenario.

426
00:32:43,888 --> 00:32:46,020
应用程序本身发生了什么变化？
What happened to the application itself?

427
00:32:46,510 --> 00:32:48,128
没变，就是重新托管。
Unchanged is re-host.

428
00:32:48,718 --> 00:32:50,276
做了微调，就是重新平台化。
Tweaked is replatform.

429
00:32:50,990 --> 00:32:53,860
用购买的产品替换了，就是重新购买。
Replaced with the purchase product is repurchase.

430
00:32:54,702 --> 00:32:56,356
重写了代码，就是重构。
Re-written is refactor.

431
00:32:56,782 --> 00:32:57,988
删除了，就是退役。
Deleted is retire.

432
00:32:58,702 --> 00:32:59,720
保持原样，就是保留。
Left alone is retain.

433
00:33:00,878 --> 00:33:04,196
且在操作不变的情况下整体迁移，就是重新定位。
And moved wholesale with operations intact is relocate.

434
00:33:04,686 --> 00:33:06,916
场景中的其他所有信息都是背景信息。
Everything else in the scenario is context.

435
00:33:08,334 --> 00:33:15,076
重新托管和重新平台化是最容易丢分的两个选项，因为它们都保持了应用程序原有的工作方式。
Re-host and replatform are the pair that cost the most marks because both keep the application working the same way.

436
00:33:15,630 --> 00:33:17,764
在重新托管中，没有任何变化。
In a re-host, nothing changes at all.

437
00:33:18,126 --> 00:33:22,596
同样的操作系统，相同的代码，只是改在 AWS 上运行。
Same operating system, same code, just running on AWS instead.

438
00:33:23,088 --> 00:33:32,516
在重新平台化中，一个组件被替换成了对应的 AWS 托管服务。最常见的是将自管理的数据库变为 Amazon RDS。
In a replatform, one component is swapped for a managed AWS equivalent. Most commonly, a self-managed database, becoming Amazon RDS.

439
00:33:33,408 --> 00:33:36,100
应用程序本身的代码没有变动。
The application code itself is untouched.

440
00:33:36,558 --> 00:33:41,732
所以区分点很简单：是否有一个 AWS 托管服务替换了某个组件？
So the separator is simple. Did a managed AWS service replace a component?

441
00:33:42,254 --> 00:33:43,716
如果是，那就是重新平台化。
If yes, replatform.

442
00:33:45,486 --> 00:33:50,852
重构和重新购买都放弃了原有的系统，所以它们会被替换掉。
Refactor and repurchase both abandon the system you had so they get swapped.

443
00:33:51,534 --> 00:33:54,404
区别在于最终谁来拥有这个软件。
The difference is who ends up owning the software.

444
00:33:55,150 --> 00:34:02,084
在重构中，你亲自重写它，把单体架构变成微服务或无服务器函数。
In a refactor, you rewrite it yourself, turning a monolith into microservices or serverless functions.

445
00:34:02,542 --> 00:34:06,340
这是七种策略中最昂贵的一种，但通常回报也最高。
It is the most expensive of the seven and usually the most rewarding.

446
00:34:07,168 --> 00:34:12,580
在重新购买中，你不再拥有软件，而是订阅一个产品。
In a repurchase, you stop owning software altogether and subscribe to a product instead.

447
00:34:13,088 --> 00:34:15,780
重构改变了软件的形态。
Refactor changes the shape of your software.

448
00:34:17,166 --> 00:34:18,659
重新购买则是把它扔掉。
Repurchase throws it away.

449
00:34:20,333 --> 00:34:22,288
有三种策略容易被忽略。
Three strategies get overlooked.

450
00:34:22,478 --> 00:34:29,476
退役是一个真实存在的选项，调查发现，往往有十分之一的资产处于没人使用的状态在运行。
Retire is a real one, and discovery exercises routinely find that a tenth of an estate is running with nobody using it.

451
00:34:29,710 --> 00:34:32,447
关掉这些是成本最低的方案。
Switching those off is the cheapest possible outcome.

452
00:34:32,654 --> 00:34:34,884
所以「退役」通常是正确答案。
So retire is often correct answer.

453
00:34:35,342 --> 00:34:43,300
「保留」意味着因为延迟、合规性规则或无法迁移的许可证，而故意不移动某些内容。
Retain means deliberately not moving something because of latency, a compliance rule, or a license that will not travel.

454
00:34:43,648 --> 00:34:46,788
这是一个有原因的决定，而不是犹豫不决。
It is a decision with a reason, not indecision.

455
00:34:47,438 --> 00:34:52,036
而「重新定位」是在不改变操作方式的情况下，整块搬迁基础设施。
And relocate moves infrastructure wholesale without changing how you operate it.

456
00:34:53,614 --> 00:34:56,547
这种逻辑有助于处理情景题。
One framing that helps with the scenario questions.

457
00:34:57,005 --> 00:35:00,368
没有真正的组织会对所有内容只采用单一策略。
No real organization picks a single strategy for everything.

458
00:35:00,608 --> 00:35:06,788
资产会被分类，不再使用的应用将被退役，简单的那些将被重新托管。
A portfolio gets sorted, the unused applications get retired, the straightforward ones get re-hosted.

459
00:35:07,088 --> 00:35:10,448
少数带有昂贵许可证的将进行重构平台。
A handful with expensive licenses get replatformed.

460
00:35:10,958 --> 00:35:17,188
一两个具有战略重要性的将进行重构，还有一些因为暂时无法移动而被保留。
One or two strategically important ones get refactored, and a few get retained because they cannot move yet.

461
00:35:18,926 --> 00:35:25,124
当题目描述整个资产时，预期答案是分类处理，而不是单一策略。
When a question describes a whole estate, expect the answer to involve sorting rather than one strategy.

462
00:35:26,862 --> 00:35:32,004
AWS 将这一过程描述为三个阶段，相应的工具也对应这些阶段。
AWS describes a journey in three phases and the tooling maps onto them.

463
00:35:32,846 --> 00:35:37,156
「评估」阶段是了解你拥有什么并建立业务案例的阶段。
Assess is where you understand what you have and build a business case.

464
00:35:37,808 --> 00:35:44,036
「动员」阶段是填补技能差距、构建着陆区并试运行一些应用的阶段。
Mobilize is where you close skill gaps, build a landing zone, and pilot a few applications.

465
00:35:44,974 --> 00:35:50,084
「迁移与现代化」则是大规模迁移并改进已迁移内容的阶段。
Migrate and modernize is where you move at scale and then improve what you moved.

466
00:35:50,528 --> 00:35:56,848
这对考试很重要，因为发现和业务案例工具属于评估阶段。
This matters for the exam because the discovery and business case tools belong to the assess phase.

467
00:35:57,088 --> 00:36:02,404
当问题关于早期规划而非执行时，这就是关键线索。
That is the clue when a question is about early planning rather than execution.

468
00:36:04,238 --> 00:36:06,980
这里有六个服务，每个都有特定的功能。
Six services and each has one job.

469
00:36:09,422 --> 00:36:15,172
应用发现服务用于盘点、你的本地部署服务器以及它们的使用情况。
Application Discovery Service Inventories, your on-premises servers, and how they are used.

470
00:36:16,110 --> 00:36:24,360
迁移评估器为迁移建立成本业务案例。Migration Hub 提供一个统一位置来跟踪跨工具和区域的进度。
Migration Evaluator builds the cost business case for moving. Migration Hub gives you one place to track progress across tools and regions.

471
00:36:25,328 --> 00:36:29,700
应用迁移服务是服务器的平移工具。
Application Migration Service is the lift and shift tool for servers.

472
00:36:29,968 --> 00:36:35,328
数据库迁移服务在源数据库继续运行的同时移动数据。
Database migration service moves the data while the source database keeps running.

473
00:36:35,488 --> 00:36:41,156
而架构转换工具负责在不同数据库引擎之间转换架构和代码。
And the Schema conversion tool converts schema and code between different database engines.

474
00:36:42,606 --> 00:36:48,388
DMS 和 SCT 经常被混淆，它们承担的是同一项工作的两个不同部分。
DMS and SCCT are constantly swapped and they do different halves of the same job.

475
00:36:48,768 --> 00:36:50,340
DMS 负责移动数据。
DMS moves the data.

476
00:36:52,430 --> 00:37:00,292
源数据库全程在线。持续复制能让目标端保持同步，切换时的停机时间极短。
The source database stays online throughout. Continuous replication keeps the target in sync and downtime at cut over is minimal.

477
00:37:01,262 --> 00:37:03,140
SCT 转换结构，
SCT converts the structure,

478
00:37:04,046 --> 00:37:07,536
包括表、视图、存储过程和函数。
tables, views, stored procedures and functions.

479
00:37:07,918 --> 00:37:10,692
这是决定大多数问题的区分点。
Here is the separator that decides most questions.

480
00:37:11,758 --> 00:37:14,532
只有在引擎不同时才需要用到 SCT。
SCT is only needed when the engines differ.

481
00:37:15,374 --> 00:37:17,508
从 Oracle 到 Postgres 需要两者。
Oracle to Postgres needs both.

482
00:37:18,286 --> 00:37:21,252
从 Oracle 到 Oracle 只需 DMS。
Oracle to Oracle needs DMS alone.

483
00:37:22,670 --> 00:37:25,892
一个词汇就能决定一整类题目。
One vocabulary word decides a whole family of questions.

484
00:37:26,256 --> 00:37:33,124
「同构」意味着两端引擎相同，比如从 Oracle 到 Oracle 或从 MySQL 到 MySQL。
Homogeneous means the same engine on both sides, Oracle to Oracle or MySQL to MySQL.

485
00:37:33,376 --> 00:37:36,388
架构已经匹配，所以仅用 DMS 就足够了。
The schema already fits, so DMS alone is enough.

486
00:37:36,656 --> 00:37:42,016
「异构」意味着不同引擎，比如从 Oracle 到 Amazon Aurora Postgres。
Heterogeneous means different engines such as Oracle to Amazon, Aurora Postgres.

487
00:37:42,830 --> 00:37:48,420
架构不匹配，所以需要 SCT 先进行转换，然后再由 DMS 迁移数据。
The schema will not fit, so SCT converts it first and then DMS moves the data.

488
00:37:49,646 --> 00:37:57,252
值得注意的是，DMS 的架构转换是 SCCP 的托管版本，在 DMS 控制台中运行。
Worth knowing that DMS C schema conversion is a managed version of SCCP that runs inside the DMS console.

489
00:37:58,926 --> 00:38:02,884
这两者都属于评估阶段，所以它们会作为选项同时出现。
Both of these sit in the assess phase, so they appear together as options.

490
00:38:03,376 --> 00:38:07,076
Application Discovery Service 用来回答：我们目前拥有什么？
Application Discovery Service answers, what have we got?

491
00:38:07,694 --> 00:38:12,868
它负责盘点服务器及其依赖关系，并收集配置和使用数据。
It inventories servers and their dependencies and collects configuration and usage data.

492
00:38:14,990 --> 00:38:18,084
迁移评估器 用来回答：这需要多少成本？
Migration evaluator answers what would it cost?

493
00:38:18,926 --> 00:38:24,324
它生成成本对比和业务案例，是面向财务人员而非工程师的。
It builds a cost comparison and a business case aimed at finance rather than engineers.

494
00:38:24,750 --> 00:38:26,948
所以区分点在于受众。
So the separator is the audience.

495
00:38:27,616 --> 00:38:30,564
「技术清单」意味着 Discovery 服务。
A technical inventory means discovery service.

496
00:38:31,056 --> 00:38:34,916
为了获得批准而进行的「成本预测」，意味着 迁移评估器。
A cost projection to get approval means migration evaluator.

497
00:38:36,590 --> 00:38:37,828
还有两个需要区分。
Two more to separate.

498
00:38:38,256 --> 00:38:42,628
Application Migration Service 是重新托管服务器的推荐方式。
Application migration service is the recommended way to re-host servers.

499
00:38:42,816 --> 00:38:48,036
它在服务器运行的同时进行持续复制，然后以极短的停机时间完成切换。
It replicates them continuously while they keep running, then cuts over with minimal downtime.

500
00:38:48,750 --> 00:38:53,732
如果题目提到「平移」且不涉及应用更改，那就是这个服务。
If a question says lift and shift with no application changes, that is the service.

501
00:38:54,670 --> 00:38:59,376
Migration Hub 在一个地方跟踪跨工具和跨区域的进度。
Migration Hub tracks progress across tools and regions in one place.

502
00:38:59,936 --> 00:39:03,620
关于 Migration Hub，关键点在于它**不**做什么。
The important thing about migration hub is what it does not do.

503
00:39:03,950 --> 00:39:05,316
它永远不会移动任何东西。
It never moves anything.

504
00:39:05,696 --> 00:39:10,020
它是一个仪表板，这正是它作为干扰项的原因。
It is a dashboard, and that is exactly why it works as a distractor.

505
00:39:11,726 --> 00:39:13,828
有一个关于可用性的警告属于这一部分。
One availability warning belongs here.

506
00:39:14,190 --> 00:39:17,092
Snow 系列曾经是这个模块的核心内容。
The Snow family used to be the centerpiece of this module.

507
00:39:17,326 --> 00:39:20,388
现在它不再对新客户开放，也不在考核范围内了。
It is now closed to new customers and off the in-scope list.

508
00:39:21,102 --> 00:39:25,316
Snowball 在商业区域的支持将于今年 12 月 31 日结束。
Snowball support ends in commercial regions on the 31st of December this year.

509
00:39:26,222 --> 00:39:33,796
较旧的题库仍将 Snowball 作为离线批量传输的答案，在考试中这个答案依然成立。
Older question banks still use Snowball as the offline bulk transfer answer, and on the exam that answer still stands.

510
00:39:34,030 --> 00:39:39,616
在实践中，它的继任者是 DataSync、Data Transfer Family 和 Direct Connect。
In practice, the successors are datasync, the data transfer terminal, and direct connect.

511
00:39:40,078 --> 00:39:42,212
第 22 模块里有详细讲解这个内容。
Module 22 covers this properly.

512
00:39:43,982 --> 00:39:46,212
实战场景 1。
Worked scenario 1.

513
00:39:50,478 --> 00:40:01,776
一家公司在自己的数据中心，在 Linux 服务器上运行 Java 应用程序，并使用独立硬件上的自管理 Postgres 数据库。租赁将在 5 个月后到期。
A company runs a Java application on Linux servers in its own data center with a self-managed Postgres database on separate hardware. The lease expires in 5 months.

514
00:40:02,094 --> 00:40:08,452
团队将 Java 应用程序迁移到 EC2 实例上，完全不需要更改代码。
The team moves the Java application onto EC2 instances with no code changes at all.

515
00:40:09,296 --> 00:40:16,964
数据库迁移到 Amazon RDS for Postgres，哪种迁移策略描述了数据库的变化？
The database moves on to Amazon RDS for Postgres, which migration strategy describes what happened to the database.

516
00:40:17,296 --> 00:40:23,536
A. 重放（Rehost），B. 重新平台化（Replatform），C. 重构（Refactor），D. 重新购买（Repurchase）。
A rehost, B Replatform, C Refactor, D. Repurchase.

517
00:40:23,886 --> 00:40:24,932
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

518
00:40:30,912 --> 00:40:32,228
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

519
00:40:32,512 --> 00:40:33,316
重新平台化。
Replatform.

520
00:40:33,710 --> 00:40:40,004
注意这个场景的操作。它描述了两个同时发生的不同策略，然后询问其中一个。
Notice what this scenario does. It describes two different strategies happening at once and then asks about one of them.

521
00:40:42,190 --> 00:40:43,844
应用程序是重放的。
The application was re-hosted.

522
00:40:44,192 --> 00:40:46,052
数据库是重新平台化的。
The database was replatformed.

523
00:40:46,670 --> 00:40:52,516
选项 A 不是对迁移过程的错误描述，而是对所提问题的错误回答。
Option A is not a wrong description of the migration, it is a wrong answer to the question that was asked.

524
00:40:52,910 --> 00:40:58,180
这种模式在这个领域很常见，因为真实的迁移总是包含多种策略。
That pattern is common in this domain because real migrations always make strategies.

525
00:40:58,702 --> 00:41:02,116
仔细阅读最后一行，并检查它指代的是哪个组件。
Read the last line carefully and check which component it names.

526
00:41:03,886 --> 00:41:05,060
实战场景 2。
Work scenario 2.

527
00:41:05,678 --> 00:41:14,660
一家保险公司必须将 Oracle 数据库迁移到 Amazon Aurora Postgres。该数据库包含数百个用 Oracle PLSQL 编写的存储过程。
An insurer must migrate an Oracle database to Amazon Aurora Postgres. It contains several hundred stored procedures written in Oracle PLSQL.

528
00:41:15,278 --> 00:41:22,592
业务要求现有的 Oracle 数据库在整个过程中对用户保持可用，仅在最后有短暂的切换窗口。
The business requires the existing Oracle database to stay available to users throughout with only a brief cutover window at the end.

529
00:41:23,182 --> 00:41:25,764
保险公司应该使用哪两个服务？
Which two services should the insurer use?

530
00:41:26,126 --> 00:41:30,532
A. Database Migration Service B. schema conversion tool（架构转换工具）。
A Database Migration Service B schema conversion tool.

531
00:41:30,992 --> 00:41:35,300
C. application migration service D. Migration Hub。
C application migration service D Migration Hub.

532
00:41:35,726 --> 00:41:35,952
E。
E.

533
00:41:36,366 --> 00:41:37,860
AWS Backup。
AWS Backup.

534
00:41:38,574 --> 00:41:39,232
选两个。
Choose two.

535
00:41:39,694 --> 00:41:40,932
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

536
00:41:47,150 --> 00:41:48,772
答案是 A 和 B。
The answers are A and B.

537
00:41:48,992 --> 00:41:57,668
题干中的两个细节起到了关键作用。从 Oracle 到 Aurora Postgres 意味着引擎不同，这使得它属于异构迁移，因此需要两件工具。
Two details in the STEM do the work. Oracle to Aurora Postgres means different engines, which makes this heterogeneous and therefore a 2-tool job.

538
00:41:58,030 --> 00:42:05,572
而且那几百个存储过程使得 SCT 变得不可或缺，因为如果不转换，PLSQL 就无法在 Postgres 上运行。
And the several hundred stored procedures make SCT unavoidable because PLSQL will not run on Postgres unconverted.

539
00:42:06,192 --> 00:42:11,716
“全程保持可用”的要求直接指向 DMS 的持续复制功能。
The stay available throughout requirement points straight at DMS continuous replication.

540
00:42:12,352 --> 00:42:20,672
选项 D 是一个有趣的干扰项，因为这里确实会用到 Migration Hub，但它本身并不负责迁移任何内容。
Option D is the interesting distractor because migration hub genuinely would be used here. It just does not migrate anything.

541
00:42:21,646 --> 00:42:23,236
工作场景 3。
Work scenario 3.

542
00:42:23,982 --> 00:42:26,916
一家制造商计划迁出其数据中心。
A manufacturer is planning to leave its data center.

543
00:42:27,950 --> 00:42:30,756
在做出决定前，董事会要求一份成本预测。
Before committing, the board wants a cost projection.

544
00:42:31,552 --> 00:42:34,148
他们需要将其与当前的现有状态进行对比。
It can compare against the current estate.

545
00:42:35,246 --> 00:42:38,244
报告必须是财务总监可以审阅的格式。
It must be in a form the finance director can review.

546
00:42:39,182 --> 00:42:44,036
目前还没有人提供 400 台服务器上实际运行内容的清单。
Nobody has yet produced a list of what is actually running on the 400 servers.

547
00:42:44,494 --> 00:42:46,500
他们应该从哪两个服务开始？
Which two services should they start with?

548
00:42:47,022 --> 00:42:49,348
A. 应用发现服务（Application Discovery Service）
A Application Discovery Service,

549
00:42:49,998 --> 00:42:52,292
B. 迁移评估器
B Migration Evaluator,

550
00:42:53,102 --> 00:42:55,012
C. 价格计算器
C Pricing Calculator,

551
00:42:55,726 --> 00:42:58,372
D. 应用迁移服务
D application migration service,

552
00:42:59,152 --> 00:42:59,392
E。
E.

553
00:42:59,792 --> 00:43:00,868
成本管理器
Cost Explorer.

554
00:43:02,318 --> 00:43:04,836
暂停并思考一下。
Choose to pause and decide.

555
00:43:11,022 --> 00:43:12,420
答案是 A 和 B。
The answers are A and B.

556
00:43:12,750 --> 00:43:15,076
两个短语将此项置于评估阶段。
Two phrases place this in the assess phase.

557
00:43:15,438 --> 00:43:18,404
“在做出决定前”以及“还没有人提供清单”。
Before committing, and nobody has yet produced a list.

558
00:43:20,238 --> 00:43:26,884
选项 C 是非常强力的干扰项，因为价格计算器确实可以估算 AWS 成本。
Option C is the strongest distractor by some distance because the pricing calculator does estimate AWS costs.

559
00:43:27,726 --> 00:43:33,348
但它只能对你已知配置的方案定价，且无法与当前的现状进行对比。
But it only prices a configuration you already know and it cannot compare against your current state.

560
00:43:34,926 --> 00:43:42,340
迁移评估器的存在就是为了做这种对比，而选项 E 在简单的逻辑点上失败了。
Migration evaluator exists specifically to make that comparison, and option E fails on a simple point of logic.

561
00:43:43,694 --> 00:43:48,324
成本管理器分析的是 AWS 的支出，而这家公司目前还没有任何支出。
Cost Explorer analyses AWS spend, and this company has none yet.

562
00:43:50,010 --> 00:43:51,230
工作场景 4。
Worked Scenario 4.

563
00:43:52,610 --> 00:43:56,650
在一次调研过程中，一家零售商发现了三个被遗忘的系统。
During a discovery exercise, a retailer finds three forgotten systems.

564
00:43:57,646 --> 00:44:00,530
一个报表工具已经有 14 个月没有登录记录了。
A reporting tool has had no logins for 14 months.

565
00:44:01,230 --> 00:44:07,460
一个薪资系统必须保留在本地，直到监管机构批准迁移，这至少需要一年的时间。
A payroll system must stay on premises until a regulator approves the move, which will take at least a year.

566
00:44:08,366 --> 00:44:15,940
还有一个客户支持派工系统正被替换为团队已经选定的商业 SaaS 订阅。
And a customer support picketing system is being replaced with a commercial SaaS subscription the team has already chosen.

567
00:44:16,814 --> 00:44:20,676
请按描述的顺序选择对应的策略。
Which strategies apply in the order the systems are described.

568
00:44:21,390 --> 00:44:22,660
暂停并思考一下。
Pause and decide.

569
00:44:28,846 --> 00:44:30,384
答案是 A。
The answer is A.

570
00:44:30,958 --> 00:44:35,044
这是本模块前面提到的“组合模式”的明确体现。
This is the portfolio pattern from earlier in the module made explicit.

571
00:44:35,424 --> 00:44:41,184
一个资产，三个系统，三种不同的策略，每一项都由一个特定的短语来标识。
One estate, three systems, three different strategies, and each one is signaled by a single clause.

572
00:44:41,424 --> 00:44:43,744
“14个月内无登录”属于退役（退役）。
No logins in 14 months is retired.

573
00:44:44,046 --> 00:44:45,988
“被监管机构阻止”属于保留（保留）。
Blocked by a regulator is retained.

574
00:44:46,926 --> 00:44:50,244
“更换为 SaaS 订阅”属于重新购买（重新购买）。
Replace by a SaaS subscription is repurchase.

575
00:44:51,246 --> 00:44:54,980
选项 D 是最接近的干扰项，而区分点在于所有权。
Option D is the closest miss and the separator is ownership.

576
00:44:56,014 --> 00:45:00,484
重新平台化（Replatform）保留你的软件，但更换其底层的组件。
Replatform keeps your software and swaps a component underneath it.

577
00:45:01,294 --> 00:45:05,668
这里是完全放弃该软件，这属于重新购买。
Here the software is being abandoned altogether, which is repurchase.

578
00:45:07,342 --> 00:45:12,676
总结一下，询问应用程序本身发生了什么变化，然后与这七个名称进行匹配。
To recap, ask what happened to the application itself and match it against the seven names.

579
00:45:13,326 --> 00:45:17,828
重新托管（Rehost）不改变任何内容，而重新平台化是将一个组件更换为托管服务。
Rehost changes nothing while replatform swaps a component for a managed service.

580
00:45:18,638 --> 00:45:24,964
不同的数据库引擎意味着 SCT，然后是 DMS；而相同的引擎仅意味着 DMS。
Different database engines means SCT, then DMS, while the same engine means DMS alone.

581
00:45:25,902 --> 00:45:34,692
发现服务清单、迁移评估器、构建业务案例以及在不移动任何内容的情况下进行跟踪的 Migration Hub。
Discovery Service Inventories, Migration Evaluator, Builds the Business Case and Migration Hub tracks without moving anything.

582
00:45:35,886 --> 00:45:39,332
下一个模块，AWS 云采用框架（云采用框架）。
Next module, the AWS Cloud Adoption Framework.

583
00:45:40,814 --> 00:45:49,540
AWS 云采用框架在考试指南中被直接提及，并且在题库分析中出现了 29 道题目。
The AWS Cloud Adoption Framework is named directly in the exam guide and it turned up in 29 questions in the bank analysis.

584
00:45:50,606 --> 00:45:54,372
对于大多数课程只给 4 分钟讲解的课题来说，这个比例很高。
That is a lot for a topic most courses give 4 minutes to.

585
00:45:56,110 --> 00:46:00,710
它几乎全是词汇量考查，这让它成为最容易拿分的题目之一。
It is also almost entirely vocabulary which makes it some of the cheapest marks available.

586
00:46:02,610 --> 00:46:09,770
先看看为什么 AWS 要费心去写这个。迁移失败通常不是因为技术不起作用。
Start with why AWS bothered to write this. Migrations do not usually fail because the technology did not work.

587
00:46:10,126 --> 00:46:17,444
它们失败是因为没人负责决策，或者运维团队从未接受过培训，或者财务部门无法批准变动费用。
They failed because nobody owned the decision or the operations team was never trained or finance could not approve a variable bill.

588
00:46:18,126 --> 00:46:24,772
云采用框架的存在是为了在同步项目之前识别出这些组织层面的漏洞。
The cloud adoption framework exists to name those organizational gaps before they sync a program.

589
00:46:26,830 --> 00:46:31,504
一旦你明白这一点，这个框架的结构就不再显得随意了。
Once you see that, the structure of the framework stops feeling arbitrary.

590
00:46:32,814 --> 00:46:36,996
这两个是人们经常混淆的框架，所以现在就把它们区分开。
These two are the frameworks people swap, so separate them now.

591
00:46:37,806 --> 00:46:40,868
云采用框架是关于组织的。
The cloud adoption framework is about the organization.

592
00:46:41,486 --> 00:46:42,304
“它准备好了吗？”
Is it ready?

593
00:46:42,542 --> 00:46:43,504
“谁负责什么？”
Who owns what?

594
00:46:43,822 --> 00:46:45,188
“技能缺口在哪里？”
Where are the skill gaps?

595
00:46:45,870 --> 00:46:48,324
它用于转型前和转型过程中。
It is used before and during a transformation.

596
00:46:48,878 --> 00:46:51,908
它的受众包括高管和人力资源部门。
And its audience includes executives and HR.

597
00:46:52,704 --> 00:47:00,100
良好架构框架（Well-Architected Framework）是关于特定工作负载设计的，用于架构师构建或审查系统时使用。
The well-architected framework is about a specific workloads design used when architects build or review a system.

598
00:47:00,544 --> 00:47:07,104
如果场景提到就绪情况、技能、利益相关者或治理，那就是 云采用框架。
If the scenario mentions readiness, skills, stakeholders, or governance, it is CAF.

599
00:47:08,878 --> 00:47:13,572
六个维度，每一个都对应一组需要参与讨论的人员。
Six perspectives and each one names a group of people who need to be in the room.

600
00:47:15,598 --> 00:47:19,460
业务维度确保云投资与业务目标相匹配。
Business makes sure cloud investment matches business objectives.

601
00:47:20,078 --> 00:47:23,876
「人员」涵盖文化、技能、培训和组织变革。
People covers culture, skills, training, and organizational change.

602
00:47:24,526 --> 00:47:28,228
「治理」负责管理风险、成本、合规性和监管。
Governance manages risk, cost, compliance, and oversight.

603
00:47:29,166 --> 00:47:33,124
「平台」构建云环境并实现工作负载现代化。
Platform builds the cloud environment and modernizes workloads.

604
00:47:33,424 --> 00:47:37,604
「安全」涵盖机密性、完整性和可用性。
Security covers confidentiality, integrity, and availability.

605
00:47:38,094 --> 00:47:40,868
而「运营」负责运行和支持各项服务。
And operations runs and supports the services.

606
00:47:41,454 --> 00:47:45,956
框架的第三版将这些内容拆分为 47 项能力。
Version 3 of the framework splits these into 47 capabilities.

607
00:47:47,214 --> 00:47:49,796
你需要记住这六个名称，而不是那 47 个。
You need the six names, not the 47.

608
00:47:51,502 --> 00:47:54,788
这种划分让这六个核心概念更容易掌握。
A split that makes the six much easier to hold.

609
00:47:55,310 --> 00:48:01,860
「业务」、「人员」和「治理」是属于高管、人力资源和合规部门的业务能力。
Business, people, and governance are the business capabilities owned by executives, HR, and compliance.

610
00:48:02,144 --> 00:48:05,924
它们回答的是：我们应该做吗？我们能做吗？谁来做决定？
They answer should we, can we, and who decides?

611
00:48:06,704 --> 00:48:11,748
「平台」、「安全」和「运营」是属于工程部门的技术能力。
Platform, security, and operations are the technical capabilities owned by engineering.

612
00:48:12,558 --> 00:48:15,012
它们回答的是：我们如何构建并运行它？
They answer how do we build and run it?

613
00:48:15,406 --> 00:48:24,676
大多数学习资料侧重于技术类的三个，而略过了其他几个，但这恰恰搞反了，因为业务类的那三个才是转型中真正卡壳的地方。
Most study material covers the technical three and skims the others, which is precisely backwards, because the business three are where transformations actually stall.

614
00:48:26,126 --> 00:48:28,612
这是你在考试中使用的反向查找逻辑。
Here is the reverse lookup you use in the exam.

615
00:48:28,846 --> 00:48:32,272
投资回报率和业务案例意味着「业务」。
Return on investment and business cases means business.

616
00:48:32,512 --> 00:48:36,672
培训、云能力熟练度和对变革的抵触情绪意味着「人员」。
Training, cloud fluency, and resistance to change means people.

617
00:48:38,112 --> 00:48:41,828
成本控制、风险和监管意味着「治理」。
Cost control, risk, and oversight means governance.

618
00:48:42,592 --> 00:48:45,252
构建着陆区意味着「平台」。
Building the landing zone means platform.

619
00:48:46,352 --> 00:48:49,072
身份验证和数据保护意味着「安全」。
Identity and data protection means security.

620
00:48:49,358 --> 00:48:52,032
监控和服务级别意味着「运营」。
Monitoring and service levels means operations.

621
00:48:52,192 --> 00:48:54,432
其中两个类别涵盖了大部分题目。
Two of these carry most of the questions.

622
00:48:54,672 --> 00:48:57,124
任何关于培训或文化的，都属于「人员」。
Anything about training or culture is people.

623
00:48:57,312 --> 00:49:00,324
任何关于成本控制或风险的，都属于「治理」。
Anything about cost control or risk is governance.

624
00:49:01,710 --> 00:49:07,072
「人员」视角值得单独用一页来讲，因为它出现的频率最高。
The people perspective deserves its own slide because it is the one that appears most.

625
00:49:07,232 --> 00:49:09,508
它涵盖的是文化，而不只是培训。
It covers culture, not just training.

626
00:49:10,190 --> 00:49:13,796
让团队从 Waterfall 转向 Agile 是一个「人员」问题。
Moving a team from waterfall to agile is a people matter.

627
00:49:14,766 --> 00:49:23,428
填补技能差距、认证路径和云能力熟练度计划都属于这里，组织变革管理和员工的抵触情绪也包含在内。
Closing skill gaps, certification paths, and cloud fluency programs all sit here, as do organizational change management and staff resistance.

628
00:49:24,110 --> 00:49:25,348
有一点值得注意
One thing worth noticing

629
00:49:25,998 --> 00:49:28,708
聘请合作伙伴来完成工作并不能解决问题
hiring a partner to do the work does not close.

630
00:49:29,166 --> 00:49:33,252
因为你的员工在之后仍然无法独立运行这些结果。这就是「人员」方面的缺口。
A people gap because your own staff still cannot run the result afterwards.

631
00:49:34,958 --> 00:49:38,500
治理和运营听起来很接近，经常被混淆。
Governance and operations sound adjacent and get swapped.

632
00:49:39,118 --> 00:49:42,052
治理是在工作之前和过程中进行的管控。
Governance is controlled before and around the work.

633
00:49:42,574 --> 00:49:46,372
包括成本管理、风险、合规性、投资组合决策。
Cost management, risk, compliance, portfolio decisions.

634
00:49:47,214 --> 00:49:49,956
运营是日常运行结果。
Operations is running the result day to day.

635
00:49:50,606 --> 00:49:54,592
监控事件、问题和服务级别。
Monitoring incidents, problems, service levels.

636
00:49:55,118 --> 00:49:58,032
核心区别在于每个维度关注的问题不同。
The clean test is the question each one asks.

637
00:49:58,352 --> 00:50:01,156
治理问的是：我们应该花这笔钱吗？
Governance asks whether we should be spending this.

638
00:50:01,632 --> 00:50:05,028
运营问的是：它现在运行正常吗？
Operations asks whether it is working right now.

639
00:50:05,550 --> 00:50:07,108
注意一点。
And be careful with one thing.

640
00:50:07,854 --> 00:50:11,620
监测威胁属于安全性视角，而不是运营。
Monitoring for threats is the security perspective, not operations.

641
00:50:13,294 --> 00:50:17,476
四个转型领域描述的是实际上在改变什么。
Four transformation domains and these describe what is actually changing.

642
00:50:18,062 --> 00:50:23,588
技术意味着迁移和现代化基础设施、应用和数据。
Technology means migrating and modernizing infrastructure, applications, and data.

643
00:50:24,270 --> 00:50:28,516
流程意味着将业务运营方式数字化和自动化。
Process means digitizing and automating how the business operates.

644
00:50:30,222 --> 00:50:34,916
组织意味着围绕产品而非职能来重组团队。
Organization means reorganizing teams around products rather than functions.

645
00:50:35,854 --> 00:50:40,004
产品意味着重新构思业务销售的内容。
And product means reimagining what the business sells.

646
00:50:41,870 --> 00:50:45,636
一个单一的举措通常会同时涉及这四个领域。
A single initiative usually touches all four at once.

647
00:50:46,350 --> 00:50:47,268
注意拼写。
Note the spelling.

648
00:50:47,950 --> 00:50:55,716
AWS 将第三个领域写成带 Z 的 组织，因为它在框架中是一个专有名词。
AWS writes the third domain as organization with a Z because it is a proper noun in the framework.

649
00:50:57,294 --> 00:51:00,484
四个阶段描述的是事情发生的时机。
Four phases and they describe when things happen.

650
00:51:01,072 --> 00:51:06,852
愿景展示云将如何加速业务成果并确定优先机会。
Envision shows how cloud will accelerate business outcomes and prioritizes opportunities.

651
00:51:07,312 --> 00:51:13,028
对齐旨在找出六个视角中的能力差距，并解决利益相关者的担忧。
Align finds capability gaps across the six perspectives and surfaces stakeholder concerns.

652
00:51:13,966 --> 00:51:18,788
启动是在生产环境中交付试点项目并验证增量价值。
Launch delivers pilot initiatives in production and proves incremental value.

653
00:51:20,014 --> 00:51:24,484
扩展是扩大这些试点，并确保收益真正实现。
Scale expands those pilots and makes sure the benefits are actually realized.

654
00:51:25,870 --> 00:51:31,460
这个序列是循环的而不是结束，因为每个新工作负载都会重新开始周期。
The sequence loops rather than ending because each new workload starts the cycle again.

655
00:51:32,750 --> 00:51:36,804
三个层面对应三个不同的问题，它们并不是互相替代的关系。
Three layers and three different questions, and they are not alternatives to each other.

656
00:51:37,710 --> 00:51:40,420
六个视角告诉你谁负责。
Six perspectives tell you who is responsible.

657
00:51:41,358 --> 00:51:43,492
四个领域告诉你改变了什么。
Four domains tell you what is changing.

658
00:51:44,238 --> 00:51:46,980
四个阶段告诉你你处于旅程的哪个位置。
Four phases tell you where you are in the journey.

659
00:51:47,918 --> 00:51:49,988
这三个维度同时在运作。
All three operate at once.

660
00:51:50,894 --> 00:51:54,468
考试中的一个有用习惯是先识别出属于哪个层面。
The useful exam habit is to identify the layer first.

661
00:51:54,862 --> 00:51:57,712
一个特定的群体意味着一个视角。
A named group of people means a perspective.

662
00:51:58,030 --> 00:52:00,100
一种变化类型意味着一个领域。
A type of change means a domain.

663
00:52:01,774 --> 00:52:04,292
时间线上的一个点意味着一个阶段。
A point in the timeline means a phase.

664
00:52:05,358 --> 00:52:08,868
选项很少会把这三者混淆，所以判断起来很快。
Answer options rarely mix the three, which makes this quick.

665
00:52:10,574 --> 00:52:16,112
考试指南列出了四个业务成果。该框架的目标就是这些，所以要把它们作为一个整体来记。
The exam guide names four business outcomes. The framework aims at so learn them as a set.

666
00:52:16,366 --> 00:52:20,612
降低业务风险，意味着更好的韧性、安全性以及合规性。
Reduce business risk, meaning better resilience, security, and compliance.

667
00:52:21,646 --> 00:52:26,788
提高环境、社会和治理表现，通常简称为 ESG。
Improved environmental, social and governance performance, usually shortened to ESG.

668
00:52:27,790 --> 00:52:38,352
通过新产品、新市场和更快的上市速度来增加收入。同时提高运营效率，意味着用更少的精力和成本完成同样的工作。
Increased revenue through new products, new markets, and faster time to market. And increased operational efficiency, meaning the same work with less effort and cost.

669
00:52:39,374 --> 00:52:45,552
ESG 是考生最不预料到的，而且在指南中明确提到了它。
ESG is the one candidates do not expect and it is named explicitly in the guide.

670
00:52:46,862 --> 00:52:48,868
处理场景 1。
Worked scenario 1.

671
00:52:49,326 --> 00:52:52,228
一家物流公司批准了云迁移。
A logistics company has approved a cloud migration.

672
00:52:52,526 --> 00:53:04,192
六周后，进度停滞。基础设施团队熟悉 AWS，但运营团队从未运行过云环境并公开表示抵触。目前没有培训计划。
Six weeks in, progress has stalled. The infrastructure team is comfortable with AWS, but the operations team has never run a cloud environment and is openly resistant. No training program exists.

673
00:53:04,814 --> 00:53:07,716
哪个云采用框架视角能解决这个问题？
Which CAF perspective addresses this?

674
00:53:08,238 --> 00:53:09,508
A. 运营。
A. Operations.

675
00:53:09,952 --> 00:53:10,912
B 人员。
B people.

676
00:53:11,598 --> 00:53:12,772
C 治理。
C governance.

677
00:53:13,072 --> 00:53:14,272
D 平台。
D platform.

678
00:53:14,606 --> 00:53:15,588
停下来做决定。
Pause and decide.

679
00:53:21,774 --> 00:53:23,792
答案是 B 人员。
The answer is B people.

680
00:53:24,352 --> 00:53:33,092
选项 A 是本课程中较好的干扰项，因为题干里确实提到了运营团队，而且确实有一个运营视角。
Option A is one of the better distractors in this course because the STEM literally says operations team and there is an operations perspective.

681
00:53:33,472 --> 00:53:35,712
但要看真正的差距在哪里。
But read what the gap actually is.

682
00:53:36,046 --> 00:53:38,992
“从未运行过云环境”是技能差距。
Never run a cloud environment is a skills gap.

683
00:53:39,438 --> 00:53:42,052
“公开抵触”是变革管理差距。
Openly resistant is a change management gap.

684
00:53:42,990 --> 00:53:45,124
“没有培训计划”是培训差距。
No training program is a training gap.

685
00:53:45,646 --> 00:53:46,948
这三者都属于人员范畴。
All three are people.

686
00:53:47,662 --> 00:53:54,212
如果问题是关于监控、事件或服务级别的，那么才会适用运营视角。
The operations perspective would apply if the question were about monitoring, incidents, or service levels.

687
00:53:54,766 --> 00:53:59,108
题干中提到的一个具体团队并不等同于一个特定的视角。
A named team in the STEM is not the same as a named perspective.

688
00:54:00,846 --> 00:54:01,892
处理场景。
Worked scenario.

689
00:54:02,446 --> 00:54:06,628
2. 一家零售商正处于其云计划的最开始阶段。
2. A retailer is at the very start of its cloud program.

690
00:54:07,022 --> 00:54:14,468
它举办了一场引导式研讨会，以确定哪些转型机会最能加速其业务目标。
It has run a facilitated workshop to identify which transformation opportunities would most accelerate its business objectives.

691
00:54:15,022 --> 00:54:19,556
每一个都与高级利益相关者和可衡量的结果挂钩。
Each one is linked to a senior stakeholder and a measurable outcome.

692
00:54:20,014 --> 00:54:23,396
它还没有评估任何人的技能，也没有构建任何东西。
It has not yet assessed anyone's skills or built anything.

693
00:54:24,110 --> 00:54:27,076
该零售商处于哪个 云采用框架 阶段？
Which CAF phase is the retailer in?

694
00:54:28,110 --> 00:54:29,092
A. 愿景
A Envision.

695
00:54:29,392 --> 00:54:30,340
B. 对齐
B align.

696
00:54:30,592 --> 00:54:31,748
C. 启动
C launch.

697
00:54:32,112 --> 00:54:33,152
D. 扩展
D scale.

698
00:54:33,632 --> 00:54:34,788
停下来思考一下，做出决定。
Pause and decide.

699
00:54:40,654 --> 00:54:41,872
答案是 A。
The answer is A.

700
00:54:42,352 --> 00:54:43,044
愿景。
Envision.

701
00:54:43,758 --> 00:54:50,404
“愿景”和“对齐”是一对需要仔细区分的选项，因为两者都在构建任何东西之前发生。
Envision and Align are the pair worth separating carefully because both happen before anything is built.

702
00:54:51,054 --> 00:54:56,516
“愿景”是根据业务目标确定优先事项，并将它们与利益相关者联系起来。
Envision prioritizes opportunities against business objectives and ties them to stakeholders.

703
00:54:57,070 --> 00:55:00,832
“对齐”是找出跨越六个视角的各种能力差距。
Align finds the capability gaps across the six perspectives.

704
00:55:01,262 --> 00:55:04,996
这个案例在最后一句中刻意加入了区分点。
The scenario plans the separator deliberately in its last sentence.

705
00:55:05,232 --> 00:55:07,492
它还没有评估任何人的技能。
It has not yet assessed anyone's skills.

706
00:55:07,792 --> 00:55:13,188
技能评估属于“对齐”活动，所以如果还没进行，该零售商仍处于“愿景”阶段。
Skills assessment is the align activity, so if it has not happened, the retailer is still in envision.

707
00:55:14,478 --> 00:55:15,588
正确的案例。
Worked scenario.

708
00:55:17,614 --> 00:55:20,592
3. 一家银行的云计划正在进行中。
3. A bank's cloud program is underway.

709
00:55:21,006 --> 00:55:26,340
财务部门担心团队现在可以在没有采购订单的情况下配置资源。
Finance is concerned that teams can now provision resources without a purchase order.

710
00:55:26,894 --> 00:55:32,900
目前还没有达成一致的方法来将支出归属到各个业务单元，或者阻止团队超出其分配额度。
There is no agreed way to attribute spend to business units or to stop a team exceeding its allocation.

711
00:55:33,712 --> 00:55:39,748
另外，首席风险官希望确保监管义务正在被跟踪。
Separately, the chief risk officer wants assurance that regulatory obligations are being tracked.

712
00:55:40,272 --> 00:55:42,692
哪个视角涵盖了这两个担忧？
Which perspective covers both concerns?

713
00:55:43,118 --> 00:55:47,940
A. 业务，B. 运营，C. 治理。
A business, B operations, C governance.

714
00:55:48,366 --> 00:55:49,636
D. 安全性。
D. Security.

715
00:55:50,254 --> 00:55:51,780
停下来思考一下，做出决定。
Pause and decide.

716
00:55:58,126 --> 00:56:01,124
答案是 C 治理。
The answer is C governance.

717
00:56:01,632 --> 00:56:08,484
这个案例故意给出了来自两个不同高管的两个问题，而这两个问题都属于同一个视角。
This scenario deliberately gives two concerns from two different executives and both land in the same perspective.

718
00:56:08,832 --> 00:56:12,932
不受控制的支出和没有成本归属属于成本管理。
Uncontrolled spend and no cost attribution is cost management.

719
00:56:14,432 --> 00:56:18,308
跟踪监管义务属于风险和合规性管理。
Tracking regulatory obligations is risk and compliance management.

720
00:56:19,214 --> 00:56:21,152
这两者都属于治理能力。
Both are governance capabilities.

721
00:56:21,392 --> 00:56:33,312
选项 D 是针对模式匹配的陷阱。虽然「银行」和「首席风险官」这些词让安全性看起来很对，但实际上并没有描述任何关于威胁、控制措施或数据保护的内容。
Option D is the trap for pattern matches. The words bank and chief risk officer make security feel right, but nothing about threats, controls, or data protection is actually described.

722
00:56:33,552 --> 00:56:37,124
要看题目要求的是什么，而不是它发生在哪个行业。
Read what is being asked for, not what industry it happens in.

723
00:56:38,766 --> 00:56:40,164
处理情景 4。
Worked scenario 4.

724
00:56:40,878 --> 00:56:44,196
一家出版商的董事会询问为什么要资助一个云项目。
A publisher's board asks why it should fund a cloud program.

725
00:56:44,782 --> 00:56:48,352
首席执行官列出了四个预期的收益。
The chief executive lists four expected benefits.

726
00:56:48,686 --> 00:56:53,572
减少影响客户的停机，降低报告中的能源消耗。
Fewer outages affecting customers, lower energy consumption in its reporting.

727
00:56:54,414 --> 00:56:57,444
一个以前无法构建的新订阅产品。
A new subscription product it could not build before.

728
00:56:58,222 --> 00:57:00,752
以及减少在手动发布上花费的人工工时。
And fewer staff hours spent on manual releases.

729
00:57:00,912 --> 00:57:09,152
这四个中有几个被提到了？云采用框架 业务成果 A1、B、2、C、3、B，全部四个。
How many of these four are named? CAF business outcomes A1, B, 2, C, 3, B, all four.

730
00:57:09,392 --> 00:57:10,468
停下来思考一下并做出决定。
Pause and decide.

731
00:57:16,302 --> 00:57:17,444
答案是 D。
The answer is D.

732
00:57:17,648 --> 00:57:18,372
全部四个。
All four.

733
00:57:18,688 --> 00:57:21,956
每一个收益都对应一个明确的成果。
Each benefit maps onto exactly one named outcome.

734
00:57:22,288 --> 00:57:28,100
减少停机是降低业务风险。降低能源消耗是提高 ESG 表现。
Fewer outages is reduced business risk. Lower energy consumption is improved. ESG performance.

735
00:57:28,528 --> 00:57:31,248
新的订阅产品是增加收入。
A new subscription product is increased revenue.

736
00:57:31,328 --> 00:57:36,036
减少手动发布的人工工时是提高运营效率。
And fewer staff hours on manual releases is increased operational efficiency.

737
00:57:36,654 --> 00:57:40,836
选项 C 是一个非常接近的干扰项，而且它之所以接近是有明确原因的。
Option C is the near miss and it is near for a predictable reason.

738
00:57:41,168 --> 00:57:48,420
大多数考生会排除掉能源这一项，因为他们不认为云框架中会提到可持续性相关的成果。
Most candidates drop the energy item because they do not expect a sustainability outcome to be named in a cloud framework.

739
00:57:48,974 --> 00:57:51,556
但在考试大纲中，它被明确列出来了。
It is named explicitly in the exam guide.

740
00:57:53,230 --> 00:57:59,492
总结一下，云采用框架 是关于组织的，而架构良好是关于工作负载的。
To recap, CAF is about the organization while well architected is about a workload.

741
00:57:59,854 --> 00:58:05,956
六个视角、四个领域、四个阶段，先识别出层级就能快速找到答案。
Six perspectives, four domains, four phases, and identifying the layer first makes the answer come quickly.

742
00:58:07,054 --> 00:58:12,132
培训和文化始终属于人员，成本控制和风险始终属于治理。
Training and culture is always people, cost control and risk is always governance.

743
00:58:13,102 --> 00:58:17,476
愿景优先考虑机会，而对齐旨在寻找能力差距。
Envision prioritizes opportunities while Align finds capability gaps.

744
00:58:17,902 --> 00:58:21,604
并且记住，题干中的名称词汇并不等同于命名视角。
And remember that a name beam in the stem is not a name perspective.

745
00:58:21,870 --> 00:58:23,940
要读出缺口所在，而不是职位头衔。
Read the gap, not the job title.

746
00:58:24,846 --> 00:58:29,892
进入下一个模块，共享责任模型以及考试中最大领域的开始。
Next module, the shared responsibility model and the start of the largest domain on the exam.

747
00:58:31,438 --> 00:58:36,928
本模块开启领域 2，这是考试中占比最大的领域，占 30%。
This module opens domain 2, the largest domain on the exam at 30%.

748
00:58:40,366 --> 00:58:49,988
在题库分析中，共享责任模型出现在 39 道题目中，这使其成为整个认证中最常被考查的概念。
The shared responsibility model appeared in 39 questions in the bank analysis, which makes it the single most tested concept in the whole certification.

749
00:58:51,118 --> 00:58:54,448
这也是大多数人认为自己已经掌握的内容。
It is also the one most people think they already know.

750
00:58:55,822 --> 00:58:59,300
这是所有其他内容都基于的基石句子。
Here is the sentence everything else hangs off.

751
00:59:00,014 --> 00:59:03,268
AWS 负责云本身的安全性。
AWS is responsible for security of the cloud.

752
00:59:03,854 --> 00:59:06,244
你负责云内部的安全性。
You are responsible for security in the cloud.

753
00:59:07,008 --> 00:59:14,724
「的」指的是运行一切的基础设施：建筑、硬件、网络和虚拟化层。
Of means the infrastructure that runs everything: buildings, hardware, networking, the virtualization layer.

754
00:59:15,566 --> 00:59:19,588
它意味着你放在上面的任何内容以及你如何配置它们。
It means whatever you put on top of it and how you configure it.

755
00:59:19,808 --> 00:59:27,812
大多数人都能理解这一点。但很少有人能在题目提到特定服务时正确应用这一原则，而这才是得分的关键。
Most people can decide this. Far fewer can apply it when the question names a specific service which is where the marks actually are.

756
00:59:29,262 --> 00:59:30,468
我们来详细看看这两个部分。
The two halves in detail.

757
00:59:31,278 --> 00:59:33,764
AWS 拥有基础设施本身。
AWS owns the infrastructure itself.

758
00:59:44,558 --> 00:59:46,928
你拥有你放在上面的所有内容。
You own everything you put on it.

759
00:59:47,470 --> 00:59:56,448
你的数据及其分类、身份和访问策略，以及在这些地方存在的操作系统和防火墙配置，
Your data and how it is classified, identity and access policies, operating system and firewall configuration where those exist,

760
00:59:56,718 --> 00:59:58,148
还有你的应用程序代码。
and your application code.

761
00:59:59,854 --> 01:00:01,028
这是一个实用的检查方法。
A useful check.

762
01:00:03,534 --> 01:00:09,444
你永远无法进入 AWS 数据中心，而且 AWS 也永远不会代你编写存储桶策略。
You can never inspect an AWS data center, and AWS can never write your bucket policy for you.

763
01:00:10,894 --> 01:00:14,596
有些事情无论你使用什么服务，始终由 AWS 负责。
Some things are always AWS, whatever service you use.

764
01:00:15,534 --> 01:00:22,084
数据中心的物理安全，包括保安、门禁卡、摄像头以及故障硬盘的销毁。
Physical security of data centers, including guards, badges, cameras, and the destruction of failed drives.

765
01:00:22,894 --> 01:00:26,692
硬件的维护和更换，因为你永远不会接触服务器。
Hardware maintenance and replacement because you never touch a server.

766
01:00:27,598 --> 01:00:31,012
连接各个区域和可用区的全球网络。
The global network connecting regions and availability zones.

767
01:00:31,918 --> 01:00:37,316
将客户彼此隔离的虚拟机管理程序和虚拟化层。
The hypervisor and virtualization layer that isolates customers from one another.

768
01:00:37,678 --> 01:00:41,540
以及区域和可用区本身的可用性。
And the availability of regions and availability zones themselves.

769
01:00:42,126 --> 01:00:43,620
这里有一个快速测试。
Here is a quick test.

770
01:00:44,078 --> 01:00:48,260
如果你在物理上无法从控制台中操作，那它就是 AWS 的责任。
If you physically could not do it from a console, it is AWS.

771
01:00:49,902 --> 01:00:51,844
而有些事情始终由你负责。
And some things are always yours.

772
01:00:52,142 --> 01:00:57,604
你的数据，意味着它的内容、敏感程度以及你允许它存储的位置。
Your data, meaning what it is, how sensitive it is, and where you allow it to live.

773
01:00:58,254 --> 01:00:59,428
谁有权访问它？
Who can access it?

774
01:00:59,758 --> 01:01:05,796
因为 IAM 用户、组、角色和策略始终由你负责。
Because I, AM users, groups, roles, and policies are always yours.

775
01:01:06,670 --> 01:01:10,528
是否开启了加密以及使用哪些密钥。
Whether encryption is switched on and which keys are used.

776
01:01:11,054 --> 01:01:14,084
客户端加密和数据完整性检查。
Client side encryption and data integrity checks.

777
01:01:14,368 --> 01:01:20,580
还有你的应用程序代码，包括其中存在的任何漏洞。其中最重要的一项是第一项。
And your application code, including any vulnerability in it. The most important of those is the first.

778
01:01:21,742 --> 01:01:28,528
客户始终对自己的数据负责，无论多么高度管理的服务，也不会改变这条底线。
The customer is always responsible for their data, and no service, however, managed moves that line.

779
01:01:29,728 --> 01:01:34,436
现在是区分能通过该领域考试的人和不能通过的人的关键点。
Now the part that separates people who pass domain to from people who do not.

780
01:01:34,768 --> 01:01:40,548
AWS 与你之间的界限并不是固定不变的，它会根据具体服务的不同而移动。
The line between AWS and you is not in a fixed place. It moves depending on the service.

781
01:01:40,928 --> 01:01:46,084
服务的托管程度越高，AWS承担的责任就越多，你承担的就越少。
The more managed the service, the more AWS takes on, and the less you are left holding.

782
01:01:46,768 --> 01:01:50,116
仅仅背诵这些内容无法回答这些问题。
Reciting of and in will not answer these questions.

783
01:01:50,368 --> 01:01:54,628
你必须知道特定服务的具体任务属于哪一方。
You have to know which side a specific task falls on for a specific service.

784
01:01:56,174 --> 01:01:58,750
这个表格就是这一页幻灯片的核心内容。
This table is the module in one slide.

785
01:01:59,566 --> 01:02:02,116
看右侧那一列，注意两点。
Look at the right hand column and notice two things.

786
01:02:02,510 --> 01:02:07,908
你的数据以及谁有权访问它，在每一行中都无一例外地出现。
Your data and who can access it appear in every single row without exception.

787
01:02:08,622 --> 01:02:12,452
但客户操作系统的补丁更新仅出现在 EC2 上。
But guest operating system patching appears only once on EC2.

788
01:02:13,038 --> 01:02:14,052
这就是规律。
That is the pattern.

789
01:02:15,190 --> 01:02:18,596
托管服务会把操作系统从你的手中拿走。
Managed services take the operating system away from you.

790
01:02:19,246 --> 01:02:23,236
但它们永远不会夺走你的数据或访问控制权。
They never take your data or your access control away from you.

791
01:02:23,886 --> 01:02:28,068
如果你从这个模块中记不住其他任何内容，也要记住向下阅读那一列。
If you remember nothing else from this module, remember reading down that column.

792
01:02:29,806 --> 01:02:40,612
这是考试中最常出现的对比点。在 EC2 上，AWS 负责补丁更新你实例下方的虚拟机管理程序，而你负责维护上层的操作系统。
This is the comparison the exam returns to most often. On EC2, AWS patches the hypervisor beneath your instance and you patch the operating system on top of it.

793
01:02:40,800 --> 01:02:44,132
如果你自己安装了数据库，你也需要负责它的补丁更新。
If you installed a database yourself, you patch that too.

794
01:02:44,494 --> 01:02:49,924
在 RDS 上，AWS 同时负责操作系统和数据库引擎的补丁更新。
On RDS, AWS patches both the operating system and the database engine.

795
01:02:50,638 --> 01:02:56,356
你保留对数据库用户、网络访问以及数据是否加密的控制权。
You keep control of database users, network access, and whether the data is encrypted.

796
01:02:57,358 --> 01:03:01,700
客户操作系统的补丁更新是考试中最明确的区分指标。
Guest operating system patching is the single clearest indicator on this exam.

797
01:03:02,222 --> 01:03:04,228
在 EC2 上，这是你的责任。
On EC2, it is yours.

798
01:03:04,782 --> 01:03:06,628
在 RDS 上，不是你的责任。
On RDS, it is not.

799
01:03:08,110 --> 01:03:13,828
EC2 和 Lambda 是范围的两端，因此对比它们可以展示界限变动的幅度。
EC2 and Lambda are the two ends of the range, so comparing them shows how far the line can travel.

800
01:03:14,862 --> 01:03:22,404
在 EC2 上，你负责操作系统补丁、加固、运行时、扩展配置和网络规则。
On EC2, you hold the operating system patching, hardening, the runtime, scaling configuration, and network rules.

801
01:03:23,278 --> 01:03:26,320
在 Lambda 上，没有供你操作的操作系统。
On Lambda, there is no operating system for you to touch.

802
01:03:26,670 --> 01:03:31,460
AWS 负责补丁更新语言运行时，并完全处理扩缩容。
AWS patches the language runtime and AWS handles scaling entirely.

803
01:03:32,814 --> 01:03:37,988
剩下的只有你的函数代码、你授予的权限以及你的数据。
What is left to you is your function code, the permissions you granted and your data.

804
01:03:38,862 --> 01:03:41,764
无服务器并不意味着让你不承担任何责任。
Serverless does not make you responsible for nothing.

805
01:03:43,600 --> 01:03:48,708
AWS 将三种控制项列为共享，且题目会直接询问这些内容。
AWS names three controls as shared and questions ask about them directly.

806
01:03:49,200 --> 01:03:56,196
补丁管理：AWS 负责基础设施的补丁，你负责客户操作系统和应用程序的补丁。
Patch management, where AWS patches the infrastructure and you patch your guest operating system and applications.

807
01:03:57,070 --> 01:04:04,612
配置管理：AWS 配置其基础设施设备，而你配置自己的资源。
Configuration management where AWS configures its infrastructure devices and you configure your own resources.

808
01:04:05,262 --> 01:04:10,180
以及意识与培训：AWS 培训其员工，而你培训你的员工。
And awareness and training where AWS trains its staff and you train yours.

809
01:04:10,894 --> 01:04:12,772
一个重要的澄清点。
One clarification that matters.

810
01:04:14,606 --> 01:04:17,348
“共享”并不意味着平分一半。
Shared does not mean split down the middle.

811
01:04:18,318 --> 01:04:23,300
这意味着双方都在各自负责的层级上执行相同的工作。
It means both parties do the same kind of work, each for the layer they own.

812
01:04:24,718 --> 01:04:28,356
加密是大家常争论的点，所以我们要表述准确。
Encryption is the row people argue about, so let us be precise.

813
01:04:29,294 --> 01:04:31,364
AWS 提供相关能力。
AWS provides the capability.

814
01:04:31,822 --> 01:04:37,508
包括 KMS、服务上的加密选项以及传输中数据的 TLS 端点。
KMS, encryption options on services, and TLS endpoints for data in transit.

815
01:04:38,574 --> 01:04:43,300
你决定是否使用它，因为启用静态加密是客户的操作。
You decide to use it because enabling encryption at rest is a customer action.

816
01:04:43,822 --> 01:04:48,388
这就是为什么静态加密通常被描述为共享责任。
That is exactly why encryption at rest is usually described as a shared responsibility.

817
01:04:48,720 --> 01:04:55,204
客户端加密完全由你负责，因为从定义上讲，AWS 无法代你完成。
Client side encryption is entirely yours because, by definition, AWS cannot do it for you.

818
01:04:55,758 --> 01:04:59,524
当你使用客户托管密钥时，密钥管理也由你负责。
And key management is yours when you use customer managed keys.

819
01:05:01,134 --> 01:05:04,400
把这一页当作练习来做，而不是单纯去阅读。
Use this slide as a drill rather than as reading.

820
01:05:04,782 --> 01:05:07,172
遮住右侧那一列，从上往下做。
Cover the right-hand column and work down.

821
01:05:07,822 --> 01:05:11,040
报废故障的磁盘驱动器是 AWS 的职责。
Destroying a failed disk drive is AWS.

822
01:05:11,982 --> 01:05:14,590
在 EC2 上修补操作系统是你自己的责任。
Patching an operating system on EC2 is you.

823
01:05:15,086 --> 01:05:18,400
在 RDS 上修补操作系统是 AWS 的责任。
Patching the operating system on RDS is AWS.

824
01:05:19,278 --> 01:05:21,732
配置存储桶策略是你自己的操作。
Configuring a bucket policy is you.

825
01:05:22,670 --> 01:05:25,840
确保可用区可用是 AWS 的职责。
Keeping an availability zone available is AWS.

826
01:05:26,222 --> 01:05:29,610
为根用户启用多重身份验证是你自己的操作。
Enabling multifactor authentication on the root user is you.

827
01:05:30,126 --> 01:05:32,772
对哪些数据属于敏感信息进行分类是你自己的责任。
Classifying which data is sensitive is U.

828
01:05:33,326 --> 01:05:37,280
将一个客户的实例与另一个客户隔离是 AWS 的职责。
And isolating one customer's instance from another's is AWS.

829
01:05:38,862 --> 01:05:42,160
这个领域中的干扰项通常呈现出四种可预测的形态。
This domain builds distractors in four predictable shapes.

830
01:05:42,478 --> 01:05:44,420
关于 RDS 服务的一个正确陈述。
A true statement about the RON service.

831
01:05:45,102 --> 01:05:49,412
「AWS 修补操作系统」对 RDS 是正确的，对 EC2 是错误的。
AWS patches the operating system is true for RDS and false for EC2.

832
01:05:50,510 --> 01:05:56,612
一些由 AWS 执行但被当作客户职责提供的项，以及频繁出现的物理安全问题。
Something AWS does, offered as a customer duty, and physical security appears constantly here.

833
01:05:57,518 --> 01:06:02,788
诸如「AWS 会自动保护所有客户数据」之类的绝对化表述。
An absolute such as AWS secures all customer data automatically.

834
01:06:03,438 --> 01:06:08,644
以及将“能力”与“行动”混淆，因为提供加密功能并不等同于应用加密。
And confusing capability with action because offering encryption is not the same as applying it.

835
01:06:09,198 --> 01:06:13,892
战胜这四种干扰项的习惯是：在阅读选项之前先确定服务类型。
The habit that beats all four is to name the service type before reading the options.

836
01:06:15,502 --> 01:06:16,516
实战场景。
Work scenario.

837
01:06:18,574 --> 01:06:19,044
1。
1.

838
01:06:19,950 --> 01:06:26,628
一家公司在应用负载均衡器后，在 Amazon EC2 实例上运行 Web 应用程序。
A company runs a web application on Amazon EC2 instances behind an application load balancer.

839
01:06:28,398 --> 01:06:33,892
安全审计发现操作系统缺失了三个月的安全更新。
A security audit finds the operating systems are missing three months of security updates.

840
01:06:34,800 --> 01:06:42,148
基础设施经理告诉审计员，作为共享责任模型的一部分，修补工作由 AWS 处理。
The infrastructure manager tells the auditor that patching is handled by AWS as part of the shared responsibility model.

841
01:06:42,640 --> 01:06:44,560
基础设施经理说的是对的吗？
Is the infrastructure manager correct?

842
01:06:44,846 --> 01:06:45,860
稍等一下，做决定。
Pause and decide.

843
01:06:51,950 --> 01:06:53,060
答案是 C。
The answer is C.

844
01:06:53,486 --> 01:07:03,908
仔细看选项 B，因为它是这里最强的干扰项，而且它用到了真实的技术。听起来很具体且专业，这会让它显得很有权威性。
Look at option B carefully because it is the best distractor here and it uses a real technique. It sounds specific and technical, which makes it feel authoritative.

845
01:07:04,814 --> 01:07:06,212
但它是个虚构的说法。
But it is an invention.

846
01:07:07,246 --> 01:07:10,948
Amazon Machine Image 在发布时就会进行补丁更新。
An Amazon machine image is patched at the point it is published.

847
01:07:11,470 --> 01:07:15,920
从你从中启动实例的那一刻起，操作系统就完全由你负责了。
From the moment you launch an instance from it, the operating system is entirely yours.

848
01:07:16,238 --> 01:07:20,388
警惕那些在错误答案中加入看似合理的限定词的选项。
Beware options that add a plausible sounding qualifier to a wrong answer.

849
01:07:20,654 --> 01:07:24,452
这些限定词通常是为了让错误的答案听起来更专业一些。
The qualifier is often there to make the wrong answer sound better informed.

850
01:07:26,062 --> 01:07:27,076
实战场景。
Work scenario.

851
01:07:36,560 --> 01:07:42,920
一家公司正将一个自管理的 Postgres 数据库从 EC2 迁移到 Amazon RDS。
A company is moving a self-managed Postgres database from EC2 to Amazon RDS.

852
01:07:43,982 --> 01:07:47,972
管理员询问她目前有哪些职责是继续保留的。
The administrator asks which of her current duties she keeps.

853
01:07:48,240 --> 01:07:55,940
她的职责包括：应用操作系统补丁、应用数据库引擎补丁，以及创建数据库用户。
Her duties are applying operating system patches, applying database engine patches, and creating database users.

854
01:07:56,654 --> 01:08:00,676
此外还包括决定存储是否加密以及更换故障磁盘。
Also deciding whether the storage is encrypted and replacing failed disks.

855
01:08:01,486 --> 01:08:03,556
迁移后哪两个职责仍由她负责？
Which two remain hers after the move?

856
01:08:05,358 --> 01:08:06,660
稍等一下，做决定。
Pause and decide.

857
01:08:12,686 --> 01:08:14,180
答案是 C 和 D。
The answers are C and D.

858
01:08:14,400 --> 01:08:18,212
这是服务表右侧列的直接应用。
This is the right hand column of the service table, applied directly.

859
01:08:18,720 --> 01:08:29,283
迁移到托管服务意味着移交操作系统和引擎，这正是 RDS 的核心目的。它永远不会移交谁可以访问数据或是否加密的决定权。
Moving to a managed service hands over the operating system and the engine, which is the whole point of RDS. It never hands over who can access the data or the decision to encrypt it.

860
01:08:29,774 --> 01:08:31,908
选项 E 值得思考一下。
Option E is worth the moment.

861
01:08:32,160 --> 01:08:38,340
这不是她在迁移中失去的东西，因为只要工作负载在 AWS 上，这本来就不是她的职责。
It is not something she loses in the move because it was never hers once the workload was on AWS at all.

862
01:08:38,800 --> 01:08:45,892
即使在 EC2 上，AWS 也会更换磁盘。把问题读作“哪些仍由她负责”，而 E 从一开始就不在选项范围内。
Even on EC2, AWS replaces the disks. Read the question as which remain hers, and E was never in the set.

863
01:08:47,278 --> 01:08:48,356
实战场景。
Worked scenario.

864
01:08:48,942 --> 01:08:57,091
3. 一名审计员要求公司演示保护运行 AWS 工作负载服务器的物理访问控制。
3. An auditor asks a company to demonstrate the physical access controls protecting the servers running its AWS workloads.

865
01:08:57,550 --> 01:09:04,452
审计员想安排参观数据中心。公司无法安排此类访问，必须用其他方式满足审计要求。
The auditor wants to schedule a data center visit. The company cannot arrange such a visit and must satisfy the auditor another way.

866
01:09:05,037 --> 01:09:06,020
它应该怎么做？
What should it do?

867
01:09:07,886 --> 01:09:10,180
a 通过 AWS 支持请求访问。
Request a visit through AWS support.

868
01:09:10,990 --> 01:09:15,200
b 提供来自 AWS artifact 的 AWS 合规性报告。
b provide AWS compliance reports from AWS artifact.

869
01:09:15,439 --> 01:09:15,680
C。
C.

870
01:09:16,046 --> 01:09:18,660
对实例运行 Amazon Inspector。
Run Amazon inspector against the instances.

871
01:09:19,182 --> 01:09:19,439
D.
D.

872
01:09:19,854 --> 01:09:22,160
启用 CloudRail 并提供日志。
Enable CloudRail and supply the logs.

873
01:09:22,542 --> 01:09:23,620
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

874
01:09:29,840 --> 01:09:31,359
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

875
01:09:31,920 --> 01:09:34,468
这个案例教给你的知识是可以反复套用的。
This scenario teaches something you will reuse.

876
01:09:35,200 --> 01:09:40,399
当审计员询问 AWS 模型中属于他们负责的那部分时，你无法亲自去检查。
When an auditor asks about AWS's half of the model, you cannot inspect it yourself.

877
01:09:40,590 --> 01:09:43,680
所以你要用 AWS 自带的审计报告来提供证据。
So you evidence it with AWS's own audit reports.

878
01:09:43,886 --> 01:09:46,160
这些报告就在 AWS artifact 中。
Those live in AWS artifact.

879
01:09:46,765 --> 01:09:53,124
选项 C 和 D 都是真实存在的安全服务，但它们关注的都是你负责的那部分模型。
Options C and D are both real security services doing real work, but both look at your half of the model.

880
01:09:53,774 --> 01:09:57,988
Inspector 检查你的工作负载，而 CloudRail 检查你的 API 活动。
Inspector examines your workloads and CloudRail examines your API activity.

881
01:09:58,702 --> 01:10:02,340
由于你运行的东西无法进入数据中心，所以这两个服务都无法看到内部情况。
Neither can see inside a data center because nothing you run can.

882
01:10:04,078 --> 01:10:06,052
案例 4 搞定了。
Worked scenario 4.

883
01:10:06,606 --> 01:10:14,480
一家公司运行三个工作负载：在 EC2 上运行的传统应用程序，在 Lambda 上运行的图像处理功能，
A company runs three workloads a legacy application on EC2, an image processing function on Lambda,

884
01:10:14,720 --> 01:10:17,380
以及保存在 Amazon S3 中的客户记录。
and its customer records in Amazon S3.

885
01:10:18,286 --> 01:10:26,800
一项新政策要求，支持这些工作负载的操作系统中的所有软件漏洞必须在 7 天内修复。
A new policy requires that all software vulnerabilities in the operating systems supporting these workloads are patched within 7 days.

886
01:10:27,120 --> 01:10:31,012
这项政策会给哪项工作负载带来额外的工作？
For which workload does this policy create work for the company?

887
01:10:31,758 --> 01:10:32,868
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

888
01:10:39,086 --> 01:10:40,260
答案是 A。
The answer is A.

889
01:10:40,704 --> 01:10:47,172
这个案例特意把三个服务放在一起，是因为同样的政策在不同服务上产生的后果不同。
This scenario puts three services side by side deliberately because the same policy lands differently on each.

890
01:10:47,584 --> 01:10:52,420
EC2 暴露了客户操作系统，所以这项政策会产生实际的工作量。
EC2 exposes a guest operating system, so the policy creates real work.

891
01:10:52,784 --> 01:10:57,348
Lambda 没有你可以接触到的操作系统，所以 AWS 已经帮你处理好了。
Lambda has no operating system you can reach, so AWS already does this.

892
01:10:57,966 --> 01:11:03,492
S3 完全没有暴露的操作系统。注意这道题到底在考什么。
S3 has no operating system exposed at all. Note what the question is really testing.

893
01:11:03,744 --> 01:11:10,596
不是在考修复是否重要，而是考你是否知道同样的具体要求，在不同服务下会产生不同的义务。
Not whether patching matters, but whether you know that the same requirement produces different obligations depending on the service.

894
01:11:11,886 --> 01:11:13,252
这就是整个模块的核心。
That is the whole module.

895
01:11:14,926 --> 01:11:23,620
总结一下，AWS 负责保障云基础设施的安全，而你负责保护放入其中的内容，但这个框架只是切入点，而不是解题关键。
To recap, AWS secures the cloud and you secure what you put in it, but that framing is the starting point rather than the answer.

896
01:11:23,984 --> 01:11:28,356
区分的关键在于服务类型，所以在阅读选项之前，先确定服务的类型。
The line moves by service, so name the service type before you read the options.

897
01:11:29,966 --> 01:11:34,624
在任何服务中，你的数据以及谁有权访问它，都是由你负责的，没有例外。
Your data and who can access it are yours on every service without exception.

898
01:11:35,150 --> 01:11:44,004
客户操作系统的修复在 EC2 上由你负责，而在托管服务上由 AWS 负责，这一条规则决定了大量的题目。
Guest operating system patching is yours on EC2 and AWS's on the managed services, and that single row decides a great many questions.

899
01:11:45,038 --> 01:11:49,284
下一个模块：Identity and Access Management。
Next module Identity and Access Management.

900
01:11:50,702 --> 01:11:54,864
Identity and Access Management 是最大领域中最大的单一主题。
Identity and Access Management is the largest single topic in the largest domain.

901
01:11:55,054 --> 01:12:00,612
在题库分析中，它出现的题目数量远超其他任何服务。
It appeared in 92 questions in the bank analysis more than any other service by a wide margin.

902
01:12:02,158 --> 01:12:04,164
好消息是相关概念很少。
The good news is that the concepts are few.

903
01:12:05,038 --> 01:12:09,892
难点在于考试会非常精确地区分这些概念。
The difficulty is that the exam separates them with precision.

904
01:12:10,222 --> 01:12:13,188
所以模糊的理解没法应付考试。
So vague understanding does not survive on tact.

905
01:12:14,638 --> 01:12:18,084
这个模块中的每个问题都可以简化成一句话。
Every question in this module reduces to one sentence.

906
01:12:23,182 --> 01:12:24,388
谁是身份？
Who is an identity?

907
01:12:24,704 --> 01:12:25,892
什么是操作？
What is an action?

908
01:12:26,286 --> 01:12:28,292
哪个资源是被操作的对象？
Which resource is the thing acted upon?

909
01:12:29,070 --> 01:12:32,804
条件是可选的约束条件，比如源地址或时间。
Conditions are optional constraints such as source address or time.

910
01:12:33,806 --> 01:12:39,332
当场景变得复杂时，把它归入这四个类别，答案通常就出来了。
When a scenario feels tangled, sort it into those four boxes and the answer usually falls out.

911
01:12:40,944 --> 01:12:43,396
四个对象，每个都有明确的功能。
Four objects and each has one job.

912
01:12:43,918 --> 01:12:49,892
用户是一个拥有长期凭证的单一身份，它可以是人或应用程序。
A user is a single identity with long-term credentials and it can be a person or an application.

913
01:12:50,670 --> 01:12:52,772
组是一群用户的集合。
A group is a collection of users.

914
01:12:53,486 --> 01:12:56,740
你可以给它关联策略，但你永远不会以群组身份登录。
You attach policies to it, but you never sign in as a group.

915
01:12:57,646 --> 01:13:02,788
角色是一个临时承担的身份，没有密码，也没有永久密钥。
A role is an identity that is assumed temporarily with no password and no permanent keys.

916
01:13:03,502 --> 01:13:08,228
而策略是一份文档，规定在哪些资源上允许或拒绝哪些操作。
And a policy is a document that says which actions are allowed or denied on which resources.

917
01:13:09,104 --> 01:13:11,236
用户和角色都是身份。
Users and roles are identities.

918
01:13:11,744 --> 01:13:14,180
组只是管理用户的一种方式。
Groups are just a way to manage users.

919
01:13:15,918 --> 01:13:18,212
这是考试最常考的区别。
This is the distinction the exam tests most.

920
01:13:18,544 --> 01:13:24,644
用户拥有长期凭证，即在更改前一直有效的密码或访问密钥。
A user has long-term credentials, a password or access keys that persist until you change them.

921
01:13:25,390 --> 01:13:33,188
角色按需发放临时凭证，这些凭证会过期，它可以被用户、应用程序或 AWS 服务承担。
A role issues temporary credentials on demand, which then expire and it can be assumed by users, applications, or AWS services.

922
01:13:34,062 --> 01:13:36,740
这是解决一系列相关问题的规则。
Here is the rule that answers a whole family of questions.

923
01:13:37,104 --> 01:13:46,116
如果一个应用程序或 AWS 服务需要权限，答案就是角色。在 EC2 实例上存储访问密钥永远是错误答案。
If an application or an AWS service needs permissions, the answer is a role. Storing access keys on an EC2 instance is always the wrong answer.

924
01:13:47,424 --> 01:13:52,996
根用户随账户创建，使用电子邮件地址而非用户名登录。
The root user is created with the account and signs in with the email address rather than a username.

925
01:13:53,504 --> 01:13:58,628
它拥有完全无限制的权限，IAM 策略无法限制它。
It has complete unrestricted access and IAM policies cannot restrict it.

926
01:13:59,024 --> 01:14:04,964
这就是为什么建议是为日常工作创建一个管理员用户，并让根用户退出。
That is precisely why the guidance is to create an administrative user for daily work and log the root user away.

927
01:14:05,870 --> 01:14:11,108
删除任何根访问密钥，因为没有任何正当理由让根用户持有这些密钥。
Delete any root access keys because there is no legitimate reason for the root user to have them.

928
01:14:12,110 --> 01:14:15,204
只有一小部分任务仍需要用到根用户。
A small set of tasks still require the root user.

929
01:14:15,630 --> 01:14:17,956
而那些正是考试会考到的内容。
And those are what the exam asks about.

930
01:14:19,504 --> 01:14:21,348
这些是值得掌握的内容。
Here are the ones worth knowing.

931
01:14:22,030 --> 01:14:25,636
更改账户名称、电子邮件地址或根密码。
Changing the account name, email address or root password.

932
01:14:26,224 --> 01:14:28,516
更改或取消支持计划。
Changing or cancelling the support plan.

933
01:14:28,944 --> 01:14:30,276
关闭账户。
Closing the account.

934
01:14:30,944 --> 01:14:36,036
当管理员将所有人锁在外面时，恢复 IAM 用户权限。
Restoring IAM user permissions when an administrator has locked everyone out.

935
01:14:36,864 --> 01:14:39,812
在 S3 存储桶上启用 MFA 删除。
Enabling MFA delete on an S3 bucket.

936
01:14:40,718 --> 01:14:44,452
以及在预留实例市场注册为卖家。
And registering as a seller in the reserved instance marketplace.

937
01:14:44,910 --> 01:14:47,844
与其死记硬背列表，不如掌握其逻辑结构。
Rather than memorizing the list, learn the shape.

938
01:14:48,590 --> 01:14:52,516
这些都是账户层面的操作，而不是资源层面的。
These are all account level actions, not resource level ones.

939
01:14:52,782 --> 01:14:56,004
任何涉及更改账户本身的操作都需要根权限。
Anything that changes the account itself needs root.

940
01:14:57,710 --> 01:15:01,348
多重身份验证在密码基础上增加第二个因素。
Multifactor authentication adds a second factor to the password.

941
01:15:01,838 --> 01:15:05,796
可以是虚拟身份验证器应用、硬件令牌或通行密钥。
A virtual authenticator app, a hardware token, or a pass key.

942
01:15:06,542 --> 01:15:13,700
AWS 支持 FIDO2 通行密钥和安全密钥，它们比一次性代码更能抵御网络钓鱼。
AWS supports FIDO2 passkeys and security keys which resist phishing better than one time codes.

943
01:15:14,990 --> 01:15:16,228
现在有一点诚实的提示
Now an honest note

944
01:15:17,070 --> 01:15:22,500
几乎所有的学习资料都将根账户的 MFA 描述为你应该遵循的最佳实践。
Almost all study material describes root MFA as a best practice you should follow.

945
01:15:23,118 --> 01:15:28,548
从 2025 年 6 月起，所有类型的账户的根用户都强制要求启用它。
Since June 2025, it is enforced for root users on every account type.

946
01:15:30,254 --> 01:15:35,236
考试答案没有改变，因为启用它仍然是你应该做的操作。
The exam answer has not changed because enabling it is still exactly what you should do.

947
01:15:36,878 --> 01:15:39,364
策略可以存在于两个位置之一。
A policy can live in one of two places.

948
01:15:39,920 --> 01:15:46,500
基于身份的策略附加到用户、组或角色上，规定该身份可以做什么。
An identity-based policy is attached to a user, group, or role and says what that identity may do.

949
01:15:47,150 --> 01:15:48,452
这是最常见的情况。
That is the common case.

950
01:15:48,942 --> 01:15:56,580
基于资源的策略附加到资源本身（例如 S3 存储桶），并明确指定委托人。
A resource-based policy is attached to the resource itself, such as an S3 bucket, and it names the principal explicitly.

951
01:15:57,518 --> 01:16:04,068
因为它指明了委托人，所以它可以授予另一个账户访问权限，而无需该账户切换角色。
Because it names the principal, it can grant access to another account without that account assuming a role.

952
01:16:04,974 --> 01:16:08,068
区别仅仅在于该策略是附加到什么的。
The separator is simply what the policy is attached to.

953
01:16:09,806 --> 01:16:11,940
有三种类型的基于身份的策略。
Three types of identity-based policy.

954
01:16:12,480 --> 01:16:19,748
AWS 管理策略由 AWS 创建和维护，例如只读访问权限和管理员访问权限。
AWS managed policies are created and maintained by AWS, such as read-only access and administrator access.

955
01:16:20,880 --> 01:16:28,292
客户管理策略是你编写的，可以在多个身份和版本之间重复使用，以便你可以回滚。
Customer managed policies are ones you write, reusable across many identities and versions so you can roll back.

956
01:16:29,200 --> 01:16:37,028
内联策略嵌入在单个身份中，严格的一对一关系，并且当该身份被删除时它们也会被删除。
Inline policies are embedded in a single identity, strictly one-to-one, and they are deleted when that identity is deleted.

957
01:16:39,630 --> 01:16:48,068
考试会专门考查内联政策，提示词是“仅适用于一个特定用户且不适用于其他任何内容的策略”。
The exam tests inline specifically and the giveaway phrase is a policy that applies to one particular user and nothing else.

958
01:16:49,326 --> 01:16:53,316
策略评估遵循固定的顺序，题目取决于这个逻辑。
Policy evaluation follows a fixed order and questions depend on it.

959
01:16:53,582 --> 01:16:57,188
每个请求最初都是被拒绝的，因为没有任何内容是默认允许的。
Every request starts denied because nothing is permitted implicitly.

960
01:16:57,360 --> 01:17:01,604
任何附加策略中的适用允许项都会将结果变为允许。
An applicable allow in any attached policy changes the result to allowed.

961
01:17:01,920 --> 01:17:04,964
然后，任何地方的显式拒绝都会覆盖所有的允许。
Then any explicit deny anywhere overrides every allow.

962
01:17:05,870 --> 01:17:09,840
所以，只有在被允许且没有被拒绝的情况下，请求才会成功。
So a request succeeds only if something allowed it and nothing denied it.

963
01:17:10,080 --> 01:17:14,084
要记住的规则是：显式拒绝永远优先。
The rule to carry away is that explicit deny always wins.

964
01:17:15,054 --> 01:17:17,636
增加另一个允许项永远无法覆盖拒绝。
Adding another allow can never override a deny.

965
01:17:19,054 --> 01:17:24,772
最小权限原则意味着只授予执行任务所需的权限，不多也不少。
Least privilege means granting only the permissions required to perform a task and nothing more.

966
01:17:25,120 --> 01:17:35,812
从最低权限开始并逐步增加，而不是从管理员权限开始再裁剪。使用组，让权限跟随工作职能而非个人。
Start from the minimum and add rather than starting from administrator access and trimming. Use groups so permissions follow a job function rather than an individual.

967
01:17:36,782 --> 01:17:41,796
并且定期审查权限，因为人员变动岗位后可能会保留旧有的访问权限。
And review permissions periodically because people change roles and keep their old access.

968
01:17:42,510 --> 01:17:45,060
对于考试来说，这提供了一个可靠的判定标准。
For the exam, this gives you a reliable tiebreaker.

969
01:17:45,520 --> 01:17:50,628
当两个选项都可行且其中一个授予的权限更少时，授予较少的那个就是正确答案。
When two options both work and one grants less, the one granting less is correct.

970
01:17:52,142 --> 01:17:57,380
基础 IAM 管理单个 AWS 账号内的身份。
Plain IAM manages identity inside one AWS account.

971
01:17:57,920 --> 01:18:06,852
IAM Identity Center 让用户在多个账号中只需登录一次，并连接现有的企业目录或身份提供商。
IAM Identity Center gives people one sign-in across many accounts and connects an existing corporate directory or identity provider.

972
01:18:07,120 --> 01:18:13,956
它以前被称为 AWS single sign on，旧的资料仍在使用那个名称。所以两个都要认出来。
It used to be called AWS single sign on and older material still uses that name. So recognize both.

973
01:18:14,830 --> 01:18:17,156
区分点在于账号的数量。
The separator is the number of accounts.

974
01:18:17,934 --> 01:18:20,480
一个账号意味着 IAM。
One account means IAM.

975
01:18:21,070 --> 01:18:24,960
多个账号或现有的企业目录意味着 IAM
Many accounts or an existing corporate directory means I

976
01:18:25,806 --> 01:18:27,652
Identity Center。
AM identity center.

977
01:18:29,390 --> 01:18:32,132
这一对选项可以筛选出那些熟悉这两个服务的考生。
This pair catches people who know both services well.

978
01:18:32,560 --> 01:18:35,760
IAM 是给使用 AWS 的人员用的。
IAM is for people who use AWS.

979
01:18:36,320 --> 01:18:42,000
登录控制台或调用 API 的员工、管理员和工程师。
Employees, administrators, and engineers signing into the console or calling the API.

980
01:18:43,566 --> 01:18:46,372
Cognito 是给使用你们应用程序的人用的。
Cognito is for people who use your application.

981
01:18:47,246 --> 01:18:53,636
注册并登录到你的应用或网站的客户，可能通过社交或企业身份提供商进行登录。
Customers signing up and signing in to your app or website, possibly through a social or enterprise identity provider.

982
01:18:54,000 --> 01:18:58,480
区分点是他们是谁。如果是你的客户，就选 Cognito。
The separator is whose users they are. Your customers means Cognito.

983
01:18:59,054 --> 01:19:01,732
在 AWS 内部工作的员工，就是 IAM。
Your staff working inside AWS means IA.

984
01:19:02,606 --> 01:19:03,083
。
AM.

985
01:19:05,038 --> 01:19:13,440
联合身份验证允许用户使用他们已有的身份来访问 AWS，而不是被分配一个新的 IAM
Federation lets people use an identity they already have to access AWS rather than being given a new IAAM

986
01:19:13,680 --> 01:19:13,956
用户。
user.

987
01:19:15,118 --> 01:19:21,040
企业目录保持为单一事实来源，因此入职和离职都在一个地方处理。
The corporate directory stays the source of truth, so joiners and leavers are handled in one place.

988
01:19:21,998 --> 01:19:27,780
AWS Directory Service 在 AWS 内部提供托管的 Microsoft Active Directory。
AWS Directory Service provides managed Microsoft Active Directory inside AWS.

989
01:19:28,686 --> 01:19:34,884
联合身份验证用户承担一个角色，这就是为什么他们获得的是临时凭证而不是密码。
Federated users assume a role, which is why they receive temporary credentials rather than a password.

990
01:19:36,014 --> 01:19:41,860
考试中的信号是：公司拥有现有的本地部署目录，并且不想进行重复建设。
The exam signal is a company with an existing on-premises directory that it does not want to duplicate.

991
01:19:47,790 --> 01:19:53,444
外部访问发现可以告诉你哪些资源与外部账户或公众共享。
External access findings tell you which resources are shared with an outside account or with the public.

992
01:19:54,190 --> 01:20:00,868
未使用访问发现可以告诉你哪些角色、访问密钥、密码和权限实际上没人使用过。
Unused access findings tell you which roles, access keys, passwords, and permissions nobody has actually used.

993
01:20:01,774 --> 01:20:09,444
第二个功能是组织如何随着时间的推移来执行最小权限原则，而不仅仅是在授予权限的那一刻。
That second capability is how organizations enforce least privilege over time rather than just at the moment of granting.

994
01:20:10,062 --> 01:20:13,220
它还可以根据观察到的 CloudTrail 活动生成策略。
It can also generate a policy from observed cloud trail activity.

995
01:20:13,760 --> 01:20:16,804
它分析的是权限，而不是检测威胁。
It analyzes permissions, it does not detect threats.

996
01:20:18,382 --> 01:20:19,684
一些实用的规则。
Some practical rules.

997
01:20:20,142 --> 01:20:26,244
访问密钥用于程序化访问，而密码是用于控制台的，两者不能互换。
Access keys are for programmatic access and a password is for the console and they are not interchangeable.

998
01:20:26,958 --> 01:20:30,564
定期轮换访问密钥，并删除没人使用的密钥。
Rotate access keys regularly and delete ones nobody uses.

999
01:20:30,862 --> 01:20:35,780
永远不要在代码、机器镜像或公共仓库中嵌入访问密钥。
Never embed access keys in code in a machine image or in a public repository.

1000
01:20:36,270 --> 01:20:43,108
密码策略为 IAM 用户设置最小长度、复杂度、过期和重复使用规则。
A password policy sets minimum length, complexity, expiry, and reuse rules for IAM users.

1001
01:20:43,408 --> 01:20:49,476
并且只要可能就优先选择角色，因为这样就没有需要轮换的东西，也不会泄露。
And prefer rows wherever a role is possible because then there is nothing to rotate and nothing to leak.

1002
01:20:50,734 --> 01:20:51,972
工作场景 1。
Work scenario 1.

1003
01:20:52,590 --> 01:20:57,444
一个运行在 Amazon EC2 实例上的应用程序需要读取 S3 存储桶中的对象。
An application on an Amazon EC2 instance needs to read objects from an S3 bucket.

1004
01:20:58,158 --> 01:21:06,084
一名开发人员为该应用创建了一个 IAM 用户，生成了访问密钥，并将它们写入到实例上的配置文件中。
A developer created an IAM user for the application, generated access keys, and wrote them into a configuration file on the instance.

1005
01:21:06,958 --> 01:21:11,888
安全审查将此标记为一种反模式。公司应该怎么做？
A security review flags this as an anti-pattern. What should the company do instead?

1006
01:21:12,128 --> 01:21:14,528
A. 每 30 天轮换一次密钥。
a rotate the keys every 30 days.

1007
01:21:14,768 --> 01:21:23,808
B. 给实例关联一个 IAM 角色。C. 加密配置文件。D. 将密钥放入环境变量中。
B. Attach an IAM role to the instance. C. Encrypt the configuration file. D. Move the keys into an environment variable.

1008
01:21:23,982 --> 01:21:25,092
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1009
01:21:31,086 --> 01:21:32,368
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

1010
01:21:32,942 --> 01:21:35,908
注意这个题目的结构，因为它有干扰项。
Notice the structure of this question because it clickers.

1011
01:21:36,590 --> 01:21:40,292
四个选项中有三个接受了这种缺陷设计，并试图更好地管理它。
Three of the four options accept the flaw design and try to manage it better.

1012
01:21:40,814 --> 01:21:44,548
轮换密钥、加密它们、把它们藏在环境变量里。
Rotate the keys, encrypt them, hide them in an environment variable.

1013
01:21:44,910 --> 01:21:47,236
只有一个选项能完全消除这个缺陷。
Only one option removes the flaw entirely.

1014
01:21:47,950 --> 01:21:55,012
当你看到三个选项是缓解问题，而只有一个是消除问题时，考试几乎总是要求选择那个消除问题的。
When you see three options that mitigate and one that eliminates, the exam almost always wants the one that eliminates.

1015
01:21:55,694 --> 01:21:57,988
而底层的规则就是我们之前提到的那条。
And the underlying rule is the one from earlier.

1016
01:21:58,990 --> 01:22:01,403
需要权限的 AWS 服务应该使用角色。
An AWS service needing permissions is a role.

1017
01:22:03,118 --> 01:22:04,260
工作场景。
Work scenario.

1018
01:22:04,622 --> 01:22:08,740
2. 一家公司需要一组仅适用于一个特定对象的权限集。
2. A company needs a permission set that applies to exactly one.

1019
01:22:09,518 --> 01:22:11,044
IAM 用户。
IAM user.

1020
01:22:12,622 --> 01:22:23,888
该用户是一名具有特殊访问要求的承包商。其他人都没有，也不会有。安全团队要求如果该用户被删除，相关权限也要自动移除。
The user is a contractor with unusual access requirements. Nobody else has or will have. The security team wants the permissions removed automatically if that user is ever deleted.

1021
01:22:24,494 --> 01:22:26,372
哪种策略类型符合这些要求？
Which policy type meets this?

1022
01:22:26,928 --> 01:22:29,668
A. 一个 AWS 托管策略。
A an AWS managed policy.

1023
01:22:30,350 --> 01:22:33,060
B. 一个客户托管策略。
B a customer managed policy.

1024
01:22:33,934 --> 01:22:35,812
C. 一个内联策略。
C. An inline policy.

1025
01:22:36,688 --> 01:22:37,008
D.
D.

1026
01:22:37,486 --> 01:22:38,980
一个基于资源的策略。
A resource-based policy.

1027
01:22:39,534 --> 01:22:40,676
停下来思考一下并做出决定。
Pause and decide.

1028
01:22:46,862 --> 01:22:48,208
答案是 C。
The answer is C.

1029
01:22:48,782 --> 01:22:54,048
这道题设计得很巧妙，因为选项 B 虽然符合第一个要求。
This question is carefully built because option B would work for the first requirement.

1030
01:22:54,382 --> 01:23:00,516
客户托管策略可以表达你想要的任何权限，并且你可以把它绑定到仅一个用户上。
A customer managed policy can express any permissions you like and you could attach it to just one user.

1031
01:23:01,390 --> 01:23:03,652
但第二句话就把它排除掉了。
What kills it is the second sentence.

1032
01:23:04,462 --> 01:23:11,556
客户托管策略在关联的用户被删除后依然存在，会留下一个孤立的策略。
A customer managed policy survives the deletion of the user it was attached to, leaving an orphaned policy behind.

1033
01:23:12,048 --> 01:23:14,852
内联策略会随身份信息一起被删除。
Inline policies are deleted with their identity.

1034
01:23:15,534 --> 01:23:20,324
两个要求都必须满足，而只有一个选项能同时满足两者。
Both requirements have to be satisfied, and only one option satisfies both.

1035
01:23:26,382 --> 01:23:31,620
一个用户属于一个允许所有 Amazon S3 操作的组策略。
A user belongs to a group whose policy allows all Amazon S3 actions.

1036
01:23:31,888 --> 01:23:38,596
该用户还有一个内联策略，显式拒绝在特定桶中删除对象。
The user also has an inline policy explicitly denying object deletion in one particular bucket.

1037
01:23:39,310 --> 01:23:46,308
然后管理员为了快速解决工单，直接给该用户添加了管理员权限。
An administrator then attaches administrator access directly to the user, hoping to resolve a ticket quickly.

1038
01:23:47,406 --> 01:23:50,180
现在用户能删除那个桶里的对象吗？
Can the user now delete objects in that bucket?

1039
01:23:51,118 --> 01:23:52,356
停下来思考一下并做出决定。
Pause and decide.

1040
01:23:58,510 --> 01:23:59,684
答案是 C。
The answer is C.

1041
01:24:00,878 --> 01:24:09,092
这个场景是为了消除人们从其他系统中带来的直觉，即更宽泛的权限或更新的设置会生效。
This scenario exists to kill an intuition people bring from other systems where a broader permission or a more recent setting wins.

1042
01:24:12,462 --> 01:24:15,236
但在 IAM 中，这两者都不成立。
In IAM, neither is true.

1043
01:24:15,664 --> 01:24:20,304
无论范围如何，显式拒绝在任何策略中都始终优先。
Explicit deny always wins from any policy regardless of breadth.

1044
01:24:20,544 --> 01:24:23,876
添加管理员权限仍然只是一个允许操作。
Attaching administrator access is still only an allow.

1045
01:24:24,686 --> 01:24:28,452
而且选项 D 值得注意，因为它听起来很高级。
And option D is worth noticing because it sounds sophisticated.

1046
01:24:29,198 --> 01:24:31,108
评估并不是按时间顺序进行的。
Evaluation is not chronological.

1047
01:24:31,344 --> 01:24:34,436
在 AAM 中没有“最后生效”的规则。
There is no last one wins rule in AAM.

1048
01:24:36,142 --> 01:24:37,508
案例 4。
Worked scenario 4.

1049
01:24:37,824 --> 01:24:44,388
一个拥有 400 名员工的工程公司已经在本地运行 Microsoft Active Directory。
An engineering form of 400 staff already runs Microsoft Active Directory on premises.

1050
01:24:44,704 --> 01:24:48,644
他们正在开设 12 个 AWS 账户，每个项目团队对应一个。
It is opening 12 AWS accounts, one per project team.

1051
01:24:48,944 --> 01:24:54,852
员工应使用现有的公司凭证登录他们有权访问的任何账户。
Staff should sign in to whichever accounts they are entitled to using their existing corporate credentials.

1052
01:24:55,758 --> 01:25:00,388
身份团队不想在每个账户中创建或维护独立的凭证。
The identity team does not want to create or maintain separate credentials in each account.

1053
01:25:00,974 --> 01:25:03,184
哪个服务符合这些要求？
Which service meets these requirements?

1054
01:25:03,534 --> 01:25:04,836
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1055
01:25:10,734 --> 01:25:11,904
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

1056
01:25:12,494 --> 01:25:18,308
题干中的三个独立信号都指向同一个方向，即 12 个账户而不是一个。
Three separate signals in the STEM all point the same way, 12 accounts rather than one.

1057
01:25:19,214 --> 01:25:21,284
现有的公司目录。
An existing corporate directory.

1058
01:25:21,966 --> 01:25:29,344
以及明确拒绝重复创建凭证。其中任何一点都会提示选择 IAM Identity Center。
And an explicit refusal to duplicate credentials. Any one of those would suggest IAM identity center.

1059
01:25:29,504 --> 01:25:31,652
这些信息结合起来，答案就非常明确了。
Together they make it unambiguous.

1060
01:25:32,622 --> 01:25:36,388
选项 C 是本模块前面提到的「群体陷阱」。
Option C is the population trap from earlier in the module.

1061
01:25:37,806 --> 01:25:40,868
Cognito 处理的是你应用程序的终端用户。
Cognito handles your applications end users.

1062
01:25:41,742 --> 01:25:48,676
这 400 人是登录 AWS 本身的员工，属于完全不同的群体。
These 400 people are staff signing into AWS itself, which is a different population entirely.

1063
01:25:50,446 --> 01:25:51,844
案例 5。
Worked scenario 5.

1064
01:25:52,494 --> 01:25:55,492
安全团队被审计人员提出了两个问题。
A security team is asked two questions by an auditor.

1065
01:25:55,744 --> 01:26:01,700
第一，是否有任何 S3 存储桶或 IAM 角色可以从组织外部访问？
First, are any S3 buckets or I AM roles accessible from outside the organization?

1066
01:26:02,224 --> 01:26:07,584
第二，哪些 IAM 角色和访问密钥在过去 90 天内未被使用过？
Second, which I AM roles and access keys have not been used in the last 90 days.

1067
01:26:07,744 --> 01:26:10,532
团队想要一个能同时回答这两个问题的单一服务。
The team wants a single service that answers both.

1068
01:26:11,118 --> 01:26:13,024
A Amazon Card Duty。
A Amazon Card Duty.

1069
01:26:13,264 --> 01:26:15,184
B AWS Cloud Plane。
B AWS Cloud Plane.

1070
01:26:15,424 --> 01:26:17,824
C IAM Access Analyzer。
C IAM Access Analyzer.

1071
01:26:18,144 --> 01:26:18,304
D。
D.

1072
01:26:18,798 --> 01:26:20,464
AWS Trusted Advisor。
AWS Trusted Advisor.

1073
01:26:20,624 --> 01:26:21,860
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1074
01:26:27,982 --> 01:26:29,264
答案是 C。
The answer is C.

1075
01:26:29,584 --> 01:26:37,188
审计员的两个问题正好对应 Access Analyzer 的两项功能，这就是为什么一个服务可以涵盖这两个问题。
The auditor's two questions map exactly onto Access Analyzer's two capabilities, which is why one service can cover both.

1076
01:26:39,342 --> 01:26:43,300
外部访问发现可以回答是否有任何内容可以从外部到达。
External access findings answer whether anything is reachable from outside.

1077
01:26:43,918 --> 01:26:47,524
未使用的访问发现可以说明哪些角色和密钥没有人使用过。
Unused access findings answer which roles and keys nobody has used.

1078
01:26:48,238 --> 01:26:49,744
选项 B 需要特别说明一下。
Option B deserves a note.

1079
01:26:49,984 --> 01:26:56,068
CloudTrail 虽然持有第二个问题的原始证据，但你必须自己去分析 90 天的日志。
Cloud Trail does hold the raw evidence for the second question, but you would have to analyze 90 days of logs yourself.

1080
01:26:56,590 --> 01:26:59,424
Access Analyzer 已经帮你完成了这项分析。
Access analyzer already does that analysis.

1081
01:26:59,664 --> 01:27:02,436
优先选择为该问题设计的服务。
Prefer the service designed for the question.

1082
01:27:03,694 --> 01:27:08,356
总结一下，将每个问题分类为：谁、做什么以及使用哪个资源。
To recap, sort every question into who, what and which resource.

1083
01:27:09,070 --> 01:27:13,584
需要权限的应用程序或 AWS 服务始终是关键路径。
An application or AWS service needing permissions is always a road.

1084
01:27:13,774 --> 01:27:15,780
绝不要在实例上直接使用访问密钥。
Never access keys on an instance.

1085
01:27:16,304 --> 01:27:21,092
明确的拒绝（deny）总是优先于任何数量的允许。
Explicit DINI always wins and no amount of additional allow over exit.

1086
01:27:21,966 --> 01:27:28,644
内联意味着仅有一个身份，且随之删除；而客户管理的则是可重复使用的并持久存在的。
Inline means exactly one identity and deleted with it while customer managed is reusable and persists.

1087
01:27:29,262 --> 01:27:37,796
多个账户或企业目录对应 IAM Identity Center，而应用程序的客户则对应 Cognito。
Many accounts or a corporate directory means IAM identity center while your application's customers means cognito.

1088
01:27:38,926 --> 01:27:41,860
进入下一个模块：检测与威胁服务。
Next module, the detection and threat services.

1089
01:27:43,182 --> 01:27:49,060
这五个服务在考试中作为选项同时出现的频率，比任何其他组合都要高。
These five services appear together as options more often than any other group on the exam.

1090
01:27:49,678 --> 01:27:56,548
在数据分析中，Shield 和 Guard Duty 同时出现 24 次，Guard Duty 和 Inspector 出现 19 次。
In the bank analysis, Shield and Guard Duty co occurred 24 times Guard Duty and Inspector 19.

1091
01:27:57,344 --> 01:28:01,508
这不是因为它们功能相似，而是因为它们听起来好像功能相似。
That is not because they do similar things, it is because they sound as though they might.

1092
01:28:03,150 --> 01:28:08,036
从这个模块中能解决最多问题的核心点开始。
Start with the thing that resolves more questions in this module than any service detail.

1093
01:28:08,398 --> 01:28:11,108
这里的服务都是用于检测的，都不是用来保护的。
Everything here detects, nothing here protects.

1094
01:28:11,470 --> 01:28:21,060
Guard Duty 会告诉你实例正在挖掘加密货币，但它不会停止该实例；Inspector 会告诉你软件有漏洞，但它不会进行修补。
Guard duty will tell you an instance is mining cryptocurrency, it will not stop the instance. Inspector will tell you software is vulnerable, it will not patch it.

1095
01:28:21,744 --> 01:28:27,652
当问题询问如何拦截、过滤或阻止某些内容时，这五个服务都不是正确答案。
When a question asks how to block, filter or prevent something, none of these five is the answer.

1096
01:28:28,144 --> 01:28:30,180
保护功能在下一个模块中。
Protection lives in the next module.

1097
01:28:31,758 --> 01:28:36,356
五个服务对应五个关键词。Guard Duty 监控行为以应对活跃威胁。
Five services and five nouns. Guard duty watches behavior for active threats.

1098
01:28:36,544 --> 01:28:42,704
Inspector 扫描工作负载中的软件漏洞。Macie 用于查找 Amazon S3 中的敏感数据。
Inspector scans workloads for software vulnerabilities. Macy finds sensitive data inside Amazon S3.

1099
01:28:43,104 --> 01:28:45,828
Detective 在发现项出现后进行调查。
Detective investigates a finding after it appears.

1100
01:28:46,544 --> 01:28:57,604
Security Hub 则汇总发现结果，并根据安全标准检查您的账户。行为、漏洞、数据、调查、聚合。
And Security Hub aggregates findings and checks your account against security standards. Behavior, vulnerabilities, data, investigation, aggregation.

1101
01:28:57,984 --> 01:29:04,100
如果你能将正确的规范对应到正确的服务上，这个模块中的大多数问题都会变得简单明了。
If you can attach the right norm to the right service, most questions in this module become straightforward.

1102
01:29:05,582 --> 01:29:08,704
Guard Duty 和 Inspector 是最常被混淆的一对。
Guard Duty and Inspector are the pair most often swapped.

1103
01:29:09,070 --> 01:29:18,372
Guard Duty 持续读取日志和网络活动，寻找异常的 API 调用、加密货币挖掘或来自异常地点的凭证使用。
Guard duty reads logs and network activity continuously, looking for unusual API calls, crypto mining, or credentials being used from somewhere improbable.

1104
01:29:19,470 --> 01:29:21,156
它能发现正在进行的攻击。
It finds an attack in progress.

1105
01:29:22,062 --> 01:29:31,844
Inspector 扫描 EC2 实例、容器镜像和 Lambda 函数，查找已知的软件漏洞和意外的网络暴露。
Inspector scans EC2 instances, container images, and lambda functions for known software vulnerabilities and unintended network exposure.

1106
01:29:32,144 --> 01:29:38,464
它在有人利用之前发现弱点。正在进行的攻击意味着 Guard Duty。
It finds weaknesses before anyone has used them. Attack in progress means guard duty.

1107
01:29:38,784 --> 01:29:41,220
潜在的弱点意味着 Inspector。
Latent weakness means inspector.

1108
01:29:42,894 --> 01:29:45,124
Guard Duty 读取您现有的日志。
Guard duty reads LOBs you already have.

1109
01:29:45,614 --> 01:29:52,356
涵盖云平面、VPC、流日志和 域名系统 日志，无需您单独启用。
Cloud plane, VPC, flow logs, and DNS logs without needing you to enable them separately.

1110
01:29:52,814 --> 01:29:59,844
无需安装、无需代理且不改变您的工作负载，这就是为什么题目经常将其与“极低成本/最少操作”的要求结合在一起。
There is nothing to install, no agent and no change to your workloads, which is why questions often pair it with a requirement for minimal effort.

1111
01:30:00,558 --> 01:30:08,804
典型的发现包括挖矿、来自异常位置的凭证使用、侦查以及与已知恶意地址的通信。
Typical findings are crypto mining, credential use from an unusual location, reconnaissance and communication with known bad addresses.

1112
01:30:09,184 --> 01:30:14,308
「异常的 API 调用」这个短语是识别 Guard Duty 最常见的线索。
The phrase unusual API calls is the single most common giveaway for guard duty.

1113
01:30:15,886 --> 01:30:23,364
Inspector 会扫描 Amazon EC2 实例，查找未修复的操作系统和应用程序漏洞。
Inspector scans three things Amazon EC2 instances for unpatched operating system and application vulnerabilities.

1114
01:30:25,998 --> 01:30:32,324
在 Amazon EC 中推送时会扫描容器镜像，并在发布新漏洞时重新扫描。
Container images in Amazon EC are scanned when pushed and rescanned as new vulnerabilities are published.

1115
01:30:33,454 --> 01:30:36,612
以及包含其代码和依赖项的 Lambda 函数。
And Lambda functions including their code and dependencies.

1116
01:30:37,454 --> 01:30:42,052
它会自动发现符合条件的负载，而不是等待被指派目标。
It discovers eligible workloads automatically rather than waiting to be pointed at them.

1117
01:30:43,726 --> 01:30:46,116
它还会报告意外的网络暴露。
It also reports unintended network exposure.

1118
01:30:46,574 --> 01:30:52,676
如果题目提到漏洞、补丁或 通用漏洞披露，那么答案就是 Inspector。
If a question mentions vulnerabilities, patching or CVEs, the answer is inspector.

1119
01:30:54,478 --> 01:30:59,556
Macie 是这个群体中的异类，知道原因后就很容易区分了。
Macy is the odd one out in this group, and knowing why makes it easy.

1120
01:31:00,046 --> 01:31:03,584
Macie 是这里唯一会打开你数据的服务。
Macy is the only service here that opens your data.

1121
01:31:03,744 --> 01:31:12,144
它利用机器学习和模式匹配来扫描 Amazon S3，以查找个人身份信息和其他敏感内容，
It uses machine learning and pattern matching over Amazon S3 to find personally identifiable information and other sensitive content,

1122
01:31:12,304 --> 01:31:13,668
然后对其进行分类。
then classifies it.

1123
01:31:14,382 --> 01:31:18,784
Guard duty 从不查看你的对象内部，只查看它们周围的行为。
Guard duty never looks inside your objects, only at behavior around them.

1124
01:31:18,944 --> 01:31:27,053
所以如果出现敏感数据、个人身份信息或 S3 内容这些词，答案就是 Macie。
So if the words sensitive data, personally identifiable information, or S3 contents appear, the answer is Mackie.

1125
01:31:28,590 --> 01:31:34,244
Detective 是大家最难定位的一个，因为它听起来像个检测服务，但其实不是。
Detective is the one people struggle to place because it sounds like a detection service and is not.

1126
01:31:34,704 --> 01:31:39,844
Guard duty 会主动产生发现结果，并告诉你发生了某些可疑情况。
Guard duty produces findings on its own and tells you something suspicious happened.

1127
01:31:40,384 --> 01:31:46,980
Detective 则消费这些发现，并构建相关活动的关联视图，以便你找出根本原因和范围。
Detective consumes findings and builds a linked view of related activity so you can work out root cause and scope.

1128
01:31:47,184 --> 01:31:49,956
只有在某些东西已经触发警报时，你才会打开 Detective。
You open detective because something has already fired.

1129
01:31:50,702 --> 01:31:52,324
清晰的区分点是这个：
The clean separator is this.

1130
01:31:52,910 --> 01:31:55,364
Detective 从不主动告诉你有什么问题。
Detective never tells you that something is wrong.

1131
01:31:56,206 --> 01:32:00,036
它是在其他服务已经提醒你之后，才告诉你原因。
It tells you why after something else already did.

1132
01:32:01,358 --> 01:32:03,780
Security Hub 是聚合层。
Security Hub is the aggregation layer.

1133
01:32:03,984 --> 01:32:12,304
它将来自 Guard Duty、Inspector、Macie、IAM、Access Analyzer、Firewall Manager 以及合作伙伴工具的发现结果
It collects findings from Guard Duty, Inspector, Messi, IAM, Access Analyzer, Firewall Manager, and Partner Tools

1134
01:32:12,464 --> 01:32:13,412
汇总到一个地方。
into one place.

1135
01:32:13,824 --> 01:32:17,860
它还会根据指定的标准运行自动的最佳实践检查。
It also runs automated best practice checks against named standards.

1136
01:32:18,624 --> 01:32:26,692
包括 CIS、PCI DSS、SOC 以及 AWS Foundational Security Best Practices。
CIS, PCID, SS, and the AWS Foundational Security Best Practices.

1137
01:32:29,326 --> 01:32:34,084
它跨多个账户和区域工作，这通常是题目选择它的原因。
It works across many accounts and regions, which is usually why a question reaches for it.

1138
01:32:35,054 --> 01:32:37,764
但「聚合」并不总是正确的答案。
But aggregation is not automatically the right answer.

1139
01:32:38,144 --> 01:32:41,732
只有当要求是提供单一中心视图时，它才是正确选项。
It is correct only when the requirement is a single center view.

1140
01:32:43,086 --> 01:32:47,332
一个可能会在你打开控制台的一瞬间就把你搞混的可用性警告。
An availability warning that will confuse you the moment you open the console.

1141
01:32:47,664 --> 01:32:59,140
在2025年6月的更新中，AWS 将原来的 Security Hub 重命名为 AWS Security Hub CSPM，用于云安全态势管理。
At reinforce in June 2025, AWS renamed the original Security Hub. It is now AWS Security Hub CSPM for Cloud Security Posture Management.

1142
01:32:59,904 --> 01:33:13,344
随后一个全新的服务采用了 AWS Security Hub 这个名称，并于2025年12月2日正式发布。考试考查的是旧版本。在考试中，请回答 security 枢纽。
A different and genuinely new service then took the name AWS Security Hub, reaching general availability on the 2nd of December 2025. The exam means the old one. On the exam answer security hub.

1143
01:33:15,086 --> 01:33:17,508
在控制台中，你可能会看到 CSPM。
In the console, expect to see CSPM.

1144
01:33:18,958 --> 01:33:24,228
这是反向查询，而且考试几乎逐字重复这些词汇。
Here is the reverse lookup and the exam reuses this vocabulary almost word for word.

1145
01:33:24,864 --> 01:33:26,532
unusual IP。
Unusual AP.

1146
01:33:27,104 --> 01:33:31,108
异常调用或被盗用的凭证意味着 GuardDuty。
I calls or compromised credentials means guard duty.

1147
01:33:32,078 --> 01:33:37,284
未打补丁的软件、漏洞或容器镜像意味着 Inspector。
Unpatched software, vulnerabilities or container images means inspector.

1148
01:33:38,224 --> 01:33:43,780
S3 中的个人身份信息或敏感数据意味着 Macie。
Personally identifiable information or sensitive data in S3 means messy.

1149
01:33:44,718 --> 01:33:48,544
调查现有发现的根本原因意味着 Detective。
Investigating the root cause of an existing finding means detective.

1150
01:33:49,326 --> 01:34:00,164
跨多个账户的统一视图意味着 Security Hub，而外部共享的资源或未使用的权限则对应前一模块中的 IAM Access Analyzer。
One view across many accounts means security hub, and resources shared externally or unused permissions means IAM access analyzer from the previous module.

1151
01:34:01,518 --> 01:34:05,316
把这些看作一个整体，而不是五个独立的框，对理解很有帮助。
It helps to see how these fit together rather than as five separate boxes.

1152
01:34:05,742 --> 01:34:10,052
某些东西进行检测，因此 GuardDuty、Inspector 或 Macie 会产生一个“发现”。
Something detects, so guard duty, inspector or messy produces a finding.

1153
01:34:10,574 --> 01:34:14,756
Security Hub 将来自每个源的“发现”收集到一个地方并统一格式。
Security Hub collects findings from every source into one place and one format.

1154
01:34:15,886 --> 01:34:19,556
EventBridge 将“发现”转化为可以触发某些操作的事件。
Event bridge turns a finding into an event that can trigger something.

1155
01:34:20,398 --> 01:34:26,724
然后你通过通知团队、运行 Lambda 函数或打开 Detective 来进行调查。
And then you respond by notifying a team, running a lambda function, or opening detective to investigate.

1156
01:34:27,310 --> 01:34:29,572
仅有检测本身不会改变任何东西。
Detection on its own changes nothing.

1157
01:34:30,062 --> 01:34:32,708
价值在于将“发现”路由到相应的响应中。
The value is in routing a finding to a response.

1158
01:34:34,350 --> 01:34:37,988
这一页内容在整个模块中比其他任何内容都更重要。
This slide is what more marks than any other in the module.

1159
01:34:38,510 --> 01:34:40,004
检测服务负责告知你情况。
Detection services tell you.

1160
01:34:53,262 --> 01:34:59,204
在关于拦截攻击的问题中回答 GuardDuty 是一个常见且代价高昂的错误。
Answering guard duty to a question about blocking an attack is a common and expensive mistake.

1161
01:35:00,078 --> 01:35:02,212
可靠的习惯是去读动词。
The reliable habit is to read the verb.

1162
01:35:03,413 --> 01:35:07,173
识别、发现、查明和警报意味着“检测”；
Identify, find, discover, and alert mean detection;

1163
01:35:07,173 --> 01:35:11,940
阻断、过滤、预防和限制意味着“保护”。
Block, filter, prevent, and restrict mean protection.

1164
01:35:13,742 --> 01:35:23,780
实战案例1：一家公司的监控显示，一个 EC2 实例正在与一个与加密货币挖矿相关的地址建立出站连接。
Worked Scenario 1: A company's monitoring shows an EC2 instance making outbound connections to an address associated with cryptocurrency mining.

1165
01:35:24,750 --> 01:35:30,404
此外，还有一个 IAM 访问密钥正被用于一个该公司没有员工的国家。
An IAM access key is also being used from a country where the company has no staff.

1166
01:35:31,344 --> 01:35:37,984
团队想要一个能在无需在实例上安装任何内容的情况下自动识别出这两点的服务。
The team wants a service that would have identified both automatically with nothing to install on the instances.

1167
01:35:38,510 --> 01:35:45,988
A. Inspector B. Macie C. GuardDuty D. Config，停下来思考一下。
A inspector B Mac key C Guard Duty D AWS config pause and decide.

1168
01:35:52,014 --> 01:35:59,613
答案是 C。这两个症状都是行为而非漏洞，因此可以立即排除 Inspector。
The answer is C. Both symptoms are behaviors rather than weaknesses, which rules out inspector immediately.

1169
01:36:00,224 --> 01:36:04,068
两者都不涉及数据内容，所以排除了 Macie。
Neither involves data content, which rules out macchi.

1170
01:36:06,190 --> 01:36:12,292
而且“无需安装”这个短语在这里起到了关键作用，因为 GuardDuty 在设计上就是无代理的。
And the phrase nothing to install is doing deliberate work here because guard duty is agentless by design.

1171
01:36:13,294 --> 01:36:17,892
这个短语出现的频率足够高，可以作为独立的一个提示点。
That phrase appears often enough to treat as a hint in its own right.

1172
01:36:18,224 --> 01:36:26,244
如果一个问题在强调检测威胁的同时，强调不需要代理且不改变工作负载，那么 GuardDuty 几乎总是预设的答案。
If a question emphasizes no agents and no changes to workloads alongside threat detection, guard duty is almost always an intended answer.

1173
01:36:27,822 --> 01:36:29,252
实战场景。
Worked scenario.

1174
01:36:29,934 --> 01:36:34,864
2. 一家医疗公司在 Amazon S3 中存储了数百万个对象。
2. A healthcare company stores several million objects in Amazon S3.

1175
01:36:35,344 --> 01:36:44,164
它必须识别哪些存储桶包含带有个人身份信息的患者记录，并对其进行分类以满足监管要求。
It must identify which buckets contain patient records with personally identifiable information and classify them to satisfy a regulator.

1176
01:36:44,814 --> 01:36:48,304
目前它不知道哪些存储桶包含受监管的数据。
It does not currently know which buckets hold regulated data.

1177
01:36:48,784 --> 01:36:50,704
它应该使用哪个服务？
Which service should it use?

1178
01:36:51,024 --> 01:36:52,388
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1179
01:36:58,320 --> 01:37:06,404
答案是 B，个人身份信息加上 S3 是 Macie 的标志性特征，把这两个词成对学习很有价值。
The answer is B personally identifiable information plus S3 is the makey signature and it is worth learning as a pair.

1180
01:37:09,070 --> 01:37:11,556
选项 C 是个有意思的选项。
Option C is the interesting one.

1181
01:37:11,840 --> 01:37:20,240
Security Hub 是一个真正有用的服务，这家公司可能也应该运行它，但它聚合的是其他服务产生的结果。
Security Hub is a genuinely useful service, and this company should probably run it, but it aggregates findings that other services produce.

1182
01:37:20,654 --> 01:37:26,244
如果 Macie 没有开启，Security Hub 就无法汇总任何关于敏感数据的信息。
If Messi is not switched on, Security Hub has nothing to aggregate about sensitive data.

1183
01:37:26,510 --> 01:37:32,036
聚合层依赖于下层的架构，因此它们很少是用于“发现”类问题的答案。
Aggregation layers depend on the layers beneath them, so they are rarely the answer to a discovery question.

1184
01:37:33,614 --> 01:37:34,724
实战场景 3。
Work scenario 3.

1185
01:37:35,150 --> 01:37:45,380
一家公司运行着一个公共 Web 应用程序。其安全团队收到警报，称该应用程序正受到 SQL 注入探测，并希望阻止这些请求到达应用程序。
A company runs a public web application. Its security team receives an alert that the application is being probed for SQL injection and wants to stop those requests reaching the application.

1186
01:37:46,030 --> 01:37:53,060
另外，团队希望在未来任何 AWS 凭证从异常位置使用时收到提醒。
Separately, the team wants to be alerted in future when any AWS credential is used from an unexpected location.

1187
01:37:53,840 --> 01:37:56,164
哪两个服务符合这些要求？
Which two services meet these requirements?

1188
01:37:56,960 --> 01:37:58,244
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1189
01:38:04,080 --> 01:38:06,340
答案是 A 和 B。
The answers are A and B.

1190
01:38:06,800 --> 01:38:13,636
这个场景旨在直接测试“检测”与“保护”的区别，因为它在同一个问题中包含了这两类中的各一个服务。
This scenario is built to test the detection and protection split directly because it puts one of each in the same question.

1191
01:38:14,160 --> 01:38:19,360
「阻止这些请求到达应用程序」是一个保护类的动词。所以是 WAF。
Stop those requests reaching the application is a protection verb. So WAF.

1192
01:38:20,142 --> 01:38:26,160
「当凭证从异常位置使用时收到提醒」是一个检测类的动词。
Be alerted when a credential is used from an unexpected location is a detection verb.

1193
01:38:26,320 --> 01:38:27,620
所以是 GuardDuty。
So guard duty.

1194
01:38:28,942 --> 01:38:34,724
五个选项中有三个是检测服务，而其中只有一个符合第二个要求。
Three of the five options are detection services and only one of those matches the second requirement.

1195
01:38:35,598 --> 01:38:38,916
如果先读动词，可以在几秒钟内缩小范围。
Reading the verbs first would have narrowed this in seconds.

1196
01:38:40,686 --> 01:38:41,796
实战场景。
Worked scenario.

1197
01:38:42,414 --> 01:38:42,916
4。
4.

1198
01:38:43,694 --> 01:38:51,172
GuardDuty 的一项发现报告称，一个 EC2 实例一直在与一个已知的命令和控制地址通信。
A guard duty finding reports that an EC2 instance has been communicating with a known command and control address.

1199
01:38:51,758 --> 01:39:00,548
团队需要确定该实例是如何被连接的、使用了哪些凭证、是否触及了其他资源，以及持续了多长时间。
The team needs to establish how the instance was reached, which credentials were used, whether other resources were touched, and over what period.

1200
01:39:01,390 --> 01:39:06,212
他们想要一个能从现有日志数据中拼凑出这一全貌的服务。
They want a service that assembles this picture from existing log data.

1201
01:39:08,334 --> 01:39:09,508
停下来做决定。
Pause and decide.

1202
01:39:15,726 --> 01:39:16,900
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

1203
01:39:17,360 --> 01:39:19,920
这个问题的结构才是关键所在。
The structure of this question is the important part.

1204
01:39:20,718 --> 01:39:24,356
发现已经存在，所以检测任务已经完成了。
The finding already exists, so the detection job is finished.

1205
01:39:24,720 --> 01:39:27,588
之后要求的所有内容都是关于理解的。
Everything asked for after that is about understanding.

1206
01:39:28,206 --> 01:39:29,360
它是如何被访问的？
How was it reached?

1207
01:39:29,710 --> 01:39:30,800
使用了哪些凭证？
Which credentials?

1208
01:39:31,214 --> 01:39:32,484
还有什么被触碰了？
What else was touched?

1209
01:39:32,880 --> 01:39:33,956
持续了多长时间？
Over what period?

1210
01:39:34,926 --> 01:39:39,360
这就是范围和根本原因，也就是检测的全部目的。
That is scope and root cause, which is detect's entire purpose.

1211
01:39:39,662 --> 01:39:45,444
一旦问题从“发生了什么”转变为“为什么发生”，你就从检测进入到了调查阶段。
Once a question moves from what happened to why it happened, you have crossed from detection into investigation.

1212
01:39:46,894 --> 01:39:48,004
实战案例
Worked scenario

1213
01:39:48,910 --> 01:39:56,708
5. 一个组织运行 40 个 AWS 账户，每个账户都启用了 GuardDuty、Inspector 和 Macie。
5. An organization runs 40 AWS accounts, each with guard duty, inspector, and Macy enabled.

1214
01:39:58,160 --> 01:40:02,788
安全团队通过依次登录每个账户来审查发现结果。
The security team reviews findings by signing in to each account in turn.

1215
01:40:03,680 --> 01:40:10,468
他们想要一个包含所有发现的统一视图，并希望根据 CIS 基准来衡量资产状况。
They want one view of all findings and want to measure the estate against the CIS benchmark.

1216
01:40:11,310 --> 01:40:13,668
哪个服务能同时满足这两个要求？
Which service meets both requirements?

1217
01:40:13,998 --> 01:40:15,332
停下来做决定。
Pause and decide.

1218
01:40:21,134 --> 01:40:27,780
答案是 C。请刻意将其与场景 2 进行对比，在那个场景中 Security Hub 是错误答案。
The answer is C. Compare this deliberately with scenario 2, where Security Hub was the wrong answer.

1219
01:40:28,270 --> 01:40:32,932
在那里，还没有任何东西产生结果，所以聚合就没有东西可供聚合。
There, nothing was producing findings yet, so aggregation had nothing to aggregate.

1220
01:40:33,806 --> 01:40:41,156
在这里，三个检测服务已经在 40 个账户中运行，问题纯粹是没人能把它们整合在一起看。
Here, three detection services are already running across 40 accounts, and the problem is purely that nobody can see them together.

1221
01:40:41,646 --> 01:40:43,844
这正是选择“聚合”的正确时机。
That is exactly when aggregation is right.

1222
01:40:44,590 --> 01:40:53,508
第二个要求证实了这一点，因为根据 CIS 等特定基准进行衡量是 Security Hub 的标准检查。
The second requirement confirms it because measuring against a named benchmark like CIS is a security hub standards check.

1223
01:40:55,246 --> 01:40:59,716
总结一下，本模块中的所有内容都是检测，而不是保护。
To recap, everything in this module detects and nothing protects.

1224
01:40:59,920 --> 01:41:01,988
所以要读题中的动词。
So read the verb in the question.

1225
01:41:02,734 --> 01:41:08,164
行为异常是 GuardDuty，漏洞是 Inspector，数据内容则是 Macie。
Behavior is guard duty, vulnerabilities are inspector, and data content is messy.

1226
01:41:08,878 --> 01:41:13,732
检测类服务解释的是已经存在的发现，且本身不会主动发出警报。
Detective explains a finding that already exists and never raises one itself.

1227
01:41:14,606 --> 01:41:23,876
当要求是跨账户的统一视图或特定的标准时，Security Hub 是正确的；而当还没有任何结果产生时，它就是错误的。
Security Hub is right when the requirement is one view across accounts or a named standard, and wrong when nothing is producing findings yet.

1228
01:41:26,446 --> 01:41:31,044
下一个模块：保护类服务、加密和密钥。
Next module: the protection services plus encryption and secrets.

1229
01:41:32,654 --> 01:41:36,064
上一个模块涵盖了告诉你“出问题了”的服务。
The previous module covered services that tell you something is wrong.

1230
01:41:36,334 --> 01:41:43,024
这个模块涵盖的是阻止事情发生，以及让数据对任何获取到它的人都变得毫无用处的服务。
This one covers services that stop it happening and services that make data useless to anyone who does get hold of it.

1231
01:41:43,374 --> 01:41:47,684
内容分为两个部分，考试会在这两个部分中随机分布干扰项。
Two halves and the exam draws distractors freely across both.

1232
01:41:49,326 --> 01:41:52,100
第一部分的核心概念是“层”。
The organizing idea for the first half is layers.

1233
01:41:52,384 --> 01:41:55,812
流量洪泛攻击发生在网络层和传输层。
A volumetric flood arrives at the network and transport layers.

1234
01:41:56,144 --> 01:41:59,108
恶意请求发生在应用层。
A malicious request arrives at the application layer.

1235
01:41:59,630 --> 01:42:03,204
端口连接在实例或子网层面进行控制。
A connection to a port is controlled at the instance or subnet.

1236
01:42:04,910 --> 01:42:08,004
每一个场景都有唯一的 AWS 对应答案。
Each of those has exactly one AWS answer.

1237
01:42:08,864 --> 01:42:13,156
如果你能确定问题所在的层，就几乎能确定对应的服务了。
If you can name the layer the problem lives at, you have almost named the service.

1238
01:42:14,606 --> 01:42:18,948
有五种阻止流量的方法，其中有一种并非表面看起来的那样。
Five things that stop traffic, and one of them is not what it appears.

1239
01:42:19,310 --> 01:42:24,932
Shield 在网络层和传输层防止大规模的拒绝服务攻击。
Shield stops volumetric denial of service attacks at the network and transport layers.

1240
01:42:25,824 --> 01:42:31,268
WAF 在应用层拦截恶意 HTTP 请求。
WAF stops malicious, HTTP requests at the application layer.

1241
01:42:32,142 --> 01:42:36,384
安全组控制到达实例和网络的流量。
Security groups control traffic reaching an instance and network.

1242
01:42:36,704 --> 01:42:39,460
ACLs 控制进入子网的流量。
ACLs control traffic entering a subnet.

1243
01:42:39,984 --> 01:42:44,544
Firewall Manager 是个例外，因为它本身并不直接拦截任何内容。
Firewall manager is the odd one out because it stops nothing itself.

1244
01:42:44,784 --> 01:42:49,476
它是在多个账户中统一应用 WAF 和 Shield 规则。
It applies WAF and Shield rules consistently across many accounts.

1245
01:42:49,664 --> 01:42:50,980
它是一个管理层。
It is a management layer.

1246
01:42:52,654 --> 01:42:54,436
Shield 和 WAF。
Shield and WA.

1247
01:42:54,894 --> 01:43:01,892
如果两者都保护面向互联网的应用程序，且在相似的位置进行挂载，这就是它们作为选项时产生竞争的原因。
If both protect internet-facing applications and both attach in similar places, which is why they compete as options.

1248
01:43:02,734 --> 01:43:12,644
Shield 关注的是流量有多少。它吸收第 3 层和第 4 层的洪泛，并且从不读取请求内容。WAF 则关心流量的内容。
Shield cares about how much traffic arrives. It absorbs floods at layers 3 and 4 and never reads a request. WAF cares about what the traffic says.

1249
01:43:13,344 --> 01:43:21,796
它会读取每一个 HTTP 请求，并应用关于 SQL 注入、跨站脚本攻击、源地址或国家的规则。
It reads every HTTP request and applies rules about SQL injection, cross-site scripting, source address or country.

1250
01:43:22,384 --> 01:43:23,876
如果是洪泛攻击，就选 Shield。
Flooding means Shield.

1251
01:43:24,544 --> 01:43:27,424
如果涉及检查请求内容，就选 WAF。
Inspecting the request means WAF.

1252
01:43:29,166 --> 01:43:31,024
Shield 有两个层级。
Shield comes in two tiers.

1253
01:43:31,502 --> 01:43:38,756
标准版对所有 AWS 客户都是自动开启的，不花钱，无需配置，且无法关闭。
Standard is automatic for every AWS customer, costs nothing, needs no configuration, and cannot be switched off.

1254
01:43:39,104 --> 01:43:47,684
如果题目问什么能保护你免受常见的拒绝服务攻击，答案就是 Shield 标准版，而且你已经拥有它了。
If a question asks what protects you from common denial of service attacks today, the answer is Shield standard and you already have it.

1255
01:43:48,622 --> 01:43:53,572
高级版是每月 3000 美元的付费订阅，并包含一年的承诺。
Advanced is a paid subscription at $3,000 a month with a one-year commitment.

1256
01:43:54,094 --> 01:44:02,692
它包含了 Shield 响应团队的成本保护，用于在遭受攻击时进行扩容，并涵盖受保护资源上的标准 WAF 费用。
It adds the Shield Response Team cost protection for scaling during an attack and covers standard WAF costs on protected resources.

1257
01:44:03,598 --> 01:44:05,604
有一个容易让人掉坑里的细节。
One detail that catches people out.

1258
01:44:06,638 --> 01:44:11,844
联系 Shield 响应团队还需要具备商业或企业级支持。
Contacting the Shield Response Team also requires business or enterprise support.

1259
01:44:13,070 --> 01:44:16,356
在实际操作中，WAF 通过 Web 工作。
In practice, WAF works through a web.

1260
01:44:16,846 --> 01:44:22,276
ACL 持有规则，在请求到达你的应用之前允许拦截或计数。
ACL holding rules that allow block or count requests before they reach your application.

1261
01:44:23,214 --> 01:44:28,420
AWS 管理规则组涵盖了常见的威胁，而无需你亲自编写任何内容。
AWS managed rule groups cover common threads without you writing anything yourself.

1262
01:44:29,294 --> 01:44:36,164
基于速率的规则会拦截发送超过指定数量请求的地址，从而处理应用层的群发攻击。
Rate-based rules block an address sending more than a chosen number of requests, which handles group flooding at the application layer.

1263
01:44:36,782 --> 01:44:43,504
它可连接到 CloudFront、应用负载均衡器、API Gateway 和 AppSync。
It attaches to CloudFront, an application load balancer, API gateway, and app sync.

1264
01:44:45,326 --> 01:44:47,300
有一个值得注意的限制。
One limitation worth knowing.

1265
01:44:48,302 --> 01:44:53,092
它不能直接保护 EC2 实例，因为必须有东西挡在前面。
It cannot protect an EC2 instance directly because something must sit in front.

1266
01:44:54,464 --> 01:45:05,700
Firewall Manager 在组织中的每个账户中集中应用保护策略，新创建的账户和资源会自动继承这些规则。
Firewall manager applies protection policies centrally across every account in an organization and new accounts and resources inherit those rules automatically as they appear.

1267
01:45:06,286 --> 01:45:08,224
它管理 WAF、
It manages WAF,

1268
01:45:09,038 --> 01:45:14,628
Web ACLs、Shield Advanced 保护以及 Security Group Policies。
Web ACLs, Shield Advanced Protections and Security Group Policies.

1269
01:45:15,502 --> 01:45:20,356
它需要 AWS Organizations，所以它永远不是单账户的答案。
It requires AWS organizations, so it is never the answer for a single account.

1270
01:45:20,846 --> 01:45:26,436
还要注意，AWS Network Firewall 是不同的服务，不在考试范围列表中。
Note also that AWS Network Firewall is a different service and it is not on the in scope list.

1271
01:45:26,784 --> 01:45:29,572
旧的题库仍将其作为干扰项。
Older question banks still use it as a distractor.

1272
01:45:31,214 --> 01:45:37,764
现在进入本模块的第二部分，它有助于明确加密的具体用途。
Now, the second half of the module it helps to be precise about what encryption is for.

1273
01:45:38,670 --> 01:45:41,188
它并不能阻止任何人获取你的数据。
It does not prevent anyone getting to your data.

1274
01:45:41,710 --> 01:45:44,164
它让那些没拿到密钥的人拿到的数据变得毫无用处。
It makes what they get useless without the key.

1275
01:45:44,942 --> 01:45:53,636
这就是为什么加密相关的题目几乎从不涉及阻止访问，而是几乎总是关于谁持有密钥以及是否开启了加密。
That is why encryption questions are almost never about stopping access and almost always about who holds the key and whether it was switched on.

1276
01:45:55,344 --> 01:46:00,196
数据要么是静止的，要么是在移动的，这两者需要不同的机制。
Data is either sitting still or moving, and the two need different mechanisms.

1277
01:46:00,624 --> 01:46:09,508
静态加密涵盖 S3 对象、EBS 卷、RDS 存储和快照，这些密钥通常通过 KMS 管理。
Encryption at rest covers S3 objects, EBS volumes, RDS storage and snapshots with keys usually managed through KMS.

1278
01:46:10,094 --> 01:46:14,308
你选择启用它，它可以防止他人获取存储设备。
You choose to enable it and it protects against someone obtaining the storage.

1279
01:46:15,086 --> 01:46:23,044
传输中加密是指客户端与服务之间使用来自 AWS Certificate Manager 的证书进行的 TLS 连接
Encryption in transit means TLS between a client and a service using certificates from AWS Certificate Manager

1280
01:46:23,534 --> 01:46:25,572
并且它能防止被拦截。
and it protects against interception.

1281
01:46:26,318 --> 01:46:28,228
“至少”意味着 KMS。
At least means KMS.

1282
01:46:31,694 --> 01:46:34,064
“传输中”意味着证书。
In transit means certificates.

1283
01:46:38,990 --> 01:46:44,784
KMS 创建、存储并控制加密大多数 AWS 服务数据的密钥。
KMS creates, stores, and controls the keys that encrypt data across most AWS services.

1284
01:46:45,024 --> 01:46:52,196
密钥永远不会以未加密的状态离开 KMS，因此你调用 KMS 来进行加密和解密，而不是自己处理密钥材料。
Keys never leave KMS unencrypted, so you call KMS to encrypt and decrypt rather than handling key material yourself.

1285
01:46:52,944 --> 01:46:59,396
客户托管密钥是你创建并用自己的密钥策略和轮换设置来控制的密钥。
Customer managed keys are ones you create and control with your own key policy and rotation settings.

1286
01:46:59,824 --> 01:47:04,548
AWS 管理密钥是为每个服务自动创建的，不需要任何管理。
AWS managed keys are created for you per service and need no administration.

1287
01:47:05,024 --> 01:47:10,500
每一次密钥的使用都会记录在 CloudRail 中，这样你就可以审计谁解密了什么内容。
And every use of a key is recorded in CloudRail, which is how you audit who decrypted what.

1288
01:47:21,664 --> 01:47:26,500
AWS 负责操作硬件，并且它与大多数 AWS 服务集成。
AWS operates the hardware and it integrates with most AWS services.

1289
01:47:27,054 --> 01:47:29,924
除非题目另有说明，否则这就是正确答案。
It is the right answer unless the question tells you otherwise.

1290
01:47:30,766 --> 01:47:39,904
CloudHSM 为你提供单租户的硬件安全模块，只有你能访问，并经过 FIPS 140-2 认证。
CloudHSM gives you single tenant hardware security modules that only you can access, validated to FIPS 140-2

1291
01:47:40,064 --> 01:47:40,644
第 3 级。
level 3.

1292
01:47:41,104 --> 01:47:47,904
只有当场景明确要求仅由你控制的专用硬件监管要求时，才选择它。
Choose it only when the scenario names a regulatory requirement for dedicated hardware that you alone control.

1293
01:47:49,582 --> 01:47:57,504
AWS Certificate Manager 为 AWS 服务配置并管理 TLS 证书。
AWS Certificate Manager provisions and manages TLS certificates for AWS services.

1294
01:47:57,902 --> 01:48:05,572
在与 CloudFront 和 Elastic Load Balancing 等集成服务配合使用时，公有证书是免费的。
Public certificates are free when used with integrated services such as CloudFront and Elastic Load Balancing.

1295
01:48:06,062 --> 01:48:13,156
关键点在于它会自动续订，从而避免因证书悄悄过期而导致的传统停机问题。
Critically, it renews them automatically, which removes the classic outage caused by a certificate quietly expiring.

1296
01:48:14,990 --> 01:48:20,484
AWS Private CA 为内部使用颁发私有证书。
AWS Private CA issues private certificates for internal use.

1297
01:48:21,024 --> 01:48:24,452
记住，它只保护传输中数据。
And remember, it secures data in transit only.

1298
01:48:25,264 --> 01:48:28,452
它与加密静态数据无关。
It has nothing to do with encrypting data at rest.

1299
01:48:30,126 --> 01:48:34,820
这一对词只要出现，就意味着它是送分题。
This pair turns on one word, which makes it a gift when you spot it.

1300
01:48:36,718 --> 01:48:44,944
Secrets Manager 具有内置的自动轮换功能，包括针对 RDS、Redshift 和 Document
Secrets Manager has built in automatic rotation, including native rotation for RDS, Redshift, and Document

1301
01:48:45,184 --> 01:48:48,784
DB 的原生轮换，并且按每个机密每月计费。
DB, and it charges per secret per month.

1302
01:48:49,326 --> 01:48:58,564
Parameter Store 是 Systems Manager 的一部分，用于存储层级配置值，并可以使用 KMS 通过安全字符串类型对其进行加密。
Parameter Store, part of Systems Manager, stores hierarchical configuration values and can encrypt them with KMS using the secure string type.

1303
01:48:59,310 --> 01:49:03,556
它的标准层是免费的，且没有内置自动轮换功能。
Its standard tier is free and it has no built-in automatic rotation.

1304
01:49:04,302 --> 01:49:06,916
“自动轮换”意味着 机密管理器。
Automatic rotation means secrets manager.

1305
01:49:07,822 --> 01:49:12,036
“免费配置存储”意味着 parameter store。
Free configuration storage means parameter store.

1306
01:49:13,454 --> 01:49:15,744
这是整个模块的反向查找规律。
Here is the reverse lookup for the whole module.

1307
01:49:16,014 --> 01:49:18,144
流量洪峰意味着 Shield。
A flood of traffic means shield.

1308
01:49:19,214 --> 01:49:24,868
SQL 注入、跨站脚本攻击或屏蔽某个国家，意味着 WAF。
SQL injection, cross-site scripting, or blocking a country means WAF.

1309
01:49:25,422 --> 01:49:29,348
所有账户遵循相同的规则，意味着 Firewall Manager。
The same rules across every account means firewall manager.

1310
01:49:30,030 --> 01:49:33,892
加密存储的数据并审计密钥，意味着 KMS。
Encrypting stored data and auditing keys means KMS.

1311
01:49:34,830 --> 01:49:39,780
监管机构要求专用单租户硬件，意味着 CloudHSM。
A regulator demanding dedicated single tenant hardware means CloudHSM.

1312
01:49:40,334 --> 01:49:43,236
证书过期意味着 certificate manager。
Certificates expiring means certificate manager.

1313
01:49:43,824 --> 01:49:49,380
且必须自动轮换的数据库凭证，意味着 机密管理器。
And database credentials that must rotate automatically means secrets manager.

1314
01:49:51,054 --> 01:49:53,156
场景 1 处理成功。
Worked scenario 1.

1315
01:49:54,062 --> 01:49:58,372
零售商的公共网站位于应用负载均衡器之后。
A retailer's public website sits behind an application load balancer.

1316
01:49:59,246 --> 01:50:01,700
在促销期间，它变得无法访问。
During a sale, it becomes unreachable.

1317
01:50:02,318 --> 01:50:04,068
同时发生了两件事。
Two things are happening at once.

1318
01:50:04,974 --> 01:50:14,308
大量的无意义数据包占满了连接，以及另一组试图对结账表单进行 SQL 注入的请求。
A very large volume of meaningless packets saturating the connection and a separate set of requests attempting SQL injection against the checkout form.

1319
01:50:15,184 --> 01:50:18,724
公司询问它需要什么以及它已经拥有了什么。
The company asks what it needs and what it already has.

1320
01:50:20,014 --> 01:50:21,092
停下来思考一下再做决定。
Pause and decide.

1321
01:50:27,278 --> 01:50:29,024
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

1322
01:50:29,344 --> 01:50:33,412
两个层面的两个问题，所以任何一个服务单独都无法解决。
Two problems at two layers, so neither service alone covers it.

1323
01:50:33,710 --> 01:50:36,804
但注意那个额外的条款以及它已经拥有的东西。
But notice the extra clause and what it already has.

1324
01:50:37,166 --> 01:50:43,812
这是为了测试你是否知道 Shield 标准对所有 AWS 客户都是免费自动提供的。
That is there to test whether you know Shi standard is automatic for every AWS customer at no charge.

1325
01:50:44,334 --> 01:50:50,944
这里提到 Shield Advanced 的选项是错误的，因为场景中没有任何内容支持支付 3000 美元的订阅费。
Options mentioning Shield Advanced are wrong here because nothing in the scenario justifies a $3,000 subscription.

1326
01:50:51,104 --> 01:50:57,380
而选项 D 是从上一个模块中故意放进这个模块的「检测与保护」陷阱。
And option D is the detection and protection trap from the previous module sitting in this one deliberately.

1327
01:50:58,958 --> 01:51:00,196
处理场景 2。
Work scenario 2.

1328
01:51:00,464 --> 01:51:04,740
一家银行必须将加密密钥存储在其他组织无法共享的硬件中。
A bank must store encryption keys in hardware no other organization shares.

1329
01:51:05,134 --> 01:51:11,524
监管机构要求提供证据，证明在任何情况下 AWS 工作人员都无法访问密钥材料。
Its regulator requires proof that AWS staff cannot access the key material under any circumstances.

1330
01:51:12,046 --> 01:51:17,508
同一家银行的第二个团队只需要用他们可以审计的密钥来加密 EBS 卷。
A second team in the same bank simply needs to encrypt EBS volumes with keys it can audit.

1331
01:51:18,350 --> 01:51:20,868
哪两个服务符合这些要求？
Which two services meet these requirements?

1332
01:51:21,422 --> 01:51:22,724
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1333
01:51:28,782 --> 01:51:31,076
答案是 A 和 B。
The answers are A and B.

1334
01:51:31,374 --> 01:51:38,500
这个场景故意把两个关键服务放在同一个问题里，因为考试要求你进行选择而不是默认选择。
This scenario deliberately puts both key services in the same question because the exam wants you to choose rather than default.

1335
01:51:39,726 --> 01:51:45,700
监管机构要求的「AWS 工作人员无法访问密钥材料」这一措辞强制指向 Cloud HSM。
The regulator's wording that AWS staff cannot access the key material forces Cloud HSM.

1336
01:51:46,670 --> 01:51:51,812
只有在你专属控制下的单租户硬件才能满足这个要求。
Single tenant hardware under your exclusive control is the only thing that satisfies it.

1337
01:51:52,064 --> 01:51:59,332
第二个团队的需求很普通，没有这类约束条件，KMS 可以配合完整的 CloudRail 审计来处理。
The second team has an ordinary need with no such constraint and KMS handles it with full CloudRail auditing.

1338
01:51:59,904 --> 01:52:04,704
如果没有明确的监管原因，KMS 总是更好的答案。
Without a stated regulatory reason, KMS is always the better answer.

1339
01:52:06,094 --> 01:52:07,588
处理场景 3。
Worked scenario 3.

1340
01:52:08,206 --> 01:52:12,452
一个应用程序从配置文件中读取数据库密码。
An application reads a database password from a configuration file.

1341
01:52:13,744 --> 01:52:19,652
政策现在要求在没有任何人工操作的情况下，每 30 天更改一次密码。
Policy now requires the password to change every 30 days without a human editing anything.

1342
01:52:20,750 --> 01:52:23,824
该应用程序必须始终获取当前值。
The application must always retrieve the current value.

1343
01:52:24,206 --> 01:52:27,780
该数据库是 Amazon RDS for MySQL。
The database is Amazon RDS for MySQL.

1344
01:52:28,782 --> 01:52:30,944
公司应该使用哪个服务？
Which service should the company use?

1345
01:52:31,264 --> 01:52:32,836
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1346
01:52:38,766 --> 01:52:40,784
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

1347
01:52:41,422 --> 01:52:45,184
选项 A 是本模块中最强的干扰项。
Option A is the strongest distractor in this module.

1348
01:52:45,614 --> 01:52:53,476
Parameter Store 确实能安全地存储机密，使用 KMS 进行加密，并且在标准层中不产生费用。
Parameter store genuinely stores secrets securely, encrypts them with KMS, and costs nothing in the standard tier.

1349
01:52:54,030 --> 01:52:59,140
如果要求仅仅是停止在文件中保存密码，那它会是一个不错的答案。
If the requirement were only to stop keeping a password in a file, it would be a fine answer.

1350
01:52:59,886 --> 01:53:06,212
导致它错误的关键词是「没有任何人工操作」，这是自动轮换要求的变体。
What kills it is the phrase without a human editing anything, which is the automatic rotation requirement in disguise.

1351
01:53:06,464 --> 01:53:12,996
而且机密管理器原生支持轮换 RDS 凭证，同时更新数据库和存储的机密。
And secrets manager rotates RDS credentials natively, updating both the database and the stored secret.

1352
01:53:16,544 --> 01:53:17,156
4。
4.

1353
01:53:18,542 --> 01:53:27,652
一家公司的公共网站因为 TLS 证书过期且没人注意到续订提醒，导致离线两小时。
A company's public website went offline for two hours because a TLS certificate expired and nobody noticed the renewal reminder.

1354
01:53:28,558 --> 01:53:33,060
该证书是手动购买并安装在应用负载均衡器上的。
The certificate was manually purchased and installed on an application load balancer.

1355
01:53:33,838 --> 01:53:36,644
公司希望确保这种情况不再发生。
The company wants to make sure this cannot happen again.

1356
01:53:37,934 --> 01:53:38,144
A
A

1357
01:53:39,344 --> 01:53:41,956
在到期日期设置 CloudWatch 警报。
set a CloudWatch alarm on the expiry date.

1358
01:53:42,224 --> 01:53:42,464
B。
B.

1359
01:53:42,926 --> 01:53:45,024
使用 AWS Certificate Manager。
Use AWS Certificate Manager.

1360
01:53:45,344 --> 01:53:47,584
C。将其存储在机密管理器中。
C. Store it in Secrets Manager.

1361
01:53:47,904 --> 01:53:50,084
D。使用 KMS 对其进行加密。
D. Encrypt it with KMS.

1362
01:53:50,574 --> 01:53:51,684
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1363
01:53:57,582 --> 01:53:58,864
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

1364
01:53:59,662 --> 01:54:05,892
这道题的结构与第 6 模块中的访问密钥问题相同，值得识别这种模式。
This has the same structure as the Access Keys question in module 6 and it is worth recognizing the shape.

1365
01:54:07,438 --> 01:54:10,980
三个选项只是在更好地管理问题，而只有一个能消除问题。
Three options manage the problem better and one removes it.

1366
01:54:11,758 --> 01:54:14,308
警报只会让被忽略的提醒变得更响。
An alarm makes the ignored reminder louder.

1367
01:54:15,214 --> 01:54:20,292
将证书存到别处或对其进行加密，都不会改变过期日期。
Storing the certificate elsewhere or encrypting it changes nothing about the expiry date.

1368
01:54:20,814 --> 01:54:31,172
只有 Certificate Manager 能实现自动续订，这样就根本不需要人工操作。当题目要求“确保这种情况不再发生”时，要找那个能消除问题而不是仅仅监控问题的选项。
Only certificate manager makes renewal automatic, so nobody has to act at all. When a question says, make sure this cannot happen again, look for the option that eliminates rather than monitors.

1369
01:54:32,654 --> 01:54:33,636
什么场景？
What scenario?

1370
01:54:37,454 --> 01:54:41,956
一家公司在 AWS Organizations 下运行 60 个 AWS 账户。
A company runs 60 AWS accounts under AWS organizations.

1371
01:54:43,118 --> 01:54:47,172
安全团队编写了一套 WAF 规则。
The security team has written a set of WAF rules.

1372
01:54:48,014 --> 01:54:54,404
每个账户中所有现有和未来的面向互联网的负载均衡器都必须应用这些规则。
Every existing and future internet facing load balancer in every account must have them applied.

1373
01:54:55,342 --> 01:55:03,172
团队经常创建新账户和负载均衡器，且不通知安全团队，哪个服务符合这一要求。
Teams create new accounts and load balancers regularly without telling the security team which service meets this requirement.

1374
01:55:03,694 --> 01:55:04,708
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1375
01:55:10,830 --> 01:55:12,416
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

1376
01:55:12,974 --> 01:55:18,788
题干中的三个条款都指向同一个方向，即“所有现有和未来的资源”
Three clauses in the STEM all point the same way, every existing and future resource

1377
01:55:20,718 --> 01:55:22,276
“跨越 60 个账户”
across 60 accounts

1378
01:55:22,926 --> 01:55:25,444
“且在未通知安全团队的情况下创建”
and created without the security team being told.

1379
01:55:25,966 --> 01:55:28,736
其中任何一个都会削弱手动操作的选项。
Any one of those weakens the manual option.

1380
01:55:28,896 --> 01:55:30,788
它们共同排除了其他选项。
Together they eliminate it.

1381
01:55:31,630 --> 01:55:38,256
选项 D 是一个更强力的干扰项，因为 Config 确实能发现负载均衡器缺少 Web ACL 的情况。
Option D is a sharper distractor because config genuinely would find load balancers missing a web, ACL.

1382
01:55:38,576 --> 01:55:43,588
但检测漏洞和修复漏洞是两回事，而这里的要求是规则必须生效。
But detecting a gap and closing it are different jobs, and the requirement here is that the rules are applied.

1383
01:55:45,038 --> 01:55:54,576
总结一下，先确定层级：容量属于 Shield，请求内容属于 WAF，而实例或子网属于安全组和网络
To recap, name the layer first, volume is shield, request content is WAF, and an instance or subnet is security groups and network

1384
01:55:54,736 --> 01:55:55,652
ACLs。
ACLs.

1385
01:55:57,614 --> 01:56:03,940
Shield 标准版是免费且默认开启的，而高级版每月费用为 3000 美元，且需要说明理由。
Shield standard is free and already on, while advanced costs $3,000 a month and needs a stated reason.

1386
01:56:04,896 --> 01:56:11,940
KMS 是密钥的默认选项，只有在监管机构要求专用硬件时才使用 CloudHSM。
KMS is the default for keys with CloudHSM only when a regulator demands dedicated hardware.

1387
01:56:12,256 --> 01:56:16,260
静态数据意味着 KMS，而传输中数据意味着证书。
At rest means KMS, while in transit means certificates.

1388
01:56:16,656 --> 01:56:19,844
自动轮换意味着机密管理器。
And automatic rotation means secrets manager.

1389
01:56:21,390 --> 01:56:26,500
下一个模块是合规性与治理，这涵盖了领域 2。
Next module, compliance and governance, which closes domain 2.

1390
01:56:28,270 --> 01:56:30,084
这个模块涉及领域 2。
This module poses domain 2.

1391
01:56:30,416 --> 01:56:38,372
它涵盖了组织如何跨多个 AWS 账户设置边界，以及在审计员询问时如何提供证据。
It covers how an organization sets boundaries across many AWS accounts and how it produces evidence when an auditor asks.

1392
01:56:38,798 --> 01:56:42,788
这是两项不同的工作，考试会将它们分开，所以我们要区分两者。
Those are two different jobs and the exam keeps them separate, so we will two.

1393
01:56:44,430 --> 01:56:52,996
这两个词听起来可以互换但不能。治理是提前设定边界，确保某些事情不会发生。
Two words that sound interchangeable and are not. Governance is about setting boundaries in advance so that certain things cannot happen.

1394
01:56:53,456 --> 01:56:58,660
合规性是事后提供证据，证明正确的事情已经发生了。
Compliance is about producing evidence afterwards that the right things did happen.

1395
01:56:58,958 --> 01:57:02,692
组织 和 控制塔 属于治理。
Organizations and Control Tower are Governance.

1396
01:57:03,502 --> 01:57:06,532
Artifact 和 Config 报告属于合规性。
Artifact and config reports are compliance.

1397
01:57:07,406 --> 01:57:11,620
当问题询问如何防止某事时，你处于治理范畴。
When a question asks how to prevent something, you are in governance.

1398
01:57:12,366 --> 01:57:15,684
当问题询问如何证明某事时，你处于合规性范畴。
When it asks how to prove something, you are in compliance.

1399
01:57:17,376 --> 01:57:25,924
AWS Organizations 让你可以将多个 AWS 账户作为一个组织集中管理，且该服务本身不收费。
AWS organizations lets you centrally manage many AWS accounts as one organization and the service itself costs nothing.

1400
01:57:26,256 --> 01:57:35,492
合并账单让你获得单一账单，更重要的是它汇总了跨账户的使用量，因此合并后的总额可以享受批量折扣。
Consolidated billing gives you a single bill and importantly aggregates usage across accounts so volume discounts apply to the combined total.

1401
01:57:36,723 --> 01:57:42,916
组织单位、分组账号，这样策略就可以一次性应用于整个组。
Organizational Units Group Accounts So a policy can be applied to a whole group at once.

1402
01:57:44,942 --> 01:57:49,988
一个管理账户支付账单，其他所有账户都是成员账户。
One management account pays the bill and everything else is a member account.

1403
01:57:50,990 --> 01:57:55,556
一些服务要求必须先存在组织才能使用它们。
Several services require organizations to exist before you can use them.

1404
01:57:57,294 --> 01:58:02,468
服务控制策略是 AWS 中最常被误解的对象。所以要准确理解。
Service control policies are the most misunderstood object in AWS. So be precise.

1405
01:58:03,056 --> 01:58:06,816
服务控制策略 设置了账户中可用的最大权限。
An SCP sets the maximum permissions available in an account.

1406
01:58:07,056 --> 01:58:08,176
它是一个上限。
It is a ceiling.

1407
01:58:08,336 --> 01:58:12,996
它从不授予任何权限，因此用户仍需要一个允许该操作的 IAM 策略。
It never grants anything, so a user still needs an IAM policy allowing the action.

1408
01:58:13,550 --> 01:58:19,588
只有当 服务控制策略 允许且 IAM 政策也允许时，操作才会成功。
An action succeeds only if the SCP allows it and an IAAM policy allows it.

1409
01:58:20,014 --> 01:58:21,348
两者都要满足，而不是其中一个。
Both, not either.

1410
01:58:21,966 --> 01:58:27,940
服务控制策略 甚至能约束成员账户的根用户，而普通的 IAM 策略做不到这一点。
SCPs bind even the root user of a member account, which ordinary AAAM policies cannot do.

1411
01:58:28,718 --> 01:58:31,076
而且它们永远不会应用于管理账户。
And they never apply to the management account.

1412
01:58:32,686 --> 01:58:38,276
服务控制策略 和 IAM 策略经常被混淆，所以要牢记它们的区别。
SCPs and IAM policies are constantly swapped, so hold the separator firmly.

1413
01:58:38,656 --> 01:58:42,340
服务控制策略 是绑定到组织单位或账户上的。
An SCP is attached to an organizational unit or an account.

1414
01:58:42,576 --> 01:58:48,260
它在不授予权限的情况下进行限制，并适用于那里的每一个身份，包括根用户。
It restricts without ever granting and applies to every identity there, including the root user.

1415
01:58:49,056 --> 01:58:56,772
IAM 策略是绑定到用户、组或角色上的，既包含授权也包含拒绝，且仅适用于该特定身份。
An IAM policy is attached to a user, group or role, both grants and denies, and applies only to that identity.

1416
01:58:57,646 --> 01:59:01,412
限制整个账户能做什么的操作就是 服务控制策略。
Restricting what an entire account can do means SCP.

1417
01:59:01,806 --> 01:59:04,743
给某一个人提供访问权限则是 IAM。
Giving one person access means high AAM.

1418
01:59:06,414 --> 01:59:13,376
今天打开组织的控制台，你会看到除了服务控制策略之外还有其他内容。以下是其他的相关项。
Open the organization's console today and you will see more than service control policies. So here is what the rest are.

1419
01:59:13,678 --> 01:59:16,896
标签策略强制执行一致的标签标准。
Tag policies enforce consistent tagging standards.

1420
01:59:17,198 --> 01:59:20,452
备份策略集中管理备份计划。
Backup policies centrally manage backup plans.

1421
01:59:21,198 --> 01:59:29,476
2024 年底新增的资源控制策略是针对资源而非身份来设定操作上限。
Resource control policies added in late 2024 set a ceiling on what can be done to a resource rather than by an identity.

1422
01:59:30,414 --> 01:59:36,644
而声明式政策为 EC2、EBS 和 VPC 执行基准配置。
And declarative policies enforce a baseline configuration for EC2, EBS, and VPC.

1423
01:59:37,742 --> 01:59:40,708
考试大纲只提到了服务控制策略。
The exam guide names service control policies only.

1424
01:59:41,614 --> 01:59:43,908
识别出其他的就足够了。
Recognizing the others is enough.

1425
01:59:45,294 --> 01:59:53,296
控制塔 利用组织、IAM Identity Center、CloudRail
Control Tower sets up a multi account landing zone for you using organizations, AAM Identity Center, CloudRail,

1426
01:59:53,456 --> 01:59:54,816
以及底层的 Config，为你建立一个多账户着陆区。
and config underneath.

1427
01:59:55,216 --> 01:59:59,876
它的控制措施（旧教材称之为护栏）分为三种。
Its controls, which older material calls guardrails, come in three kinds.

1428
02:00:02,496 --> 02:00:05,604
预防性、检测性以及主动型。
Preventive, Detective, and Proactive.

1429
02:00:06,542 --> 02:00:08,016
账户工厂负责供应。
Account factory provisions.

1430
02:00:08,256 --> 02:00:12,996
即提供已经符合你标准的账户。了解这些组件如何关联起来很有用。
New accounts that already conform to your standard. Worth knowing how the pieces connect.

1431
02:00:13,376 --> 02:00:19,172
预防性控制通过 服务控制策略 实现，检测性控制通过 Config 规则实现。
Preventive controls are implemented with SCPs and detective controls are implemented with config rules.

1432
02:00:19,536 --> 02:00:22,820
控制塔 是基于组织构建的，而不是取代它。
Control tower based on organizations rather than replacing it.

1433
02:00:24,334 --> 02:00:26,852
组织为你提供构建块。
Organizations give you building blocks.

1434
02:00:27,502 --> 02:00:35,776
包括账户、组织单位、服务控制策略和合并账单，由你来设计结构。
Accounts, organizational units, service control policies, and consolidated billing with you designing the structure.

1435
02:00:36,302 --> 02:00:46,116
控制塔 提供一个已按照 AWS 建议构建好的着陆区，并开启了控制措施，且账户工厂已准备好供应更多账户。
Control tower gives you a landing zone already built to AWS recommendations with controls switched on and account factory ready to provision more accounts.

1436
02:00:46,670 --> 02:00:48,772
它灵活性较低，但速度快得多。
It is less flexible and far quicker.

1437
02:00:49,838 --> 02:00:51,684
关键的提示词是“速度”。
The giveaway phrase is speed.

1438
02:00:52,878 --> 02:00:56,484
快速建立一个安全的多账户环境意味着 控制塔。
Quickly set up a secure multi-account environment means control tower.

1439
02:00:57,390 --> 02:01:01,252
管理账户并应用策略意味着组织。
Manage accounts and apply policies means organizations.

1440
02:01:02,830 --> 02:01:08,336
服务目录是经过筛选的、用户可以自行启动的获准产品列表。
Service catalog is a curated list of approved products that users can launch for themselves.

1441
02:01:08,590 --> 02:01:15,136
核心团队定义哪些内容是获批的，用户从该列表中部署，无需广泛的权限。
A center team defines what is approved and users deploy from that list without needing broad permissions.

1442
02:01:15,376 --> 02:01:20,804
这些产品是 CloudFormation 模板，因此每次部署的内容都是一致的。
The products are cloud formation templates, so what gets deployed is consistent every time.

1443
02:01:21,856 --> 02:01:30,884
它的存在是为了平衡让团队快速行动与保持控制之间的矛盾。不要把它和销售第三方软件的 AWS 市场 混淆。
It exists to resolve the tension between letting teams move fast and keeping control. Do not confuse it with AWS Marketplace, which sells third-party software.

1444
02:01:31,376 --> 02:01:34,180
Service Catalog 列出的是你自己的获批项目。
Service catalog lists your own approved items.

1445
02:01:35,790 --> 02:01:41,412
对于这些服务，它们都会报告有问题，而考试会让你在这些选项中做出选择。
For services, all report that something is wrong and the exam makes you choose between them.

1446
02:01:42,414 --> 02:01:45,124
区别在于应用的是谁的标准。
The difference is whose standard is being applied.

1447
02:01:45,934 --> 02:01:48,996
Config 是根据你启用或编写的规则进行检查。
Config checks against rules you enable or write.

1448
02:01:49,390 --> 02:01:51,204
也就是说，是按照你定义的合规性。
So your definition of compliant.

1449
02:01:52,110 --> 02:02:00,656
顾问 根据 AWS 在成本、性能、安全性、容错性方面的最佳实践进行检查，
Trusted advisor checks against AWS best practices across cost, performance, security, fault tolerance,

1450
02:02:00,816 --> 02:02:01,924
以及服务配额。
and service quotas.

1451
02:02:04,270 --> 02:02:13,188
Security Hub 根据特定的安全标准（如 CIS、PCI 等）进行检查，并汇总其他服务的发现。
Security Hub checks against named security standards such as CIR as NP, CIDSS, and aggregates other services findings.

1452
02:02:13,774 --> 02:02:18,148
控制塔 在着陆区内根据其自身的控制措施进行检查。
Control tower checks against its own controls across the landing zone.

1453
02:02:19,758 --> 02:02:25,124
AWS Artifact 是 AWS 合规性报告的自助式下载服务。
AWS artifact is a self-service download of AWS compliance reports.

1454
02:02:25,646 --> 02:02:30,176
包括 SOC、ISO、PCI 等许多其他标准。
SOC, ISO, PC, I, and many others.

1455
02:02:30,496 --> 02:02:38,084
这是你证明 AWS 在共享责任模型中承担的那部分职责的方式，因为你自己无法检查数据中心。
This is how you evidence AWS's half of the shared responsibility model because you cannot inspect a data center yourself.

1456
02:02:38,958 --> 02:02:45,508
它还包含你可以查阅并接受的协议，例如针对医疗数据的业务伙伴协议。
It also holds agreements you can review and accept, such as a business associate addendum for healthcare data.

1457
02:02:46,446 --> 02:02:47,908
Artifact 不进行审计。
Artifact audits nothing.

1458
02:02:48,206 --> 02:02:51,588
它是一个文档库，这就是该服务的全部功能。
It is a document repository, and that is the entire service.

1459
02:02:52,398 --> 02:02:57,924
注意 AWS Audit Manager 是不同的服务，不在本次考试的范围内。
Note that AWS Audit Manager is a different service and is not in scope for this exam.

1460
02:02:59,182 --> 02:03:06,980
关于日志的问题很常见，且答案非常明确。CloudTrail 记录 API 调用和账户活动。所以是“谁做了什么”？
Log questions are common and the answers are distinct. Cloud Trail records API calls and account activity. So who did what?

1461
02:03:08,174 --> 02:03:12,836
CloudWatch 日志包含你发送给它的应用程序和操作系统的日志。
CloudWatch logs holds application and operating system logs that you send to it.

1462
02:03:13,296 --> 02:03:18,852
VPC 流日志记录进入和离开网络接口的 IP 流量。
VPC flow logs record IP traffic going to and from network interfaces.

1463
02:03:19,598 --> 02:03:24,196
S3 服务器访问日志记录对存储桶中对象的请求。
S3 server access logs record requests made to objects in a bucket.

1464
02:03:24,496 --> 02:03:31,204
而 Config 保留随时间变化的配置状态，虽然它严格来说不是日志，但往往是问题真正想要的答案。
And config holds configuration state over time, which is not strictly a log but often what a question is actually after.

1465
02:03:32,846 --> 02:03:38,976
题目场景：1. 一家公司在组织下拥有 90 个 AWS 账户。
What scenario? 1. A company has 90 AWS accounts under organizations.

1466
02:03:39,216 --> 02:03:48,900
策略规定，无论是谁申请，研究组织单位之外的任何账户都不得在欧盟以外的区域启动资源。
Policy states that no account outside the research organizational unit may launch resources in regions outside the European Union, regardless of who is asking.

1467
02:03:49,856 --> 02:03:54,404
其中几个账户有拥有完整 IAM 权限的管理员。
Several accounts have their own administrators with full IAM permissions.

1468
02:03:54,656 --> 02:03:56,576
公司应该如何强制执行这一规定？
How should the company enforce this?

1469
02:03:56,942 --> 02:03:58,052
停下来思考一下并做出决定。
Pause and decide.

1470
02:04:04,302 --> 02:04:05,424
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

1471
02:04:05,584 --> 02:04:09,424
题干中的两个条款共同作用，排除了某些选项。
Two clauses in the STEM work together to eliminate option.

1472
02:04:09,744 --> 02:04:10,064
A。
A.

1473
02:04:10,606 --> 02:04:16,384
无论是谁在申请，且多个账户都有拥有完整 IAM 权限的管理员。
Regardless of who is asking, and several accounts have administrators with full IAM permissions.

1474
02:04:16,750 --> 02:04:23,904
基于 IAM 的控制可以被任何拥有 IAM 权限的人移除，因此它无法约束管理员。
AAAM based control can be removed by anyone with IAM permissions, so it cannot bind an administrator.

1475
02:04:24,590 --> 02:04:28,804
服务控制策略 高于整个 IAM 层级。
An SCP sits above IAM entirely.

1476
02:04:29,422 --> 02:04:33,540
选项 C 是开头幻灯片中提到的治理和合规 PID。
Option C is the governance and compliance pid from the opening slide.

1477
02:04:34,318 --> 02:04:38,212
Config 是事后检测，而这里的要求是预防。
Config detects afterwards, and the requirement here is prevention.

1478
02:04:39,854 --> 02:04:41,344
处理场景 2。
Worked scenario 2.

1479
02:04:41,584 --> 02:04:51,744
一家医疗保健提供商的审计员要求提供证据，证明托管其工作负载的数据中心的物理和环境控制符合 SOC2
A healthcare provider's auditor requests evidence that physical and environmental controls at the data centers hosting its workloads meet SOC2

1480
02:04:51,904 --> 02:04:52,676
要求。
requirements.

1481
02:04:53,024 --> 02:05:01,504
该提供商还需要与 AWS 签署一份业务伙伴协议，并且不能参观任何 AWS 设施。
The provider also needs to sign a business associate addendum with AWS and cannot visit any AWS facility.

1482
02:05:02,510 --> 02:05:04,304
它应该使用哪个服务？
Which service should it use?

1483
02:05:04,590 --> 02:05:05,892
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1484
02:05:11,982 --> 02:05:13,264
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

1485
02:05:14,144 --> 02:05:20,516
这刻意重复了模块 5 中的审计师问题，并增加了第二个要求来让题目更清晰。
This repeats the auditor question from Module 5 deliberately and adds a second requirement to make it sharper.

1486
02:05:21,550 --> 02:05:29,668
物理和环境控制属于共享责任模型中 AWS 的那一半，所以你无法自己提供这些证据。
Physical and environmental controls belong to AWS's half of the shared responsibility model, so you cannot produce that evidence yourself.

1487
02:05:30,158 --> 02:05:31,460
Artifact 提供这些信息。
Artifact supplies it.

1488
02:05:32,366 --> 02:05:38,020
业务伙伴协议是第二个信号，而协议存在于 Artifact 2 中。
The business associate addendum is the second signal and agreements live in artifact 2.

1489
02:05:39,374 --> 02:05:46,052
选项 A、C 和 D 都属于你负责的那部分模型，这就是为什么它们都没法解决这个问题。
Options A, C and D all look at your half of the model, which is why none of them can help here.

1490
02:05:47,758 --> 02:05:48,900
处理场景。
Worked scenario.

1491
02:05:49,550 --> 02:05:54,948
3. 一家公司即将从一个 AWS 账户扩展到大约 30 个。
3. A company is about to expand from one AWS account to roughly 30.

1492
02:05:55,726 --> 02:06:01,156
它希望快速建立一个安全的多账户环境，并从一开始就有一套标准的控制措施。
It wants a secure multi-account environment quickly with a standard set of controls from the start.

1493
02:06:02,062 --> 02:06:06,276
它还要求集中日志记录以及一种可重复的申请新账户的方法。
It also wants centralized logging and a repeatable way to request new accounts.

1494
02:06:07,214 --> 02:06:10,436
它目前没有现成的多账户设计，且时间有限。
It has no existing multi-account design and limited time.

1495
02:06:11,086 --> 02:06:12,740
它应该使用哪个服务？
Which service should it use?

1496
02:06:13,262 --> 02:06:14,596
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1497
02:06:20,654 --> 02:06:22,864
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

1498
02:06:24,174 --> 02:06:27,876
选项 A 在技术上并非不可能。
Option A is not wrong in the sense of being impossible.

1499
02:06:28,750 --> 02:06:32,036
使用 组织 加上手动编写的策略也能达到目的。
Organizations plus handwritten policies would get there.

1500
02:06:33,070 --> 02:06:38,276
但“快速”、“没有现有设计”和“时间有限”的组合排除了它。
What rules it out is the combination of quickly and no existing design and limited time.

1501
02:06:39,246 --> 02:06:43,844
考试用这些词来区分原始能力和带有特定预设的配置。
The exam uses those words to separate the raw capability from the opinionated setup.

1502
02:06:44,224 --> 02:06:48,676
注意第四个要求，就是团队申请新账户的一种可重复的方法。
And notice the fourth requirement, a repeatable way for teams to request new accounts.

1503
02:06:49,166 --> 02:06:52,868
这就是账户工厂，它只属于控制塔。
That is account factory, and it belongs to control tower alone.

1504
02:06:54,414 --> 02:06:55,364
实战场景。
Worked scenario.

1505
02:06:55,854 --> 02:06:56,304
4。
4.

1506
02:06:57,646 --> 02:07:06,500
一个平台团队希望开发小组能按需部署预先批准且配置正确的环境，同时不给他们创建任意资源的权限。
A platform team wants development squads to deploy pre-approved, correctly configured environments on demand without giving them permission to create arbitrary resources.

1507
02:07:07,342 --> 02:07:14,564
另外，安全团队要求每当任何已部署的资源偏离要求的加密设置时，都要发出警报。
Separately, the security team wants an alert whenever any deployed resource drifts from the required encryption settings.

1508
02:07:14,944 --> 02:07:17,344
哪两个服务符合这些要求？
Which two services meet these requirements?

1509
02:07:17,710 --> 02:07:18,852
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1510
02:07:24,942 --> 02:07:26,820
答案是 A 和 C。
The answers are A and C.

1511
02:07:27,342 --> 02:07:29,572
两个要求，分别对应一个服务。
Two requirements, one service each.

1512
02:07:30,478 --> 02:07:34,724
在不授予广泛权限的情况下部署预先批准的环境是服务目录。
Pre-approved environments deployed without broad permissions is service catalog.

1513
02:07:35,024 --> 02:07:37,904
偏离要求的设置则是 Config。
Drift from a required setting is config.

1514
02:07:38,670 --> 02:07:45,860
选项 E 是这里最强力的干扰项，而区分点在于“谁在检查什么”的对照表。
Option E is the sharpest distractor here, and the separator is the one from the who checks what table.

1515
02:07:46,830 --> 02:07:50,384
顾问是根据 AWS 的最佳实践来衡量你。
Trusted advisor measures you against AWS's best practices.

1516
02:07:50,624 --> 02:07:52,868
Config 是根据你自己的规则来衡量。
Config measures you against your own rules.

1517
02:07:53,184 --> 02:07:59,364
场景中提到的是“要求的加密设置”，意味着公司的标准，这在任何时候都是 Config。
The scenario says the required encryption settings, meaning the company's own standard, which is config every time.

1518
02:08:00,974 --> 02:08:07,972
总结一下，这部分结束了领域 2：治理是预防，而合规性是证明。所以要看题目要求哪一个。
To recap, and this closes domain 2, governance prevents while compliance proves. So read which one the question wants.

1519
02:08:09,966 --> 02:08:12,080
服务控制策略 是上限，而不是授权。
An SCP is a ceiling, never a grant.

1520
02:08:12,400 --> 02:08:15,684
操作需要同时具备 服务控制策略 允许和 IAM 允许。
The action needs both an SCP allow and an IAM allow.

1521
02:08:17,166 --> 02:08:21,956
服务控制策略 约束成员账户的根用户，但绝不约束管理账户。
SCPs bind the root user of a member account, but never the management account.

1522
02:08:22,862 --> 02:08:28,996
控制塔是快速且有预设配置的着陆区，而组织是底层的原始能力。
Control tower is the quick opinionated landing zone while organizations is the raw capability underneath.

1523
02:08:29,360 --> 02:08:33,604
Artifact 是 AWS 自有审计报告的存储库。
An artifact is a repository of AWS's own audit reports.

1524
02:08:34,318 --> 02:08:37,732
下一模块进入领域 3，从全球基础设施开始。
Next module opens domain 3 with global infrastructure.

1525
02:08:39,470 --> 02:08:43,920
本模块开启领域 3，这是占比最大的领域，占 34%。
This module opens domain 3, the largest domain at 34%.

1526
02:08:44,846 --> 02:08:49,700
全球基础设施是该领域其余部分默认使用的词汇，所以它排在最前面。
Global infrastructure is the vocabulary the rest of the domain assumes, so it comes first.

1527
02:08:50,478 --> 02:08:59,108
在题库分析中，区域和可用区共同出现了 24 次，这使其成为考试中最常考的组合之一。
Region and availability zone co-occurred 24 times in the bank analysis, which makes it one of the most tested pairs on the exam.

1528
02:09:00,846 --> 02:09:09,380
AWS 基础设施是一个层级结构，这里几乎每个问题其实都在问：哪个层级的架构能解决所述问题。
AWS infrastructure is a hierarchy, and almost every question here is really asking which level of that hierarchy solves the stated problem.

1529
02:09:10,926 --> 02:09:12,676
区域是一个地理区域。
A region is a geographic area.

1530
02:09:13,614 --> 02:09:15,780
在其中包含可用区。
Inside it are availability zones.

1531
02:09:16,398 --> 02:09:19,108
边缘站点分布得要广泛得多。
Scattered far more widely are edge locations.

1532
02:09:20,046 --> 02:09:26,660
确定需求属于哪个层级，答案通常就出来了。
Identify which level the requirement belongs to and the answer is usually already decided.

1533
02:09:27,918 --> 02:09:30,148
共有 5 个层级，从大到小排列。
5 levels, largest to smallest.

1534
02:09:31,182 --> 02:09:35,396
区域是一个包含多个可用区的地理区域。
A region is a geographic area containing multiple availability zones.

1535
02:09:36,590 --> 02:09:41,572
可用区是一个或多个与其它中心隔离的独立数据中心。
An availability zone is one or more discrete data centers isolated from the others.

1536
02:09:42,254 --> 02:09:46,948
本地区域是更靠近人口中心的区域扩展。
A local zone is an extension of a region placed nearer a population center.

1537
02:09:47,886 --> 02:09:52,868
边缘站点是 CloudFront 的缓存站点，它们的数量比区域多得多。
An edge location is a caching site for CloudFront, and there are far more of these than regions.

1538
02:09:53,280 --> 02:09:58,852
AWS Outposts 是安装在你自己的数据中心中的 AWS 管理硬件。
An AWS outposts is AWS managed hardware installed in your own data center.

1539
02:10:00,110 --> 02:10:03,236
区域和可用区是你运行业务的地方。
Regions and availability zones are where you run things.

1540
02:10:03,822 --> 02:10:06,340
边缘站点是缓存内容的地方。
Edge locations are where content is cached.

1541
02:10:08,046 --> 02:10:09,380
这是基础的一对概念。
The foundational pair.

1542
02:10:10,094 --> 02:10:15,492
区域是一个以地点命名的、包含多个可用区的地理区域。
A region is a geographic area named for a place containing multiple availability zones.

1543
02:10:15,950 --> 02:10:20,900
在你创建大多数资源时选择其中一个，除非你主动移动，否则数据不会离开该区域。
You pick one when you create most resources and your data does not leave it unless you move it.

1544
02:10:21,774 --> 02:10:28,132
可用区是该区域内拥有独立电力和冷却系统的隔离基础设施。
An availability zone is isolated infrastructure inside that region with its own power and cooling.

1545
02:10:28,400 --> 02:10:33,924
它在物理上与其他中心隔开，但足够近，可以支持低延迟的私有网络。
It is physically separated from the others, but close enough for low latency private networking.

1546
02:10:34,798 --> 02:10:40,260
区分点是题目关注的内容。地理位置和数据驻留意味着区域。
The separator is what the question worries about. Geography and data residency means region.

1547
02:10:41,038 --> 02:10:43,972
能够承受故障意味着可用区。
Surviving a failure means availability zone.

1548
02:10:45,360 --> 02:10:51,492
了解可用区为何这样设计很有意义，因为它解释了它们的用途。
It is worth understanding why availability zones are designed the way they are because it explains their use.

1549
02:10:51,840 --> 02:10:57,124
每一个都是拥有独立电力、冷却和物理安全的多个数据中心。
Each is one or more data centers with independent power, cooling, and physical security.

1550
02:10:57,440 --> 02:11:02,180
它们之间的距离足够远，以至于一个灾难不太可能影响到两个。
They are separated by enough distance that one disaster is unlikely to affect two.

1551
02:11:02,990 --> 02:11:07,280
但它们又足够近，可以实现同步复制。
But they stay close enough for replication between them to be synchronous.

1552
02:11:07,520 --> 02:11:09,604
这种权衡是刻意设计的。
That trade-off is deliberate.

1553
02:11:10,000 --> 02:11:11,460
注意最后一点。
And note the last point.

1554
02:11:11,918 --> 02:11:17,988
在同一个可用区中的两个实例提供冗余，但不提供高可用性。
Two instances in the same availability zone give you redundancy but not high availability.

1555
02:11:19,406 --> 02:11:24,880
这对概念在分析中出现了 14 次，区分点非常明确。
This pair co-occurred 14 times in the analysis and the separator is clean.

1556
02:11:25,326 --> 02:11:31,876
可用区是运行工作负载的地方，你使用多个可用区来应对基础设施故障。
Availability zones are where your workload runs and you use several of them to survive infrastructure failure.

1557
02:11:32,430 --> 02:11:39,684
边缘站点是缓存内容的地方，你利用它们为远离你所在区域的用户降低延迟。
Edge locations are where content is cached and you use them to reduce latency for users far from your region.

1558
02:11:40,622 --> 02:11:46,884
在更多城市有更多的边缘站点，而且你永远不会在其中部署工作负载。
There are far more edge locations in many more cities, and you never deploy a workload into one.

1559
02:11:47,694 --> 02:11:50,948
高可用性意味着可用区。
High availability means availability zones.

1560
02:11:51,982 --> 02:11:55,300
向远方用户快速交付内容意味着边缘站点。
Fast delivery to distant users means edge locations.

1561
02:11:56,782 --> 02:12:05,040
在实际操作中，CloudFront 在边缘站点缓存内容，这样用户就可以从附近获取内容，而不是从源站获取。
In practice, CloudFront caches content at edge locations so users fetch it from somewhere nearby rather than from the origin.

1562
02:12:05,742 --> 02:12:13,796
区域边缘缓存位于边缘站点和源站之间，用于存放那些体积太大或请求频率太低、无法保留在边缘的内容。
Regional edge caches sit between the edge locations and the origin, holding content too large or too infrequently requested to stay at the edge.

1563
02:12:14,766 --> 02:12:23,108
Route 53 和 Global Accelerator 也使用边缘网络，而 Shield 标准版和 WAF 在与 CloudFront 一起使用时也会在这些位置运行。
Route 53 and Global Accelerator also use the edge network, and Shivi Standard and WAF operate there when used with CloudFront.

1564
02:12:23,406 --> 02:12:24,164
有一个注意事项
One caution

1565
02:12:25,550 --> 02:12:28,388
在边缘进行缓存并不会提高源站的可用性。
Caching at the edge does not make your origin more available.

1566
02:12:28,640 --> 02:12:31,972
如果源站宕机，任何未被缓存的内容都无法访问。
If the origin is down, anything uncached still fails.

1567
02:12:33,518 --> 02:12:36,452
当一个区域距离不够近时，有三个服务可以解决这个问题。
Three services exist for when a region is not close enough.

1568
02:12:36,800 --> 02:12:44,804
本地区域将计算和存储部署在靠近人口密集中心的地方，为当地用户提供单数毫秒级的延迟。
Local zones place compute and storage nearer a large population center, giving single-digit millisecond latency to users there.

1569
02:12:45,440 --> 02:12:51,204
Outposts 在您自己的数据中心安装 AWS 管理的机架，从而在本地运行 AWS 服务。
Outpost installs AWS managed racks in your own data center, running AWS services locally.

1570
02:12:52,110 --> 02:13:00,228
当数据必须物理上保留在您的 premises 上，或者到最近区域的延迟无法接受时，Outposts 是正确的答案。
Outposts is the answer when data must physically remain on your premises or when latency to the nearest region is unacceptable.

1571
02:13:00,878 --> 02:13:02,884
这两者都会连接回母源区域。
Both connect back to a parent region.

1572
02:13:03,438 --> 02:13:09,636
AWS Wavelength 为第五代移动网络提供服务，它不在本次考试的考核范围内。
AWS Wavelength serves fifth generation mobile networks and it is not on the in-scope list for this exam.

1573
02:13:11,360 --> 02:13:16,356
有四个因素决定一个区域，而考试中这些因素出现的顺序大致如下。
Four factors decide a region, and the exam uses them in roughly this order.

1574
02:13:16,800 --> 02:13:22,756
首先是合规性，即数据治理和法律要求，这是不可逾越的条件。
Compliance first, meaning data governance and legal requirements, and this one is non-negotiable.

1575
02:13:23,758 --> 02:13:28,036
其次是延迟，因为离用户近一点可以节省几毫秒的时间。
Then latency, because proximity to your users costs milliseconds.

1576
02:13:28,782 --> 02:13:37,860
然后是服务可用性，因为并非所有服务都存在于每个区域；最后是定价，因为同样的资源在不同地方的成本不同。
Then service availability, because not every service exists in every region, and finally pricing, since the same resource costs different amounts in different places.

1577
02:13:38,510 --> 02:13:44,068
如果场景中提到关于数据存放位置的法律要求，那么合规性将优先于其他所有因素。
If a scenario mentions a legal requirement about where data may live, compliance override as everything else.

1578
02:13:45,710 --> 02:13:49,040
您部署范围有多广，取决于您要防范什么风险。
How far you spread depends on what you are protecting against.

1579
02:13:49,280 --> 02:13:58,756
在同一个区域内使用多个可用区可以应对数据中心的故障，这是在不增加太多复杂性的情况下实现高可用性的标准答案。
Multiple availability zones within one region survives the loss of a data center, and it is the standard answer for high availability with little added complexity.

1580
02:13:59,438 --> 02:14:09,668
使用多个区域可以应对整个区域的故障，用于服务全球用户以及满足数据驻留规则的情况。
Multiple regions survive the loss of an entire region and is used for disaster recovery for serving global users and where data residency rules demand it.

1581
02:14:10,222 --> 02:14:12,740
这会增加成本并增加复杂度。
It costs more and adds complexity.

1582
02:14:13,422 --> 02:14:16,900
高可用性意味着多可用区。
High availability means multi-availability zone.

1583
02:14:18,126 --> 02:14:21,732
容灾或全球覆盖意味着多区域。
Disaster recovery or global reach means multi-region.

1584
02:14:23,360 --> 02:14:28,240
服务有其范围，关于在第二个区域启动的问题取决于这个范围。
Services have a scope and questions about launching in a second region depend on it.

1585
02:14:28,400 --> 02:14:33,828
全球服务包括 IAM、Route 53、CloudFront 和组织。
Global services include IAM, Route 53, CloudFront, and organizations.

1586
02:14:34,080 --> 02:14:43,364
区域性服务包括 EC2、VPC、RDS、DynamoDB 和 Lambda。这些必须在您想要部署的每个区域中重新创建。
Regional services include EC2, VPC, RDS, DynamoDB, and Lambda. Those must be created again in each region you want them in.

1587
02:14:44,302 --> 02:14:46,212
有两个容易让人混淆的细节。
Two details that catch people.

1588
02:14:48,206 --> 02:14:53,220
S3 存储桶名称是全球唯一的，但存储桶本身存在于一个特定的区域。
S3 bucket names are globally unique, but the bucket itself lives in one region.

1589
02:14:54,798 --> 02:15:00,580
而且 Amazon machine image 是区域性的，因此将其复制到其他地方是一个有意的步骤。
And an Amazon machine image is regional, so copying it elsewhere is a deliberate step.

1590
02:15:01,966 --> 02:15:03,920
六种表述方式对应六个答案。
Six phrasings and six answers.

1591
02:15:04,160 --> 02:15:09,412
几乎每一个关于全球基础设施的题目，都是这些表述的不同变体。
And almost every global infrastructure question is one of these dressed differently.

1592
02:15:10,094 --> 02:15:14,948
如果数据中心故障仍能保持可用，意味着有多个可用区。
Staying available if a data center fails means multiple availability zones.

1593
02:15:17,070 --> 02:15:21,124
能够承受整个区域的损失，意味着有多个区域。
Surviving the loss of a whole region means multiple regions.

1594
02:15:22,062 --> 02:15:32,772
数据必须留在国家边界内，意味着基于合规性选择区域；全球用户抱怨页面加载慢，意味着 CloudFront 和边缘站点。
Data remaining within a country's borders means choosing the region on compliance grounds. Users worldwide complaining of slow page loads means cloud front and edge locations.

1595
02:15:33,120 --> 02:15:41,316
数据留在你自己的大楼里，意味着 AWS Outposts；在同一个城市实现个位数的毫秒级延迟，意味着本地区域。
Data staying in your own building means outposts. And single-digit millisecond latency in one city means local zones.

1596
02:15:42,958 --> 02:15:44,324
动词场景 1。
Verb scenario 1.

1597
02:15:44,910 --> 02:15:53,124
一家公司在负载均衡器后运行 Web 应用程序，有两个 EC2 实例，且都在同一个可用区内。
A company runs its web application on two EC2 instances behind a load balancer, both in the same availability zone.

1598
02:15:53,998 --> 02:15:58,820
在影响该区域的电力事件期间，该应用完全无法使用。
During a power event affecting that zone, the application became completely unavailable.

1599
02:15:59,694 --> 02:16:06,560
公司希望在单个可用区故障时仍能保持可用，且要求成本和复杂度尽可能低。
The company wants it to stay available if a single availability zone fails at the lowest reasonable cost and complexity.

1600
02:16:06,734 --> 02:16:07,652
它应该怎么做？
What should it do?

1601
02:16:08,078 --> 02:16:09,348
停下来思考一下并做出决定。
Pause and decide.

1602
02:16:15,406 --> 02:16:16,548
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

1603
02:16:16,976 --> 02:16:22,308
选项 C 值得思考，因为它并不是在功能上不可行的意思。
Option C is worth dwelling on because it is not wrong in the sense of failing to work.

1604
02:16:22,736 --> 02:16:26,820
第二个区域肯定能应对可用区的故障。
A second region would certainly survive an availability zone failure.

1605
02:16:27,278 --> 02:16:29,636
但它错误的原因是过度设计了。
It is wrong because it is disproportionate.

1606
02:16:30,510 --> 02:16:37,156
要求中提到了单个可用区故障，并要求最低的合理成本和复杂度。
The requirement names a single availability zone failure and asks for the lowest reasonable cost and complexity.

1607
02:16:37,616 --> 02:16:41,348
多区域解决了更大的问题，但代价要高得多。
Multi-region solves a bigger problem at a much higher price.

1608
02:16:42,096 --> 02:16:48,580
在这场考试中，完全符合所述要求的选项优于超出要求的选项。
On this exam, the option that exactly matches the stated requirement beats the option that exceeds it.

1609
02:16:50,190 --> 02:16:51,616
工作场景 2。
Work scenario 2.

1610
02:16:51,852 --> 02:16:57,572
一家德国保险公司必须将所有客户数据物理上保存在德国境内，以满足监管机构的要求。
A German insurer must keep all customer data physically within Germany to satisfy its regulator.

1611
02:16:57,856 --> 02:17:03,492
它还希望法兰克福和慕尼黑的员工能获得低延迟，并且更倾向于选择最便宜的方案。
It also wants low latency for staff in Frankfurt and Munich and would prefer the cheapest option.

1612
02:17:03,982 --> 02:17:06,308
一个区域可以满足驻留规则。
One region satisfies the residency rule.

1613
02:17:06,575 --> 02:17:08,420
另一个区域可能更便宜。
A different region is cheaper.

1614
02:17:09,230 --> 02:17:11,652
哪个因素应该决定选择哪个区域？
Which factor should decide the region?

1615
02:17:12,206 --> 02:17:13,284
停下来思考一下并做出决定。
Pause and decide.

1616
02:17:19,150 --> 02:17:20,415
答案是 C。
The answer is C.

1617
02:17:22,510 --> 02:17:25,188
这个场景是围绕两个动词构建的。
This scenario is built around two verbs.

1618
02:17:25,870 --> 02:17:30,020
“必须”保存在德国境内，以及“倾向于”选择最便宜的选项。
Must keep data within Germany and would prefer the cheapest option.

1619
02:17:30,446 --> 02:17:33,508
其中一个是约束条件，另一个只是一个愿望。
One of those is a constraint and the other is a wish.

1620
02:17:33,870 --> 02:17:37,892
而约束条件在阅读其他参考信息之前就会排除掉一些选项。
And constraints eliminate options before references are read at all.

1621
02:17:38,736 --> 02:17:41,763
这种阅读习惯在其他模块中也同样适用。
That reading habit transfers well beyond this module.

1622
02:17:42,016 --> 02:17:47,299
要注意区分“必须要求”和“强制性”，以及“倾向于”、“想要”和“希望”。
Watch for must required and mandated on one hand and prefer want and would like on the other.

1623
02:17:47,616 --> 02:17:49,763
它们在题目中的权重完全不同。
They carry very different weight in a question.

1624
02:17:51,423 --> 02:17:52,083
场景是什么？
What Scenario?

1625
02:17:55,342 --> 02:18:00,036
一家媒体公司在单一的美国区域内托管视频和图像。
A media company hosts video and images in a single United States region.

1626
02:18:00,814 --> 02:18:09,056
澳大利亚和日本的用户反映页面加载需要几秒钟，尽管应用程序运行正常且从未不可用。
Users in Australia and Japan report pages taking several seconds to load, although the application performs normally and is never unavailable.

1627
02:18:09,456 --> 02:18:15,716
公司希望在不移动或复制应用的情况下，让这些用户的页面加载更快。
The company wants faster page loads for those users without moving or duplicating the application.

1628
02:18:16,270 --> 02:18:17,442
它应该使用什么？
What should it use?

1629
02:18:18,382 --> 02:18:19,652
停下来思考一下并做出决定。
Pause and decide.

1630
02:18:25,582 --> 02:18:26,816
答案是 C。
The answer is C.

1631
02:18:26,976 --> 02:18:31,075
题干中的细节往往可以忽略，而且这两类信息都很容易被扫视过去。
The STEM plans to disqualifying details and both are easy to skim past.

1632
02:18:31,376 --> 02:18:36,674
“应用从未不可用”这一项排除了所有关于可用性的选项。
The application is never unavailable, which rules out every availability answer including option.

1633
02:18:37,456 --> 02:18:41,442
B 项以及“不移动或复制应用”的条件排除了相关选项。
B and without moving or duplicating the application rules out option.

1634
02:18:42,976 --> 02:18:43,296
选 A。
A.

1635
02:18:44,270 --> 02:18:51,396
剩下的就是一个关于静态内容和远距离用户的纯延迟问题，这是 CloudFront 的典型特征。
What remains is a pure latency problem with static content and distant users, which is the CloudFront signature.

1636
02:18:52,206 --> 02:18:55,396
注意“从未不可用”这个短语起到了多大的作用。
Notice how much work the phrase never unavailable does.

1637
02:18:56,174 --> 02:19:00,388
延迟和可用性是两个不同的问题，对应的答案也不同。
Latency and availability are different problems with different answers.

1638
02:19:02,156 --> 02:19:03,332
处理好的场景。
Worked scenario.

1639
02:19:07,852 --> 02:19:13,476
一家制造商在工厂运行机器，这些机器必须在极低延迟的情况下进行控制。
A manufacturer runs machinery in a factory that must be controlled with very low latency.

1640
02:19:13,998 --> 02:19:20,036
国家法规要求处理后的数据必须留在工厂现场。
A national regulation requires the processed data to remain physically inside the factory site.

1641
02:19:20,590 --> 02:19:28,004
最近的 AWS 区域在几百公里外，而公司希望使用 AWS 服务和工具。
The nearest AWS region is several hundred kilometers away and the company wants to use AWS services and tooling.

1642
02:19:29,772 --> 02:19:32,096
哪个服务符合这些要求？
Which service meets these requirements?

1643
02:19:32,494 --> 02:19:33,826
停下来思考一下并做出决定。
Pause and decide.

1644
02:19:40,096 --> 02:19:41,412
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

1645
02:19:41,856 --> 02:19:51,268
选项 A 是最强的干扰项，因为本地区域确实是低延迟的解决方案，如果只有延迟这一要求，它就是正确的。
Option A is the strongest distractor because local zones genuinely are the low latency answer, and if latency were the only requirement, it would be correct.

1646
02:19:52,256 --> 02:19:54,340
第二个要求决定了最终答案。
The second requirement decides it.

1647
02:19:55,278 --> 02:20:02,052
数据必须留在工厂内部，而本地区域是位于其他地方的 AWS 设施。
The data must remain physically inside the factory site, and a local zone is an AWS facility somewhere else.

1648
02:20:02,350 --> 02:20:05,856
只有 Outpost 能将 AWS 硬件部署在您自己的建筑内。
Only outpost puts AWS hardware in your own building.

1649
02:20:06,096 --> 02:20:13,316
当出现两个要求时，要对照这两个要求来测试每一个选项，因为干扰项通常能完美满足其中一个。
When two requirements appear, test every option against both because the distractor usually satisfies one of them beautifully.

1650
02:20:14,896 --> 02:20:21,316
总结一下：区域是地理位置，可用区是隔离性，边缘站点是缓存。
To recap, region is geography, availability zone is isolation, edge location is caching.

1651
02:20:22,222 --> 02:20:29,604
多可用区提供高可用性，而多区域提供容灾、全球覆盖或数据主权。
Multi-availability zone gives high availability while multi-region gives disaster recovery, global reach or data sovereignty.

1652
02:20:30,606 --> 02:20:35,780
选择区域时，先看合规性，再看延迟，然后是服务可用性，最后是价格。
Choose a region by compliance, then latency, then service availability, then price.

1653
02:20:36,526 --> 02:20:44,900
Outpost 意味着在您自己的建筑中，而本地区域意味着附近的城市。而且边缘缓存不会提高源站的可用性。
Outpost means your own building while local zones means a nearby city. And edge caching does not make the origin more available.

1654
02:20:46,318 --> 02:20:50,084
下一个模块是关于在 AWS 上部署和运行的方法。
Next module the ways to deploy and operate on AWS.

1655
02:20:51,536 --> 02:20:59,300
本模块涵盖了您实际如何与 AWS 交互，以及如何描述基础设施以便能够重复构建。
This module covers how you actually interact with AWS and how you describe infrastructure so it can be built repeatedly.

1656
02:21:00,078 --> 02:21:05,412
它对服务的讲解较少，但对区别的强调很多，而这正是考试的处理方式。
It is short on services and heavy on distinctions, which is exactly how the exam treats it.

1657
02:21:07,118 --> 02:21:12,612
从一个让本模块变简单的事实开始：只有一个 AWS API。
Start with something that makes this module simple. There is only one AWS API.

1658
02:21:13,070 --> 02:21:20,100
管理控制台调用它，命令行界面调用它，软件开发工具包也调用它，
The management console calls it, the command line interface calls it, the software development kits call it,

1659
02:21:20,750 --> 02:21:22,180
CloudFormation 也调用它。
CloudFormation calls it.

1660
02:21:23,182 --> 02:21:30,180
有四种方式可以发出相同的请求，这就是为什么 CloudTrail 可以记录无论如何执行的所有操作。
There are four ways of making the same request, which is why Cloud Trail can record every action regardless of how it was performed.

1661
02:21:31,310 --> 02:21:33,572
问题从来不是 AWS 能做什么。
The question is never what AWS can do.

1662
02:21:34,382 --> 02:21:36,516
而是哪种界面适合这项任务。
It is which interface suits the task.

1663
02:21:38,126 --> 02:21:42,404
四种界面，产生的都是相同的 API 调用。
Four interfaces, all producing the same API calls.

1664
02:21:43,150 --> 02:21:49,252
管理控制台适用于探索、学习、一次性任务和可视化审查。
The management console suits exploring, learning, one-off tasks, and visual review.

1665
02:21:49,870 --> 02:21:54,084
命令行界面适用于从终端进行脚本编写和可重复的操作。
The command line interface suits scripting and repeatable operations from a terminal.

1666
02:21:55,086 --> 02:21:59,940
软件开发工具包让您能在自己的应用程序代码中调用 AWS。
The software development kits let you call AWS from inside your own application code.

1667
02:22:00,736 --> 02:22:06,564
而基础设施即代码描述的是整个环境，以便能够被完全相同地重建。
And infrastructure as code describes a whole environment so it can be rebuilt identically.

1668
02:22:07,086 --> 02:22:11,460
CloudTrail 以同样的方式记录这四种方式，因为它们在底层是相同的。
CloudTrail records all four the same way because underneath they are identical.

1669
02:22:12,750 --> 02:22:18,404
控制台和命令行界面做同样的事情，但考试根据可重复性将它们区分开来。
The console and the command line interface do the same things and the exam separates them on repeatability.

1670
02:22:19,150 --> 02:22:21,572
控制台是人进行一次性的操作。
The console is a person doing something once.

1671
02:22:22,414 --> 02:22:25,508
点击即可，无需学习，适合调查。
Point and click, nothing to learn, good for investigating.

1672
02:22:26,478 --> 02:22:30,372
但很难完全相同地重复，且不会留下步骤记录。
But it is hard to repeat identically and leaves no record of the steps.

1673
02:22:31,342 --> 02:22:35,236
命令行界面是脚本在重复执行某项操作。
The command line interface is a script doing something repeatedly.

1674
02:22:35,726 --> 02:22:42,724
命令可以被保存、重新运行、用于自动化以及进行审查，因为它们只是文本。
Commands can be saved, rerun, used in automation, and reviewed because they are just text.

1675
02:22:43,566 --> 02:22:45,700
一次性任务意味着控制台。
One off means console.

1676
02:22:46,382 --> 02:22:49,056
可重复操作意味着 CLI。
Repeatable means CLI.

1677
02:22:50,862 --> 02:22:56,644
软件开发工具包是编程语言的库，它封装了 AWS API。
A software development kit is a library for a programming language that wraps the AWS API.

1678
02:22:56,896 --> 02:23:02,884
有针对 Python、Java、JavaScript、.NET、Go 等语言的 SDK。
There are SDKs for Python, Java, JavaScript, .NET, Go, and others.

1679
02:23:03,216 --> 02:23:09,060
当您的应用程序本身需要调用 AWS 而不是由人或脚本操作时，您就使用它。
You use one when your application itself needs to call AWS rather than a person or a script.

1680
02:23:09,838 --> 02:23:18,212
凭证依然适用，且在 AWS 上运行的代码应使用 IAM 角色而非嵌入式密钥，正如第 6 模块中所涵盖的内容一样。
Credentials still apply, and code running on AWS should use an IAM role rather than embedded keys, exactly as covered in module 6.

1681
02:23:19,456 --> 02:23:22,576
考试中不要求你编写任何代码。
You are not expected to write any code on this exam.

1682
02:23:23,918 --> 02:23:32,164
现在进入本模块的第二部分：基础设施即代码，意味着通过文件来描述你想要的内容，而不是通过点击操作来创建。
Now the second half of the module, infrastructure as code, means describing what you want in a file rather than clicking to create it.

1683
02:23:32,656 --> 02:23:35,396
这听起来像是很小的变化，但其实不然。
That sounds like a small change and is not.

1684
02:23:36,302 --> 02:23:42,336
一旦环境变成一份文档，你就可以在它存在之前进行审查，并将其纳入版本控制。
Once an environment is a document, you can review it before it exists and keep it in version control.

1685
02:23:43,342 --> 02:23:48,516
你可以在其他地方完全一致地重建它，并且可以干净利落地删除整个系统。
You can rebuild it identically elsewhere and delete the whole thing cleanly.

1686
02:23:49,422 --> 02:23:55,652
考试中提到的基础设施即代码的所有优点，都源于这一转变。
Every benefit the exam attributes to infrastructure as code follows from that one shift.

1687
02:23:57,294 --> 02:24:00,676
CloudFormation 是基础设施即代码的服务。
CloudFormation is the infrastructure as code service.

1688
02:24:01,056 --> 02:24:07,108
你用 JSON 或 YAML 编写一个模板，来描述你想要的所有资源。
You write a template in JSON or YAML describing the resources you want.

1689
02:24:07,598 --> 02:24:13,028
CloudFormation 会按照正确的顺序将它们作为堆栈创建出来，并自动处理依赖关系。
CloudFormation creates them as a stack in the right order, working out dependencies itself.

1690
02:24:13,838 --> 02:24:20,964
删除堆栈会移除它创建的所有内容，这就是为什么临时测试环境既便宜又安全。
Deleting the stack removes everything it created, which is what makes temporary test environments cheap and safe.

1691
02:24:22,638 --> 02:24:26,884
漂移检测会报告那些在模板之外被修改过的资源。
Drift detection reports resources that have been changed outside the template.

1692
02:24:27,502 --> 02:24:32,580
而且该服务本身是免费的，你只需要为它创建的资源付费。
And the service itself is free, so you pay only for the resources it creates.

1693
02:24:34,318 --> 02:24:36,516
考试会明确这些特定的优点。
The exam name specific benefits.

1694
02:24:36,736 --> 02:24:38,468
所以要记住这些表述方式。
So learn these phrasings.

1695
02:24:39,214 --> 02:24:43,812
可重复性，因为相同的模板每次都能生成相同的环境。
Repeatability, because the same template produces the same environment every time.

1696
02:24:44,430 --> 02:24:49,188
版本控制，因为基础设施的更改会像应用程序的更改一样经过审查。
Version control, because infrastructure changes get reviewed like application changes.

1697
02:24:49,936 --> 02:24:53,668
跨环境的一致性，确保开发环境与生产环境匹配。
Consistency across environments, so development matches production.

1698
02:24:54,656 --> 02:24:59,780
更快的恢复，因为重建意味着运行一个模板，而不是去回忆你之前做了哪些操作。
Faster recovery because rebuilding means running a template rather than remembering what you did.

1699
02:25:00,096 --> 02:25:05,316
以及消除配置中的人为错误，这通常就是正确答案中的准确措辞。
And removing human error from provisioning, which is often the exact phrase in the correct answer.

1700
02:25:06,990 --> 02:25:11,376
CDK（CDK）经常被误认为是 CloudFormation 的替代品。
The cloud development kit is often misunderstood as an alternative to cloud formation.

1701
02:25:11,630 --> 02:25:12,420
它并不是。
It is not.

1702
02:25:14,030 --> 02:25:20,176
使用 CloudFormation 时，你编写一个描述最终状态的声明式模板。不需要编程知识。
With cloud formation, you write a declarative template describing the end state. No programming knowledge is needed.

1703
02:25:20,718 --> 02:25:27,428
使用 CDK 时，你可以使用循环和条件判断来编写 TypeScript、Python 或 Java，而不是重复操作。
With the CDK, you write TypeScript, Python, or Java using loops and conditions instead of repetition.

1704
02:25:29,326 --> 02:25:36,196
但随后 CDK 会合成一个 CloudFormation 模板，由 CloudFormation 来执行实际的配置。
But the CDK then synthesizes a CloudFormation template, and CloudFormation does the actual provisioning.

1705
02:25:37,424 --> 02:25:40,612
Elastic Beanstalk 则采取相反的方法。
Elastic Beanstop takes the opposite approach.

1706
02:25:40,864 --> 02:25:50,784
你提供应用程序代码，AWS 为你配置并运行环境。它会创建 EC2 实例、负载均衡器、自动扩容和健康监控。
You provide application code and AWS provisions and runs the environment for you. It creates EC2 instances, a load balancer, autoscaling, and health monitoring.

1707
02:25:50,944 --> 02:25:56,260
它支持 Java、.NET、PHP、Node、Python、Ruby、Go 和 Docker。
It supports Java, .NET, PHP, Node, Python, Ruby, Go and Docker.

1708
02:25:57,102 --> 02:26:03,104
重要的是，你仍然拥有对底层资源的完全访问权限，并在需要时进行调整。
Importantly, you keep full access to the underlying resources and can adjust them if you need to.

1709
02:26:03,470 --> 02:26:08,772
该服务是免费的，你只需为 EC2 实例和其他创建的资源付费。
The service is free and you pay for the EC2 instances and other resources it creates.

1710
02:26:10,350 --> 02:26:16,868
这是本模块中考试最常考的一对对比。使用 CloudFormation 时，你描述的是基础设施。
This is the pair the exam returns to most in this module. With CloudFormation, you describe the infrastructure.

1711
02:26:17,424 --> 02:26:23,844
任何排列组合的 AWS 资源，只要由你决定架构且输入是模板，就是基础设施即代码。
Any AWS resource in any arrangement with you deciding the architecture and the input is a template.

1712
02:26:24,430 --> 02:26:27,204
使用 Elastic Beanstalk 时，你提供的是应用程序。
With Elastic Beanstalk, you provide the application.

1713
02:26:28,078 --> 02:26:34,852
AWS 决定架构，为你提供标准的 Web 应用环境，而你的输入是代码。
AWS decides the architecture, gives you a standard web application environment, and the input is your code.

1714
02:26:35,278 --> 02:26:38,724
“将任何基础设施定义为代码”意味着 CloudFormation。
Define any infrastructure as code means cloud formation.

1715
02:26:39,790 --> 02:26:44,164
“上传一个应用并让 AWS 来运行它”意味着 Beanstalk。
Upload an application and let AWS run it means Beanstalk.

1716
02:26:45,742 --> 02:26:48,356
三种部署模型以及考试中的相关名称。
Three deployment models and the exam names.

1717
02:26:48,718 --> 02:26:49,380
这三项都要掌握。
All three.

1718
02:26:49,904 --> 02:26:54,116
“云”意味着所有内容都在云端运行，无论是新构建的还是完全迁移过来的。
Cloud means everything runs in the cloud, either built there or fully migrated.

1719
02:26:54,702 --> 02:26:59,140
“混合云”意味着部分工作负载在云端，一部分在本地部署并连接在一起。
Hybrid means some workloads in the cloud and some on-premises connected together.

1720
02:27:00,046 --> 02:27:05,572
“本地部署”意味着所有内容都留在你自己的数据中心，这有时被称为私有云。
On-premises means everything stays in your own data center, which is sometimes called private cloud.

1721
02:27:06,382 --> 02:27:13,664
“混合云”出现的频率最高，因为法规要求和遗留系统导致部分工作负载在本地保留多年。
Hybrid is the one that appears most because regulation and legacy systems keep some workloads at home for years.

1722
02:27:14,926 --> 02:27:22,756
有四个服务用于连接混合环境，在网络模块正式讲解之前，把它们放在一起看有助于理解。
Four services connect a hybrid environment and it helps to see them together before the networking module covers them properly.

1723
02:27:23,150 --> 02:27:29,220
站点到站点 VPN 通过互联网加密将你的网络连接到 VPC。
Site-to-site VPN connects your network to a VPC over the Internet encrypted.

1724
02:27:29,902 --> 02:27:34,596
Direct Connect 提供具有稳定带宽的专用私有链路。
Direct Connect provides a dedicated private link with consistent bandwidth.

1725
02:27:35,246 --> 02:27:44,260
Outpost 将 AWS 硬件放入你自己的数据中心，而存储网关让本地部署系统能够访问 AWS 存储。
Outpost puts AWS hardware in your own data center, and storage gateway gives on-premises systems access to AWS storage.

1726
02:27:45,198 --> 02:27:47,780
通过互联网快速且廉价的意味着 VPN。
Quick and cheap over the internet means VPM.

1727
02:27:48,910 --> 02:27:51,524
稳定且私有的意味着 Direct Connect。
Consistent and private means direct connect.

1728
02:27:53,198 --> 02:27:54,116
工作场景题。
Work scenario.

1729
02:27:54,143 --> 02:27:59,812
1. 一家公司在每次发布前，通过控制台手动创建测试环境。
1. A company creates a test environment by hand in the console before each release.

1730
02:28:00,398 --> 02:28:04,548
工程师报告称，测试环境经常与生产环境在一些细节上不一致。
Engineers report the test environment frequently differs from production in small ways.

1731
02:28:05,518 --> 02:28:09,924
最近的一次故障被追溯到其中一个环境存在但另一个不存在的安全组规则。
A recent outage was traced to a security group rule present in one but not the other.

1732
02:28:10,830 --> 02:28:16,804
该公司希望测试环境能与生产环境完全匹配，并且在之后可以被销毁。
The company wants test environments that match production exactly and can be destroyed afterwards.

1733
02:28:17,326 --> 02:28:18,596
停下来做决定。
Pause and decide.

1734
02:28:24,814 --> 02:28:33,060
答案是 A。选项 C 是一个有趣的干扰项，因为编写 CLI 脚本确实比在控制台中点击操作更高效。
The answer is A. Option C is the interesting distractor because scripting the CLI is a genuine improvement over clicking in the console.

1735
02:28:33,344 --> 02:28:41,444
它无法解决的问题是：仍然由人来运行命令，仍可能漏掉某一项，且文档也会随着时间的推移而与现状脱节。
What it does not fix is that a person still runs the commands and can still skip one and the documentation drifts from reality over time.

1736
02:28:42,446 --> 02:28:45,284
CloudFormation 则能将人完全从这个过程中剔除。
Cloud formation removes the person from the loop entirely.

1737
02:28:45,614 --> 02:28:48,804
选项 D 又是关于治理和合规性的区分。
And option D is the governance and compliance split again.

1738
02:28:49,934 --> 02:28:52,132
Config 会告诉你环境之间存在差异。
Config would tell you the environments differ.

1739
02:28:52,590 --> 02:28:54,564
但公司要求它们不能有差异。
The company wants them not to differ.

1740
02:28:56,206 --> 02:28:57,156
动词场景题。
Verb scenario.

1741
02:28:57,228 --> 02:29:06,020
2. 一个小团队编写了一个 Python Web 应用程序。他们希望在 AWS 上运行，并配备负载均衡器和自动扩展功能。
2. A small team has written a Python web application. They want it running on AWS with a load balancer and automatic scaling.

1742
02:29:06,638 --> 02:29:11,364
没人有基础设施经验，而且他们不想设计架构。
Nobody has infrastructure experience and they do not want to design an architecture.

1743
02:29:13,166 --> 02:29:16,964
但他们确实希望在需要时能够调整实例类型。
They do want the ability to adjust the instance type later if needed.

1744
02:29:17,838 --> 02:29:19,652
他们应该使用哪种服务？
Which service should they use?

1745
02:29:20,302 --> 02:29:21,572
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1746
02:29:27,790 --> 02:29:29,424
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

1747
02:29:29,838 --> 02:29:34,276
题干中的两个条款分别排除了两个最强的备选项。
Two clauses in the stem eliminate the two strongest alternatives, one each.

1748
02:29:34,624 --> 02:29:45,156
他们不想设计架构，这排除了 CloudFormation；他们想在以后调整实例类型，而由于无服务器没有可调整的实例类型，所以排除了 Lambda。
They do not want to design an architecture which rules out cloud formation, and they want to adjust the instance type later, which rules out lambda, since serverless has no instance type to adjust.

1749
02:29:46,062 --> 02:29:51,428
第二个条款很容易被忽略，但它起到了关键的作用。
That second clause is easy to skim past and it is doing deliberate work.

1750
02:29:52,973 --> 02:30:00,944
Elastic Beanstalk 正好处于两者之间，它提供了一个构建好的环境，同时让资源保持可见且可调节。
Beanstalk sits precisely between the two, giving you a built environment while leaving the resources visible and adjustable.

1751
02:30:02,606 --> 02:30:03,812
动词场景 3。
Verb scenario 3.

1752
02:30:04,064 --> 02:30:08,900
一名运维工程师必须在每天晚上关闭分布在多个账户中的 300 个 EC2 实例。
An operations engineer must drop 300 EC2 instances across several accounts each evening.

1753
02:30:09,454 --> 02:30:11,172
他们必须在每天早上重新启动这些实例。
They must start again each morning.

1754
02:30:11,950 --> 02:30:14,468
实例标识符是已知且稳定的。
The instance identifiers are known and stable.

1755
02:30:14,926 --> 02:30:17,508
该任务必须在无人值守的情况下运行。
The task must run without anyone being present.

1756
02:30:18,126 --> 02:30:20,004
哪种方法最合适？
Which approach is most appropriate?

1757
02:30:20,878 --> 02:30:22,212
因果判断并决定。
Cause and decide.

1758
02:30:28,304 --> 02:30:29,744
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

1759
02:30:30,064 --> 02:30:32,144
这个场景区分了两个概念。
This scenario separates two things.

1760
02:30:32,462 --> 02:30:33,828
人们往往会把它们混淆。
People blur together.

1761
02:30:34,144 --> 02:30:37,664
CloudFormation 定义的是什么基础设施应该存在。
Cloud formation describes what infrastructure should exist.

1762
02:30:38,158 --> 02:30:42,864
CLI 对已经存在的基础设施执行操作。
The CLI performs operations on infrastructure that already exist.

1763
02:30:43,694 --> 02:30:51,556
启动和停止实例是一种操作，而不是一种描述。所以选项 C 是类别错误，而不仅仅是服务选择错误。
Starting and stopping instances is an operation, not a description. So option C is the wrong category rather than the wrong service.

1764
02:30:51,984 --> 02:30:58,980
而且「在无人值守的情况下」这个短语明确表达了自动化要求，这立刻排除了控制台。
And the phrase without anyone being present is the automation requirement stated plainly, which eliminates the console immediately.

1765
02:31:00,558 --> 02:31:02,148
工作场景 4。
Worked scenario 4.

1766
02:31:02,702 --> 02:31:06,180
一家制造商正将大部分工作负载迁移到 AWS。
A manufacturer is moving most workloads to AWS.

1767
02:31:06,734 --> 02:31:12,484
但监管机构要求其质量记录系统在自己的数据中心保留 3 年。
But a regulator requires its quality record system to stay in its own data center for 3 more years.

1768
02:31:13,006 --> 02:31:17,700
该系统必须与目前在 AWS 上运行的应用程序持续交换数据。
That system must exchange data continuously with applications now running in AWS.

1769
02:31:18,542 --> 02:31:23,044
公司希望在这两者之间获得一致且可预测的网络性能。
The company wants consistent, predictable network performance between the two.

1770
02:31:23,662 --> 02:31:24,900
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

1771
02:31:31,022 --> 02:31:32,384
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

1772
02:31:33,070 --> 02:31:35,556
这个问题有两个部分，对应的选项也有两个部分。
This question has two halves and option.

1773
02:31:36,206 --> 02:31:39,716
D 项对其中一个正确，这让它成为了最强的干扰项。
D gets one of them right, which makes it the strongest distractor.

1774
02:31:41,518 --> 02:31:47,236
因为工作负载在两个地方运行，所以 B 和 D 的部署模型都是混合云。
The deployment model is hybrid in both B and D because workloads run in both places.

1775
02:31:47,504 --> 02:31:49,444
区分它们的是连接方式。
The connection is what separates them.

1776
02:31:50,414 --> 02:31:56,388
点对点的 VPN 运行在公共互联网上，因此其性能随网络状况而变化。
A side-to-side VPN runs over the public internet, so its performance varies with internet conditions.

1777
02:31:57,070 --> 02:32:02,308
Direct Connect 是专用的私有链路，这正是“稳定且可预测”的含义。
Direct connect is a dedicated private link, which is what consistent and predictable means.

1778
02:32:02,830 --> 02:32:05,796
注意那些只有一部分不同的双重选项。
Watch for two-part answers where only one part differs.

1779
02:32:07,406 --> 02:32:08,196
总结一下：
To recap,

1780
02:32:10,062 --> 02:32:10,532
1。
1.

1781
02:32:11,182 --> 02:32:13,104
具有四个接口的 API。
API with four interfaces.

1782
02:32:13,390 --> 02:32:22,948
“人”指的是控制台，“脚本”指 CLI，“应用程序”指 SDK，CloudFormation 用于描述基础设施，而 Elastic Beanstalk 用来运行你的应用。
A person means the console, a script means the CLI, an application means an SDK, cloud formation describes infrastructure while Beanstalk runs your application.

1783
02:32:23,184 --> 02:32:26,628
CDK 是生成 CloudFormation 而不是取代它。
The CDK generates cloud formation rather than replacing it.

1784
02:32:27,374 --> 02:32:33,860
“可重复的”、“相同的”、“无人为错误”以及“事后销毁”，这些都是 CloudFormation 的关键词。
Repeatable, identical, no human error, and destroy afterwards are all cloud formation phrases.

1785
02:32:34,544 --> 02:32:40,836
还要记住，描述基础设施和运营现有基础设施是两件不同的工作。
And remember that describing infrastructure and operating existing infrastructure are different jobs.

1786
02:32:42,606 --> 02:32:46,660
进入下一个模块：计算，这是课程中占比最大的部分。
Next module, compute, which is the largest in the course.

1787
02:32:47,904 --> 02:32:55,876
这是课程中最大的模块，在题库分析中，计算类题目占所有题目的 34%，是最大的类别。
This is the largest module in the course, and compute was the largest cluster in the bank analysis at 34% of all questions.

1788
02:32:56,224 --> 02:33:04,804
它包含 8 个实战案例而不是 4 个，因为在“计算”这个领域，考核的技能是“选择”而非单纯的知识。
It also has eight worked scenarios rather than four because compute is a domain where the skill being tested is selection rather than knowledge.

1789
02:33:06,094 --> 02:33:09,956
在这场考试中，每一个关于计算的决策背后都对应着一个问题。
There is one question underneath every compute decision on this exam.

1790
02:33:10,224 --> 02:33:12,420
你想管理多少比例的堆栈？
How much of the stack do you want to manage?

1791
02:33:12,686 --> 02:33:15,556
在这一端，你自己运行操作系统。
At one end, you run the operating system yourself.

1792
02:33:15,744 --> 02:33:20,292
在另一端，你交给 AWS 一个函数，再也不用考虑服务器了。
At the other, you hand AWS a function and never think about a server again.

1793
02:33:21,134 --> 02:33:28,196
本模块中的每个服务都处于这条线的某个位置，而场景描述总是会告诉你公司想要达到什么目标。
Every service in this module sits somewhere on that line, and the scenario always tells you where the company wants to be.

1794
02:33:29,806 --> 02:33:31,908
这里有一张表展示这个光谱。
Here is the spectrum in one table.

1795
02:33:32,080 --> 02:33:41,540
在 EC2 上，你负责管理操作系统、补丁、扩展和容量，而 AWS 管理硬件和虚拟机管理程序。
On EC2, you manage the operating system, patching, scaling, and capacity, while AWS manages hardware and the hypervisor.

1796
02:33:42,240 --> 02:33:45,668
在 EC2 上使用容器时，你仍然需要管理主机。
With containers on EC2, you still manage the hosts.

1797
02:33:46,894 --> 02:33:50,276
使用 Fargate 时，你只负责管理容器镜像。
With Fargate, you manage only the container images.

1798
02:33:51,246 --> 02:33:56,676
使用 Elastic Beanstalk 时，你提供应用程序代码；而使用 Lambda 时，你只提供一个函数，别无他物。
With Elastic Beanstalk, you provide application code and with Lambda you provide a function and nothing else.

1799
02:33:56,960 --> 02:34:03,040
阅读中间那一列，你会看到它在变短。随着长度缩短，运维开销降低，但你的控制权也会相应减少。
Read the middle column and watch it shorten. As it does, operational overhead falls, and so does your control.

1800
02:34:04,622 --> 02:34:11,396
EC2 提供虚拟服务器，你可以选择操作系统、尺寸和网络放置。
EC2 provides virtual servers where you choose the operating system, the size, and the network placement.

1801
02:34:12,160 --> 02:34:19,680
你负责客户操作系统以及安装在上面的所有内容，就像在模块中提到的那样。
You are responsible for the guest operating system and everything installed on it, exactly as covered in module life.

1802
02:34:20,270 --> 02:34:24,708
大多数 Linux 实例按秒计费，最少计费时间为 60 秒。
Billing is per second for most Linux instances with a 60 second minimum.

1803
02:34:24,960 --> 02:34:30,596
停止实例会停止计算费用，但挂载的 EBS 存储仍需付费。
Stopping an instance stops the compute charge, but attached EBS storage still costs money.

1804
02:34:30,880 --> 02:34:34,020
注意“停止”和“终止”之间的区别。
And note the difference between stopping and terminating.

1805
02:34:37,198 --> 02:34:39,236
停止会保留实例。
Stopping preserves the instance.

1806
02:34:39,886 --> 02:34:41,380
终止会销毁它。
Terminating destroys it.

1807
02:34:43,086 --> 02:34:46,320
实例系列根据它们擅长的功能对实例进行分组。
Instance families group instances by what they are good at.

1808
02:34:46,638 --> 02:34:50,052
通用型平衡了计算、内存和网络。
General purpose balances compute, memory, and networking.

1809
02:34:50,958 --> 02:34:54,084
计算优化型适用于处理密集型任务。
Compute optimized suits processor heavy work.

1810
02:34:54,702 --> 02:34:57,796
内存优化型适用于大型数据和高内存需求的数据集。
Memory optimized suits large and memory data sets.

1811
02:34:58,414 --> 02:35:01,252
存储优化型适用于高本地磁盘吞吐量。
Storage optimized suits high local disk throughput.

1812
02:35:02,030 --> 02:35:04,720
加速计算提供 GPU 支持。
An accelerated computing provides GPS.

1813
02:35:04,960 --> 02:35:10,628
你不需要记住具体的类型名称或规格，只需要根据瓶颈情况匹配到对应的系列即可。
You are not expected to know type names or specifications only to match a bottleneck to a family.

1814
02:35:10,926 --> 02:35:19,556
Amazon machine image 是实例启动时使用的模板，它是区域性的，因此将其复制到其他地方是需要刻意操作的一步。
An Amazon machine image is the template an instance launches from and it is regional, so copying it elsewhere is a deliberate step.

1815
02:35:20,782 --> 02:35:26,596
EC2 和 Lambda 是光谱的两端，考试中会不断对比这两者。
EC2 and Lambda are the two ends of the spectrum and the exam contrasts them constantly.

1816
02:35:26,926 --> 02:35:32,452
EC2 在你停止它之前一直运行，并支持任何运行时环境或软件。
EC2 runs continuously until you stop it and supports any runtime or software.

1817
02:35:32,720 --> 02:35:36,356
无论你是否使用它，它都会按运行时间计费。
It bills for the time it runs, whether you use it or not.

1818
02:35:37,134 --> 02:35:43,108
Lambda 在被触发时运行，并在每次调用中最多持续 15 分钟后停止。
Lambda runs when something triggers it and then stops with a maximum of 15 minutes per invocation.

1819
02:35:43,886 --> 02:35:47,972
没有需要打补丁的服务器，且按请求次数和时长计费。
There are no servers to patch and billing is per request and duration.

1820
02:35:48,320 --> 02:35:51,760
“持续运行”或“超过 15 分钟”意味着 EC2。
Continuous or longer than 15 minutes means EC2.

1821
02:35:52,334 --> 02:35:54,628
“事件驱动型”且“短时间”意味着 Lambda。
Event driven and short means lambda.

1822
02:35:56,238 --> 02:36:00,560
Lambda 的约束条件是决定题目关键点所在的地方，所以要准确掌握它们。
Lambda's constraints are what decide questions, so learn them precisely.

1823
02:36:01,518 --> 02:36:06,756
单次调用最长只能持续 15 分钟，更长时间的任务需要其他方案。
15 minutes is the hard maximum for a single invocation, and longer work needs something else.

1824
02:36:07,086 --> 02:36:11,556
它可以在无需配置的情况下，自动从零扩展到多个并发执行。
It scales automatically from zero to many concurrent executions with no configuration.

1825
02:36:12,494 --> 02:36:17,668
在不运行时不产生任何费用，非常适合突发或不频繁的工作负载。
You pay nothing when it is not running, which suits spiky or infrequent workloads.

1826
02:36:17,998 --> 02:36:26,436
它可以通过 S3 上传、API 网关请求、EventBridge 定时任务、队列消息等多种来源触发。
It is triggered by S3 uploads, API, gateway requests, event bridge schedules, queue messages, and many other sources.

1827
02:36:26,640 --> 02:36:30,948
而且它是无状态的，所以任何必须持久保存的数据都得放在别处。
And it is stateless, so anything that must persist goes elsewhere.

1828
02:36:32,238 --> 02:36:35,364
三种容器服务，各有不同的职能。
Three container services with three distinct jobs.

1829
02:36:35,790 --> 02:36:42,148
ECS 是 AWS 自家的容器编排器，更简单且与 AWS 深度集成。
ECS is AWS's own container orchestrator, simpler and deeply integrated with AWS.

1830
02:36:42,510 --> 02:36:47,524
EKS 是托管的 Kubernetes，当你明确要求使用 Kubernetes 时就选择它。
EKS is Managed Kubernetes and you choose it when Kubernetes specifically is required.

1831
02:36:48,430 --> 02:36:54,880
ECR 是存储容器镜像的注册表，它不负责任何编排工作。
ECR is the registry where container images are stored and it orchestrates nothing at all.

1832
02:36:55,182 --> 02:37:06,948
ECS 和 EKS 都可以运行在您管理的 EC2 实例或 Fargate 上。在关于运行容器的题目中，要注意 ECR 作为干扰项。它只负责存储镜像。
Both ECS and EKS can run on EC2 instances you manage or on Fargate. Watch for ECR as a distractor in questions about running containers. It only stores images.

1833
02:37:08,686 --> 02:37:13,732
ECS 和 EKS 都运行容器，两者的区别很简单。
ECS and EKS both run containers and the separator is simple.

1834
02:37:14,190 --> 02:37:26,160
ECS 是 AWS 自家的编排器，操作更简单、集成度高，且不需要 Kubernetes 知识。EKS 是托管的 Kubernetes，为您提供标准的、可移植的 Kubernetes。
ECS is AWS's own orchestrator, simpler to operate, tightly integrated, and needing no Kubernetes knowledge. EKS is managed Kubernetes, giving you the standard portable Kubernetes.

1835
02:37:26,320 --> 02:37:29,348
API 展示了现有的工具链和技能迁移。
API show existing tooling and skills transfer.

1836
02:37:29,966 --> 02:37:39,204
考试在这里的题目非常直接。如果场景中提到 Kubernetes，或者提到现有的 Kubernetes 技能或工作负载，就选 EKS。
The exam is unusually direct here. If the scenario says Kubernetes or mentions existing Kubernetes skills or workloads, choose EKS.

1837
02:37:39,694 --> 02:37:41,892
否则，默认选择 ECS。
Otherwise, ECS is the default.

1838
02:37:43,406 --> 02:37:47,568
Fargate 和 EC2 启动类型是运行相同容器的两种方式。
Fargate and the EC2 launch type are two ways to run the same containers.

1839
02:37:47,982 --> 02:37:51,108
使用 Fargate 时，无需去配置或打补丁实例。
With Fargate, there are no instances to provision or patch.

1840
02:37:51,470 --> 02:37:57,380
您只需为每个任务请求的资源付费，AWS 会完全处理容量问题。
You pay for the resources each task requests, and AWS handles capacity entirely.

1841
02:37:57,728 --> 02:38:02,084
使用 EC2 启动类型时，您需要自己去配置并打补丁实例。
With the EC2 launch type, you provision and patch the instances yourself.

1842
02:38:02,990 --> 02:38:08,932
无论实例处于繁忙还是闲置状态，您都要为其付费，但您可以控制实例类型和放置位置。
You pay for them whether busy or idle and keep control over instance type and placement.

1843
02:38:09,422 --> 02:38:11,556
无需管理服务器意味着选择 Fargate。
No servers to manage means far gate.

1844
02:38:12,048 --> 02:38:17,408
需要主机控制权或已有已支付费用的容量，则意味着选择 EC2。
Needing host control or having capacity you already pay for means EC2.

1845
02:38:18,958 --> 02:38:23,876
当出现明确信号时，会出现这两个特定的答案。
Two specialized answers that appear when their exact signal is present.

1846
02:38:24,368 --> 02:38:32,288
AWS Batch 用于运行大量的批处理计算作业，自动提供计算资源并排队工作。
AWS Batch runs large numbers of batch computing jobs, provisioning compute automatically and queuing the work.

1847
02:38:32,528 --> 02:38:38,884
它的识别信号是：一夜之间处理数千个任务，或者进行科学和金融计算。
Its signal is thousands of jobs overnight processing or scientific and financial computation.

1848
02:38:39,630 --> 02:38:50,820
Amazon LightSail 是简化版的虚拟专用服务器，具有可预测的月度价格，将计算、存储和网络捆绑在一起，并提供如 WordPress 等预配置好的蓝图。
Amazon LightSail is a simplified virtual private server with a predictable monthly price, bundling compute, storage, and networking with pre-configured blueprints such as WordPress.

1849
02:38:51,470 --> 02:38:57,220
它的识别信号是：简单的应用程序、小型团队，以及希望避免 AWS 复杂性的需求。
Its signal is a simple application, a small team, and a wish to avoid AWS complexity.

1850
02:38:58,670 --> 02:38:59,328
EC2。
EC2.

1851
02:38:59,726 --> 02:39:05,568
自动扩容在设定的最小和最大范围内增加或减少实例以匹配需求。
Autoscaling adds and removes instances to match demand within a minimum and maximum use set.

1852
02:39:05,968 --> 02:39:12,356
它还会自动替换不健康的实例，这使其既是可靠性功能，也是成本控制功能。
It also replaces unhealthy instances automatically, which makes it a reliability feature as much as a cost one.

1853
02:39:13,088 --> 02:39:20,368
动态扩容响应于指标；计划扩容遵循已知模式；预测性扩容则预估需求。
Dynamic scaling responds to a metric. Scheduled scaling follows a known pattern and predictive scaling forecast demand.

1854
02:39:20,558 --> 02:39:25,604
它与弹性负载均衡配合使用，因此新实例会自动接收流量。
It works with elastic load balancing so new instances receive traffic automatically.

1855
02:39:25,968 --> 02:39:31,204
记住第一章的规则：自动扩容改变的是数量，而不是尺寸。
And remember the rule from module 1: auto scaling changes the count, never the size.

1856
02:39:32,782 --> 02:39:37,380
弹性负载均衡有四种类型，其中两种涵盖了几乎所有的题目。
Elastic load balancing has four types and two of them carry almost all the questions.

1857
02:39:37,648 --> 02:39:45,092
应用负载均衡器工作在第七层，支持基于路径或主机的 HTTP 和 HTTPS 路由。
The application load balancer works at layer 7 with HTTP and HTTPS routing on path or hostname.

1858
