02:50:29,518 --> 02:50:30,176
OneNote。
OneNote.

1988
02:50:30,830 --> 02:50:34,500
购买选项是在第 18 模块讲解的，而不是在这里。
The purchase options are taught in module 18 rather than here.

1989
02:50:35,246 --> 02:50:36,932
下一个模块：存储。
Next module storage.

1990
02:50:38,702 --> 02:50:42,180
关于存储的问题通常由两点决定。
Storage questions are usually decided by two things.

1991
02:50:42,830 --> 02:50:47,748
工作负载需要哪种形态的存储，以及数据被读取的频率。
Which shape of storage the workload needs and how often the data will be read.

1992
02:50:48,398 --> 02:50:52,740
只要搞清楚这两点，这个模块的大部分题目都能迎刃而解。
Get those two right and most of this module answers itself.

1993
02:50:54,414 --> 02:50:57,860
有三种类型的存储，它们并不是可以互换的。
There are three shapes of storage and they are not interchangeable.

1994
02:50:58,336 --> 02:51:03,012
对象存储是可以通过名称通过 HTTP 获取的完整项目。
Object storage holds whole items retrieved by name over HTTP.

1995
02:51:03,616 --> 02:51:06,820
块存储就像是连接到一台机器上的磁盘。
Block storage looks like a disk attached to one machine.

1996
02:51:07,406 --> 02:51:12,176
文件存储看起来像是许多机器都可以挂载的共享文件夹。
File storage looks like a shared folder that many machines can mount.

1997
02:51:12,718 --> 02:51:21,124
为一种类型编写的应用程序通常在不重写的情况下无法使用另一种，这就是为什么考试非常强调这个区别的原因。
An application written for one cannot usually use another without being rewritten, which is why the exam leans on this distinction so heavily.

1998
02:51:22,862 --> 02:51:24,507
三种形态对应三个答案。
Three shapes and three answers.

1999
02:51:25,267 --> 02:51:30,747
对象存储意味着通过 HTTP 按名称获取的项目，即 Amazon S3。
Object storage means items fetched by name over HTTP which is Amazon S3.

2000
02:51:31,278 --> 02:51:36,736
块存储意味着连接到一台机器的磁盘，即 EBS 或实例存储。
Block storage means a disk attached to one machine, which is EBS or an instance store.

2001
02:51:37,136 --> 02:51:43,076
文件存储意味着许多机器挂载的共享文件夹，即 EFS 或 FSX。
File storage means a shared folder that many machines mount, which is EFS or FSX.

2002
02:51:43,886 --> 02:51:46,948
这是能帮你拿分的排除法。
Here is the elimination rule that earns marks.

2003
02:51:47,296 --> 02:51:55,876
如果应用必须在不修改的情况下挂载文件系统，那么无论 S3 的价格看起来多诱人，它都不是选项。
If an application must mount a file system without being modified, S3 is out, however attractive its price looks.

2004
02:51:57,358 --> 02:52:00,336
在 S3 中，对象存放在存储桶中。
In S3, objects live in buckets.

2005
02:52:00,656 --> 02:52:08,452
存储桶名称是全球唯一的，但存储桶本身位于一个区域，这是第 10 模块中值得重复强调的细节。
Bucket names are globally unique, but the bucket itself lives in one region, which is the detail from module 10 worth repeating.

2006
02:52:09,518 --> 02:52:15,076
它通过在至少 3 个可用区冗余存储数据，提供 11 个 9 的持久性。
It offers 11 9s of durability by storing data redundantly across at least 3.

2007
02:52:16,654 --> 02:52:18,180
可用区。
Availability zones.

2008
02:52:19,054 --> 02:52:23,376
存储空间实际上是无限的，单个对象可以高达 5TB。
Storage is effectively unlimited, and a single object can be up to 5TB.

2009
02:52:24,334 --> 02:52:29,540
版本控制保留之前的副本，而对象锁定能让对象变得不可变以符合合规性要求。
Versioning keeps previous copies and object lock makes objects immutable for compliance.

2010
02:52:30,702 --> 02:52:33,936
但它不是文件系统，无法被挂载。
But it is not a file system and cannot be mounted.

2011
02:52:35,214 --> 02:52:37,732
这两个数字被混淆了，其实不该混淆。
Two numbers that get merged and should not be.

2012
02:52:38,222 --> 02:52:45,764
持久性是问数据是否依然存在，对于 S3 来说，几乎所有类别都是 119s。
Durability asks whether the data will still exist, and for S3, that is 119s across almost every class.

2013
02:52:46,734 --> 02:52:52,772
可用性是问你现在能不能访问到它，这才是不同类别之间的真正区别。
Availability asks whether you can reach it right now, and that is where the classes genuinely differ.

2014
02:52:53,646 --> 02:52:58,336
这一点很重要，因为单可用区类别的持久性在正常运行下并不更差。
This matters because one zone classes do not have worse durability in normal operation.

2015
02:52:58,496 --> 02:53:01,156
它们将数据存储在单个可用区中。
They store the data in a single availability zone.

2016
02:53:01,518 --> 02:53:06,500
如果该可用区不可用，你就无法访问数据；如果它被毁坏，数据就丢失了。
If that zone is unavailable, you cannot reach your data, and if it is destroyed, the data is gone.

2017
02:53:07,950 --> 02:53:11,460
这 7 个类别是按读取数据的频率排序的。
7 classes ordered by how often you read the data.

2018
02:53:12,016 --> 02:53:13,924
标准型适用于频繁访问。
Standard for frequent access.

2019
02:53:15,982 --> 02:53:16,896
智能型。
Intelligent.

2020
02:53:17,136 --> 02:53:23,524
分层存储适用于访问模式未知或不断变化的情况，因为 AWS 会自动帮你跨层移动对象。
Tiering when the access pattern is unknown or changing because AWS moves objects between tiers for you.

2021
02:53:23,856 --> 02:53:29,056
标准低频访问适用于仍需毫秒级响应但很少被读取的数据。
Standard infrequent access for data still needed in milliseconds but read rarely.

2022
02:53:29,582 --> 02:53:30,372
单可用区。
One zone.

2023
02:53:55,856 --> 02:53:56,256
两者。
Both

2024
02:53:56,256 --> 02:54:00,836
这两者都会自动移动数据，考试会根据“谁来决定”来区分它们。
of these move data automatically, and the exam separates them on who decides.

2025
02:54:03,182 --> 02:54:03,904
智能型。
Intelligent.

2026
02:54:04,526 --> 02:54:12,900
分层存储会监控实际访问情况并为你移动对象，每项对象收取少量的监控费，但在其内部层级之间切换时没有检索费。
Tiering observes actual access and moves objects for you, charging a small monitoring fee per object but no retrieval fees between its tiers.

2027
02:54:13,806 --> 02:54:22,948
生命周期策略会在你指定的若干天后转换对象且不收取监控费，但你必须提前知道规律。
A life cycle policy transitions objects after a number of days that you specify with no monitoring charge, but you must know the pattern in advance.

2028
02:54:23,424 --> 02:54:26,916
未知或不可预测的访问意味着智能型。
Unknown or unpredictable access means intelligent.

2029
02:54:28,014 --> 02:54:28,704
分层存储。
Tiering.

2030
02:54:29,774 --> 02:54:32,644
基于已知年龄规则的规则意味着生命周期策略。
A known age-based rule means a life cycle policy.

2031
02:54:34,254 --> 02:54:37,504
一个 EBS 卷连接到一台 EC2 实例。
An EBS volume attaches to one EC2 instance.

2032
02:54:37,664 --> 02:54:47,268
它必须位于与该实例相同的可用区，这是一个硬性约束条件。它独立于实例存在，所以终止实例并不需要销毁卷。
It must sit in the same availability zone as that instance, which is a hard constraint. It persists independently of the instance, so terminating the instance need not destroy the volume.

2033
02:54:48,142 --> 02:54:54,756
SSD 类型适用于数据库和启动卷，而 HDD 类型适合大容量顺序吞吐量。
SSD types suit databases and boot volumes, while HDD types suit large sequential throughput.

2034
02:54:55,104 --> 02:54:59,588
卷可以使用 KMS 进行加密，且快照会继承该加密。
Volumes can be encrypted with KMS and snapshots inherit that encryption.

2035
02:55:00,078 --> 02:55:04,452
并且记住，停止的实例仍会产生其挂载存储的费用。
And remember that a stopped instance still builds for its attached storage.

2036
02:55:05,998 --> 02:55:11,104
EBS 和实例存储都是块存储，区别在于生存能力。
EBS and instance store are both block storage and the difference is survival.

2037
02:55:11,424 --> 02:55:19,364
EBS 是网络连接的，独立于实例存在，可以分离和重新挂载，并且可以快照到 S3。
EBS is network attached, possessed independently of the instance, can be detached and reattached, and can be snapshotted to S3.

2038
02:55:20,384 --> 02:55:24,100
实例存储在物理上连接到主机，所以速度非常快。
Instance store is physically attached to the host, so it is very fast.

2039
02:55:25,104 --> 02:55:30,276
但当实例停止时数据就会丢失，且它无法被分离或创建快照。
But the data is lost when the instance stops and it cannot be detached or snapshotted.

2040
02:55:30,638 --> 02:55:33,028
任何你重视的数据都应该放在 EBS 上。
Anything you care about goes on EBS.

2041
02:55:34,144 --> 02:55:37,508
实例存储用于缓存、缓冲和临时数据。
Instance store is for caches, buffers, and scratch data.

2042
02:55:38,862 --> 02:55:43,744
快照是存储在 Amazon S3 中的卷的特定时间点备份。
A snapshot is a point-in-time backup of a volume stored in Amazon S3.

2043
02:55:44,144 --> 02:55:51,364
快照是增量的，因此只存储自上次快照以来发生变化的块，这让它们成本很低。
Snapshots are incremental, so only the blocks changed since the last snapshot are stored, which keeps them cheap.

2044
02:55:52,046 --> 02:55:57,796
它们可以复制到另一个区域，这就是 EBS 数据跨越区域边界的方式。
They can be copied to another region, and that is how EBS data crosses a region boundary.

2045
02:55:58,286 --> 02:56:03,344
从快照创建的新卷可以放置在不同的可用区。
A new volume created from a snapshot can be placed in a different availability zone.

2046
02:56:03,694 --> 02:56:08,324
这是移动卷的标准方法，因为卷本身是无法移动的。
That is the standard way to move a volume since volumes themselves cannot move.

2047
02:56:09,902 --> 02:56:14,340
两者都提供共享文件存储，协议决定使用哪一个。
Both provide shared file storage and the protocol decides between them.

2048
02:56:14,926 --> 02:56:24,836
EFS 可以通过 NFS 同时被多个 Linux 实例挂载，能够自动扩缩容，并跨越多个可用区。
EFS is mounted by many Linux instances at once using NFS, grows and shrinks automatically, and spans multiple availability zones.

2049
02:56:25,550 --> 02:56:27,197
FSX 有不同的变体。
FSX comes in variants.

2050
02:56:28,302 --> 02:56:35,492
FSX for Windows File Server 支持 SMB 并支持包括 Active Directory 在内的原生 Windows 功能。
FSX for Windows File Server speaks SMB and supports native Windows features including Active Directory.

2051
02:56:35,854 --> 02:56:39,424
FSX for Lustre 为高性能计算提供服务。
FSX for Lustre serves high performance computing.

2052
02:56:39,598 --> 02:56:45,988
Linux 和 NFS 代表 EFS。Windows 和 SMB 代表 FSX for Windows File Server。
Linux and NFS means EFS. Windows and SMB means FSX for Windows File Server.

2053
02:56:47,630 --> 02:56:55,984
存储网关让本地部署系统通过它们熟悉的协议访问 Azure 存储，这就是它作为混合
Storage gateway gives on-premises systems access to Adzebur storage using protocols they already speak, which is what makes it a hybrid

2054
02:56:56,224 --> 02:56:56,548
服务的原因。
service.

2055
02:56:57,582 --> 02:57:01,508
文件网关将 S3 展示为 NFS 或 SMB 共享。
File gateway presents S3 as an NFS or SMB share.

2056
02:57:02,350 --> 02:57:07,716
卷网关提供由 S3 支持的、通过 iSCSI 的块存储。
Volume gateway presents block storage over ISCCSI backed by S3.

2057
02:57:08,462 --> 02:57:14,212
而磁带网关则用由 S3 和 Glacier 存储类别支持的服务来替代物理磁带库。
And Tape Gateway replaces a physical tape library backed by S3 and the Glacier classes.

2058
02:57:14,704 --> 02:57:19,140
关键信号是始终存在且无法更改的本地部署系统。
The signal is always an existing on-premises system that cannot be changed.

2059
02:57:19,744 --> 02:57:23,876
特别是磁带网关，是替换磁带备份的明确标志。
Tape gateway in particular is the giveaway for replacing tape backups.

2060
02:57:25,486 --> 02:57:33,264
AWS Backup 从单一位置集中管理 EBS、RDS、Dynamo DB、EFS、FSX 等的备份
AWS backup centralizes backup across EBS, RDS, Dynamo DB, EFS, FSX and more

2061
02:57:33,424 --> 02:57:34,564
。
from a single place.

2062
02:57:35,438 --> 02:57:39,652
备份计划定义了计划和保留期，并可应用于整个组织。
Backup plans define schedule and retention and can apply across an organization.

2063
02:57:40,590 --> 02:57:46,468
AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery 不断地将服务器复制到 AWS，以便您可以快速恢复。
AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery continuously replicates servers into AWS so you can recover quickly.

2064
02:57:47,374 --> 02:57:54,628
当场景中提到资产的恢复时间目标时，这就是标准答案。要区分这两个概念。备份是你可以从中恢复的副本。
It is the answer when a scenario names a recovery time objective for an estate. Keep the two apart. A backup is a copy you restore from.

2065
02:57:55,406 --> 02:57:57,988
容灾是你可以进行故障转移的备用系统。
Disaster recovery is a standby you fail over to.

2066
02:57:59,374 --> 02:58:03,520
有一个命名警告，因为 Glacier 这个词现在代表两层含义。
One naming warning because the word Glacier now means two things.

2067
02:58:03,760 --> 02:58:09,860
S3 Glacier 存储类别是完全可用的，是归档数据的推荐方式。
The S3 Glacier storage classes are fully available and are the recommended way to archive data.

2068
02:58:10,574 --> 02:58:19,844
但 Amazon Glacier，即最初基于 vault 的独立服务，已于 2025 年 12 月 15 日停止接受新客户。
But Amazon Glacier, the original standalone vault-based service, stopped accepting new customers on the 15th of December 2025.

2069
02:58:20,334 --> 02:58:24,964
现有数据将一直保持可访问状态，且不需要迁移。
Existing data stays accessible indefinitely and no migration is required.

2070
02:58:25,680 --> 02:58:28,196
考试考查的是存储类别。
The exam means the storage classes.

2071
02:58:29,070 --> 02:58:36,132
如果题目提到“vaults”和“archives”而不是“buckets”和“objects”，那它描述的就是旧服务。
If a question talks about vaults and archives rather than buckets and objects, it is describing the old service.

2072
02:58:37,678 --> 02:58:40,036
这 8 种表述涵盖了大部分存储相关的题目。
8 phrasings covering most storage questions.

2073
02:58:40,320 --> 02:58:44,080
许多 Linux 实例共享文件，意味着是 EFS。
Many Linux instances sharing files means EFS.

2074
02:58:44,240 --> 02:58:52,452
Windows 和 SMB 指的是 FSx for Windows file server。单个实例需要持久磁盘则意味着 EBS。
Windows and SMB means FSX for Windows file server. A single instance needing a persistent disk means EBS.

2075
02:58:52,814 --> 02:58:56,480
任何数量的通过 HTTP 传输的数据，意味着 S3。
Any amount of data over HTTP means S3.

2076
02:58:57,358 --> 02:59:02,436
接受 12 小时检索时间的归档，意味着 Glacier Deep Archive。
Archive with 12-hour retrieval acceptable means Glacier Deep Archive.

2077
02:59:02,894 --> 02:59:06,244
不可预测的访问模式意味着智能型。
An unpredictable access pattern means intelligent.

2078
02:59:07,342 --> 02:59:08,004
分层。
Tiering.

2079
02:59:08,974 --> 02:59:11,780
替换磁带库意味着 Tape Gateway。
Replacing a tape library means tape gateway.

2080
02:59:12,654 --> 02:59:17,668
跨服务的统一备份策略意味着 AWS Backup。
And a central backup policy across services means AWS backup.

2081
02:59:18,990 --> 02:59:20,196
实战场景
Work scenario

2082
02:59:20,942 --> 02:59:21,444
1。
1.

2083
02:59:22,958 --> 02:59:27,492
一家公司将法律案件文件存储在 S3 中，并必须保留 10 年。
A company stores legal case files in S3 and must keep them for 10 years.

2084
02:59:27,918 --> 02:59:32,068
在前 90 天内它们只被读取几次，之后几乎从不被访问。
They are read a handful of times in the first 90 days and then almost never.

2085
02:59:32,718 --> 02:59:36,836
但请求可能随时到达，并且必须在一天内完成处理。
But a request can arrive at any time and must be satisfied within a day.

2086
02:59:37,742 --> 02:59:41,764
该公司希望在满足此条件的前提下，获得最低的存储成本。
The company wants the lowest storage cost that meets this.

2087
02:59:43,406 --> 02:59:44,548
停下来思考并做出决定。
Pause and decide.

2088
02:59:50,720 --> 02:59:52,132
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

2089
02:59:52,590 --> 02:59:57,508
起决定作用的细节是检索窗口，而且它被刻意设定得很宽松。
The deciding detail is the retrieval window and it is deliberately generous.

2090
02:59:58,000 --> 03:00:01,700
“必须在一天内完成”比毫秒级响应要慢得多。
Must be satisfied within a day is much slower than milliseconds.

2091
03:00:02,510 --> 03:00:07,440
选项 A、C 和 D 都会让你为速度付费。
Options A, C and D all make you pay for speed.

2092
03:00:07,694 --> 03:00:08,676
而你并不需要这些。
You do not need.

2093
03:00:14,640 --> 03:00:22,884
一定要根据题目给出的检索窗口来核对对应的类别，因为考试会精确设定这个时间，从而让一个选项正确，而相邻的选项显得浪费资源。
Always check the stated retrieval window against the class because the exam sets it precisely to make one class correct and the neighboring one wasteful.

2094
03:00:24,398 --> 03:00:25,200
实战场景。
Work scenario.

2095
03:00:25,360 --> 03:00:31,780
2. 一家公司在跨越三个可用区的 12 个 EC2 实例上运行一个内容管理应用。
2. A company runs a content management application on 12 EC2 instances across three availability zones.

2096
03:00:32,160 --> 03:00:38,660
所有 12 个实例都必须读写同一套上传的文档，且应用程序要求挂载的文件系统路径。
All 12 must read and write the same set of uploaded documents and the application expects a mounted file system path.

2097
03:00:39,438 --> 03:00:43,460
这些实例运行 Linux，且应用程序无法修改。
The instances run Linux and the application cannot be modified.

2098
03:00:44,334 --> 03:00:45,680
停下来思考并做出决定。
Pause and decide.

2099
03:00:51,520 --> 03:00:53,280
答案是 C。
The answer is C.

2100
03:00:53,680 --> 03:00:57,220
两个条款共同起作用，排除了最强的干扰项。
Two clauses work together to eliminate the strongest distractor.

2101
03:00:59,200 --> 03:01:04,260
该应用程序要求挂载的文件系统路径，且不能被修改。
The application expects a mounted file system path and it cannot be modified.

2102
03:01:04,640 --> 03:01:07,748
如果只看其中一项，S3 可能仍有争议。
Either one alone might leave S3 arguable.

2103
03:01:08,400 --> 03:01:13,760
但两者结合在一起就排除了它，因为使用 S3 需要修改应用程序。
Together they close it because using S3 would require changing the application.

2104
03:01:14,318 --> 03:01:20,100
这是本模块开头提到的排除法，考试也是按照这个逻辑设计的。
This is the elimination rule from the opening of the module and the exam plans it exactly this way.

2105
03:01:20,974 --> 03:01:23,876
选项 B 在两方面都不符合要求，因为
Option B fails on both counts since

2106
03:01:25,550 --> 03:01:28,356
EBS 是单实例且单区域的。
EBS is single instance and single zone.

2107
03:01:29,997 --> 03:01:31,197
案例场景 3
Work Scenario 3

2108
03:01:32,238 --> 03:01:36,388
一个数据科学团队在运行任务时会生成大量临时文件。
A data science team writes large temporary files while a job runs.

2109
03:01:36,814 --> 03:01:43,556
这些文件在每次运行时都会重新生成，之后不再需要，且团队要求尽可能快的磁盘吞吐量。
The files are regenerated on every run, are never needed afterwards, and the team wants the fastest possible disk throughput.

2110
03:01:44,974 --> 03:01:48,420
成本很重要，而且他们愿意随时丢失这些数据。
Cost matters and they are willing to lose the data at any time.

2111
03:01:49,390 --> 03:01:51,040
他们应该使用哪种存储？
Which storage should they use?

2112
03:01:51,374 --> 03:01:52,484
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

2113
03:01:58,702 --> 03:02:00,068
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

2114
03:02:02,542 --> 03:02:06,820
实例存储通常是错误选项，因为大多数情况下数据都很重要。
Instance store is usually the wrong answer because most data matters.

2115
03:02:07,214 --> 03:02:10,852
这个场景是个例外，而且题目明确说明了这一点。
This scenario is the exception and it says so explicitly.

2116
03:02:11,502 --> 03:02:17,252
每次运行都重新生成，之后不再需要，且愿意随时丢失数据。
Regenerated on every run, never needed afterwards, and willing to lose the data at any time.

2117
03:02:18,222 --> 03:02:22,468
这三个要素的存在就是为了让临时存储变得可行。
Those three phases exist to make ephemeral storage acceptable.

2118
03:02:22,800 --> 03:02:30,916
一旦符合这些条件，实例存储在速度和成本上都胜出，因为它物理连接在机器上且包含在实例价格中。
Once it is acceptable, instance store wins on both speed and cost because it is physically attached and included in the instance price.

2119
03:02:32,302 --> 03:02:33,924
案例场景 4。
Worked scenario 4.

2120
03:02:34,894 --> 03:02:38,640
一家公司在 S3 中有大量的研究数据存档。
A company has a large archive of research data in S3.

2121
03:02:39,040 --> 03:02:47,684
有些数据集每周下载一次，有些已经两年没动过，分析师偶尔会毫无预警地重新启用旧的数据集。
Some datasets are downloaded weekly, others untouched in two years, and analysts occasionally revive an old dataset without warning.

2122
03:02:48,654 --> 03:02:56,612
公司希望降低成本，但无法预测哪些数据会被需要，且不希望有检索延迟或费用。
The company wants to reduce cost but cannot predict which data will be needed and does not want retrieval delays or fees.

2123
03:03:00,590 --> 03:03:01,924
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

2124
03:03:08,137 --> 03:03:11,040
答案是 C。拿这个和场景一对比。
The answer is C. Compare this with scenario one.

2125
03:03:11,438 --> 03:03:15,812
这是故意设计的，因为两者都是关于存档数据，但答案却相反。
Deliberately, because both are about archive data and the answers are opposite.

2126
03:03:17,070 --> 03:03:21,840
在那个案例中，访问模式是已知的，且检索时间窗口很充裕。
There, the access pattern was known and the retrieval window was generous.

2127
03:03:22,126 --> 03:03:24,676
所以用一个生命周期规则来深度归档。
So a lifecycle rule to deep archive one.

2128
03:03:25,582 --> 03:03:30,880
而在这里，模式明确是不可预测的，并且排除了延迟和检索费用。
Here the pattern is explicitly unpredictable and both delays and retrieval fees are ruled out.

2129
03:03:31,182 --> 03:03:34,756
有三个约束条件，只有智能分层能满足所有三项。
Three constraints and only intelligent. Tiering satisfies all three.

2130
03:03:35,502 --> 03:03:38,532
可预测性是这两个问题之间的关键区别点。
Predictability is the hinge between these two questions.

2131
03:03:39,950 --> 03:03:41,028
实战场景。
Worked scenario.

2132
03:03:43,182 --> 03:03:43,760
5。
5.

2133
03:03:44,640 --> 03:03:57,520
一家公司仍在使用备份软件将本地部署的服务器备份到物理磁带，并写入磁带库。它希望停止处理磁带，转而在 AWS 中存储备份。
A company still backs up on-premises servers to physical tape using backup software that writes to a tape library. It wants to stop handling tapes and store backups in AWS instead.

2134
03:03:57,760 --> 03:04:02,148
它不想更换或重新配置现有的备份软件。
It does not want to replace or reconfigure its existing backup software.

2135
03:04:02,560 --> 03:04:03,908
暂停并做出决定。
Pause and decide.

2136
03:04:10,000 --> 03:04:11,300
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

2137
03:04:11,600 --> 03:04:19,908
选项 C 很诱人，因为 Glacier Deep Archive 确实是这类数据最终应该存放的地方，而 Tape Gateway 也能将数据存入那里。
Option C is the interesting one because Glacier Deep Archive is genuinely where this data should end up, and Tape Gateway will put it there.

2138
03:04:20,160 --> 03:04:22,468
但 C 忽略了约束条件。
What C misses is the constraint.

2139
03:04:23,022 --> 03:04:30,628
备份软件写入磁带库，如果不重新配置就无法写入 S3，而公司已经排除了重新配置的选项。
The backup software writes to a tape library and it cannot write to S3 without being reconfigured, which the company ruled out.

2140
03:04:31,182 --> 03:04:34,628
所有形式的存储网关都是基于同样的理由存在的。
Every form of storage gateway exists for that same reason.

2141
03:04:35,406 --> 03:04:42,916
现有系统遵循某种协议，你需要在不改变系统的情况下，在这些协议背后接入 AWS 存储。
An existing system speaks a protocol, and you need AWS storage behind that protocol without changing the system.

2142
03:04:44,627 --> 03:04:45,987
实战场景 6。
Work scenario 6.

2143
03:04:46,638 --> 03:04:52,324
一个位于某可用区的 EC2 实例有一个包含应用数据的 EBS 卷。
An EC2 instance in one availability zone has an EBS volume holding application data.

2144
03:04:52,640 --> 03:05:00,452
公司正在进行高可用性重新设计，需要在另一个可用区的新实例上挂载一个相同的卷。
The company is redesigning for high availability and needs an identical volume attached to a new instance in a different availability zone.

2145
03:05:01,326 --> 03:05:04,996
数据必须在极短的停机时间内完成跨区域复制。
The data must be copied across with minimal downtime.

2146
03:05:05,646 --> 03:05:06,960
应该如何操作？
How should it do this?

2147
03:05:07,246 --> 03:05:08,388
暂停并做出决定。
Pause and decide.

2148
03:05:14,542 --> 03:05:15,812
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

2149
03:05:16,334 --> 03:05:21,796
选项 C 值得特别提一下，因为它是一个听起来非常合理但实际上并不存在的虚构功能。
Option C is worth naming explicitly because it is a fabricated feature that sounds entirely plausible.

2150
03:05:22,638 --> 03:05:29,440
多可用区是一个真实的 AWS 术语，但它属于 RDS，而不是 EBS 卷。
Multi-availability zone is a real AWS term, but it belongs to RDS, not to EBS volumes.

2151
03:05:30,062 --> 03:05:36,260
考试中确实会使用从相邻服务借用真实词汇构成的虚假选项。
The exam does use invented options built from real vocabulary borrowed from a neighboring service.

2152
03:05:36,640 --> 03:05:43,108
如果一个选项描述的是你从未遇到过的功能，要保持警惕，而不是默认它是正确的。
If an option describes a feature you have never encountered, be suspicious rather than assuming the date.

2153
03:05:44,526 --> 03:05:53,124
总结一下，先判断是对象、块还是文件，并记住“可挂载的文件系统”这一要求会排除 S3。
To recap, decide object, block or file first and remember that a mountable file system requirement eliminates S3.

2154
03:05:53,966 --> 03:05:56,260
根据两个事实来选择 S3 类型。
Two facts pick an S3 class.

2155
03:05:56,910 --> 03:06:00,196
数据被读取的频率以及需要多快返回。
How often the data is read and how fast it must come back.

2156
03:06:01,070 --> 03:06:07,524
不可预测的访问意味着智能分层，而基于已知年龄规则则意味着生命周期策略。
Unpredictable access means intelligent, tiering, while a known age rule means a lifecycle policy.

2157
03:06:08,238 --> 03:06:10,852
EBS 是持久性的且受限于可用区。
EBS persists and is zone-bound.

2158
03:06:11,120 --> 03:06:16,868
实例存储速度快但会消失，而快照是数据跨越可用区和区域的方式。
Instance store is fast and disappears, and snapshots are how data crosses zones and regions.

2159
03:06:17,360 --> 03:06:19,876
NFS 和 Linux 意味着 EFS。
NFS and Linux means EFS.

2160
03:06:20,240 --> 03:06:23,492
SMB 和 Windows 意味着 FSX。
SMB and Windows means FSX.

2161
03:06:24,654 --> 03:06:26,596
下一模块，数据库。
Next module, databases.

2162
03:06:28,174 --> 03:06:36,036
AWS 故意提供多种数据库而非单一产品，其原则是每种工作负载都有适合它的形态。
AWS deliberately offers many databases rather than one on the principle that each workload has a shape that suits it.

2163
03:06:37,486 --> 03:06:39,760
考试会直接考查这一原则。
The exam tests that principle directly.

2164
03:06:40,078 --> 03:06:43,428
它会给出一个工作负载，并询问哪种数据库最合适。
It gives you a workload and asks which database fits.

2165
03:06:43,520 --> 03:06:47,428
所以这项技能是匹配形态，而不是深入了解某一个服务。
So the skill is matching a shape rather than knowing any one service deeply.

2166
03:06:49,134 --> 03:06:53,028
按顺序提出两个问题，就能解决本模块大部分内容。
Ask two questions in order and most of this module resolves.

2167
03:06:54,606 --> 03:06:56,624
首先，数据是关系型的吗？
First, is the data relational?

2168
03:06:57,262 --> 03:07:04,772
如果题目提到 SQL 连接、事务或现有的关系型架构，那么你就属于 RDS 系列。
If a question mentions SQL joins, transactions, or an existing relational schema, you are in the RDS family.

2169
03:07:06,254 --> 03:07:08,708
如果不是，再问数据是什么形态的。
If not, ask what shape the data has.

2170
03:07:09,584 --> 03:07:14,304
键值对查询、文档、图形、按时间排序的分析。
Key value lookups, documents, graphs, time-ordered analytics.

2171
03:07:14,766 --> 03:07:19,140
每种形态都有一个对应的 AWS 答案，考试要求你准确说出它。
Each shape has one AWS answer and the exam expects you to name it.

2172
03:07:20,462 --> 03:07:23,300
共有 7 个服务，每个都对应一种特定形态。
7 services, each suiting a shape.

2173
03:07:23,694 --> 03:07:27,140
RDS 是关系型的，由六种引擎提供管理。
RDS is relational with six engines managed for you.

2174
03:07:27,744 --> 03:07:34,148
Aurora 是关系型的，兼容 MySQL 和 Postgres，且性能更高。
Aurora is relational to MySQL and Postgres compatible with higher performance.

2175
03:07:34,624 --> 03:07:40,964
DynamoDB 是键值和文档类型的无服务器数据库，响应速度在毫秒级。
Dynamo DB is key value and document serverless with single-digit millisecond responses.

2176
03:07:41,838 --> 03:07:50,144
Redshift 是基于数据仓库的分析工具，采用列式存储，支持 PB 级扩展。ElastiCache 是位于较慢系统前端的内存缓存。
Redshift is analytics over a data warehouse, columnar, and petabyte scale. ElasticAche is an in-memory cache in front of something slower.

2177
03:07:50,304 --> 03:07:57,732
Neptune 用于图形数据库，重点在于事物之间的关系。DocumentDB 则服务于兼容 MongoDB 的工作负载。
Neptune is for graphs, where relationships between things are the point. And DocumentDB serves MongoDB compatible workloads.

2178
03:07:59,214 --> 03:08:03,904
这是将第 5 模块中的共享责任模型应用于数据库的情况。
This is the shared responsibility question from module 5 applied to databases.

2179
03:08:04,110 --> 03:08:08,516
使用 RDS 时，AWS 会负责修复操作系统和引擎。
With RDS, AWS patches the operating system and the engine.

2180
03:08:08,814 --> 03:08:15,300
它提供自动备份并支持秒级恢复，并且只需勾选即可实现多可用区故障转移。
It runs automated backups with point-in-time recovery and makes multi-availability zone failover a checkbox.

2181
03:08:16,046 --> 03:08:20,100
而在 EC2 上部署数据库时，这些操作都得由你来完成。
With a database on EC2, you do all of that yourself.

2182
03:08:20,304 --> 03:08:24,580
但你会获得完全的控制权，包括支持非标准引擎和版本。
But you get full control, including unsupported engines and versions.

2183
03:08:25,024 --> 03:08:27,204
RDS 是默认答案。
RDS is the default answer.

2184
03:08:27,664 --> 03:08:32,676
只有当场景中明确提到 RDS 无法实现的功能时，才选择 EC2。
Choose EC2 only when the scenario names something RDS cannot do.

2185
03:08:34,286 --> 03:08:36,900
RDS 支持六种引擎。
RDS supports six engines.

2186
03:08:37,344 --> 03:08:44,064
MySQL、Postgres、MariaDB、Oracle、SQL Server 和 DB2。
My SQL, Postgres, MariaDB, Oracle, SQL Server, and BB2.

2187
03:08:45,104 --> 03:08:51,620
引擎与应用程序现有的就是一样的，所以现有应用通常无需更改即可运行。
The engine is the same one an application already uses, so existing applications usually work unchanged.

2188
03:08:52,224 --> 03:08:57,252
这就是为什么 RDS 是平移数据库迁移的标准答案。
That is why RDS is the standard answer for lift and shift database migrations.

2189
03:08:58,126 --> 03:09:05,636
它提供具备秒级恢复功能的自动备份，以及你可以保留任意长时间的手动快照。
It provides automated backups with point-in-time recovery plus manual snapshots you keep as long as you like.

2190
03:09:06,254 --> 03:09:08,548
存储可以使用 KMS 进行加密。
Storage can be encrypted with KMS.

2191
03:09:09,344 --> 03:09:11,972
而且你无法访问操作系统。
And you have no operating system access.

2192
03:09:12,064 --> 03:09:15,204
所以，如果场景需要这种权限，就排除 RDS。
So a scenario needing that eliminates RDS.

2193
03:09:16,784 --> 03:09:24,100
Aurora 是 RDS 系列的一部分，而不是独立服务，两者的区别在于引擎兼容性。
Aurora is part of the RDS family rather than a separate service, and the separator is engine compatibility.

2194
03:09:24,686 --> 03:09:32,420
Aurora 仅兼容 MySQL 和 Postgres，并提供比标准引擎更高的吞吐量。
Aurora is MySQL and Postgres compatible only and offers higher throughput than the standard engines.

2195
03:09:33,134 --> 03:09:38,884
它在三个可用区中存储六份数据副本，并提供无服务器选项。
It stores six copies of your data across three availability zones and has a serverless option.

2196
03:09:39,344 --> 03:09:47,364
标准 RDS 还涵盖 Oracle、SQL Server、DB2 和 MariaDB，且它们是这些数据库的唯一选择。
Standard RDS also covers Oracle, SQL Server, DB2, and MariaDB and is the only option for those.

2197
03:09:47,982 --> 03:09:52,064
所以，如果涉及 Oracle 或 SQL Server，意味着使用标准 RDS，绝不是 Aurora。
So Oracle or SQL Server means standard RDS, never Aurora.

2198
03:09:53,806 --> 03:09:58,532
这就是本模块存在的目的，考试也会不断考查这一点。
This is the pair the module exists for and the exam tests it constantly.

2199
03:09:58,784 --> 03:10:08,868
多可用区部署利用同步复制在另一个区域保留备用副本，并在主节点故障时自动进行故障转移。
A multi-availability zone deployment keeps a standby copy in another zone using synchronous replication and fails over automatically if the primary fails.

2200
03:10:09,678 --> 03:10:13,264
它的存在是为了保证可用性，备用副本并不是用来提供读取服务的。
It exists for availability and the standby is not there to serve reads.

2201
03:10:13,664 --> 03:10:22,340
只读副本是使用异步复制的额外可读副本，没有自动故障转移，并且可以部署在另一个区域。
Read replicas are additional readable copies using asynchronous replication with no automatic failover, and they can live in another region.

2202
03:10:24,846 --> 03:10:27,344
为了应对故障导致的生存问题，选择多可用区。
Surviving failure means multi-AZ.

2203
03:10:28,366 --> 03:10:32,132
如果读取查询过载导致数据库压力过大，则使用只读副本。
Read queries overwhelming the database means read replicas.

2204
03:10:33,646 --> 03:10:41,124
DynamoDB 是全无服务器的键值和文档数据库。因此无需配置或打补丁。
Dynamo DB is a key value and document database that is fully serverless. So there is nothing to provision or patch.

2205
03:10:41,504 --> 03:10:46,020
它的核心卖点是在任何规模下都能提供单位数毫秒级的性能。
Its defining claim is single digit millisecond performance at any scale.

2206
03:10:46,544 --> 03:10:52,612
按需模式按请求计费，而预留容量对于稳定且可预测的负载更便宜。
On demand capacity charges per request, while provision capacity is cheaper for steady predictable load.

2207
03:10:53,486 --> 03:11:00,944
全局表跨区域复制，而 DynamoDB 加速器为微秒级读取提供内存缓存。
Global tables replicate across regions and Dynamo DB accelerator adds an in-memory cache for microsecond reads.

2208
03:11:01,358 --> 03:11:06,884
它不支持连接操作或 SQL，因此不适合复杂的关系型查询。
What it does not do is joins or SQL, so complex relational queries are the wrong fit.

2209
03:11:08,398 --> 03:11:14,372
在题库分析中，DynamoDB 和 Redshift 出现了 22 次，所以要仔细区分它们。
DynamoDB and Redshift Co. occurred 22 times in the bank analysis, so separate them carefully.

2210
03:11:14,798 --> 03:11:23,364
DynamoDB 处理大量快速的小型操作，不断通过键查找单个项目，以实时为应用程序提供服务。
DynamoDB handles many small fast operations, looking up one item by its key constantly to serve an application in real time.

2211
03:11:24,334 --> 03:11:33,060
Redshift 处理少量大型复杂查询，聚合数百万行数据来为分析师生成报告。区分点在于谁在等待。
Redshift handles few large complex queries, aggregating millions of rows to produce a report for analysts. The separator is who is waiting.

2212
03:11:33,486 --> 03:11:36,196
如果是应用程序在等待，那就是 DynamoDB。
If an application is waiting, it is DynamoDB.

2213
03:11:36,544 --> 03:11:39,140
如果是分析师在等待，那就是 Redshift。
If an analyst is waiting, it is Redshift.

2214
03:11:40,526 --> 03:11:47,012
Redshift 是专为超大规模数据集的分析查询而构建的列式数据仓库。
Redshift is a columnar data warehouse built for analytical queries over very large datasets.

2215
03:11:47,424 --> 03:11:54,916
列式存储是它处理此类工作快速的原因，因为读取三个列时不会读取其他 97 个。
Columnar storage is why it is fast for this work, because a query reading three columns does not read the other 97.

2216
03:11:55,726 --> 03:12:01,700
它使用 SQL，因此分析师和现有的商业智能工具可以直接与其配合。
It uses SQL, so analysts and existing business intelligence tools work with it directly.

2217
03:12:03,854 --> 03:12:11,140
Redshift 无服务器取消了集群管理，而 Redshift Spectrum 可以查询存储在 Amazon S3 中的数据。
Redshift serverless removes cluster management and Redshift Spectrum Queries data sitting in Amazon S3.

2218
03:12:11,918 --> 03:12:17,060
但它不用于支撑应用程序，因此避免将其用于高频率的单行查找。
But it is not for serving an application, so avoid it for high volume single row lookups.

2219
03:12:18,798 --> 03:12:26,788
ElastiCache 是位于数据库前端的内存缓存，能在微秒内处理重复读取。
Elastic Cache is an in-memory cache that sits in front of a database and serves repeated reads in microseconds.

2220
03:12:29,454 --> 03:12:35,204
它的经典用途是缓解那些读取负载主要由少数相同查询组成的数据库。
Its classic use is relieving a database whose read load is dominated by the same few queries.

2221
03:12:36,142 --> 03:12:45,924
这些引擎包括 Valkey、开源的 Redis 以及 memcached，在 2024 年 10 月 Redis 更改许可后增加了对 Valkey 的支持。
The engines are Valkyrie, Redis open source, and memcaged, with Valky support added in October 2024 after the Redis license changed.

2222
03:12:46,464 --> 03:12:50,084
它还用于会话存储、排行榜和速率限制。
It is also used for session storage, leaderboards, and rate limiting.

2223
03:12:51,024 --> 03:12:53,220
但缓存并不是数据库。
But a cache is not a database.

2224
03:12:53,504 --> 03:12:57,156
所以任何必须持久保存的数据都应该放在持久性存储中。
So anything that must persist belongs somewhere durable.

2225
03:12:58,817 --> 03:13:02,948
当出现特定关键词时，会出现两个专用答案。
Two purpose built answers that appear when their exact signal is present.

2226
03:13:03,406 --> 03:13:08,612
Amazon Neptune 是一个图形数据库，查询的是项目之间的关系。
Amazon Neptune is a graph database where the relationships between items are what you query.

2227
03:13:09,006 --> 03:13:15,524
提到的应用场景包括推荐引擎、欺诈检测环、社交网络和知识图谱。
Recommendation engines, fraud detection rings, social networks, and knowledge graphs are the named use cases.

2228
03:13:16,142 --> 03:13:24,784
Amazon Document DB 是一个兼容 MongoDB 的文档数据库，它的关键词是公司不想重写现有的 MongoDB 应用。
Amazon Document DB is a document database with MongoDB compatibility and its signal is an existing MongoDB application the company does not want to rewrite.

2229
03:13:24,944 --> 03:13:29,412
两者都是托管服务，因此 AWS 会负责补丁、备份和可用性。
Both are managed, so AWS handles patching, backups, and availability.

2230
03:13:30,990 --> 03:13:33,476
本模块有一个关于可用性的警示。
One availability warning for this module.

2231
03:13:37,390 --> 03:13:49,700
账本数据库 Amazon QLDB 已于 2025 年 7 月 31 日停止支持。AWS 的迁移路径是 Aurora Postgres。
Amazon QLDB, the ledger database, reached end of support on the 31st of July 2025. AWS's migration path was to Aurora Postgres.

2232
03:13:50,606 --> 03:14:00,036
旧的题库仍将 QLDB 作为不可变、加密可验证账本的答案，但该服务已不再存在。
Older question banks still offer QLDB as the answer for an immutable, cryptographically verifiable ledger, and that service no longer exists.

2233
03:14:01,262 --> 03:14:07,780
Amazon Keyspaces 和 Amazon MemoryDB 不在考试范围内，所以看到它们时只需识别即可，不需要深入学习。
Amazon Key Spaces and Amazon MemoryDB are not on the in scope list, so recognize them without studying them.

2234
03:14:08,558 --> 03:14:10,980
本模块中的其他内容都是最新的。
Everything else in this module is current.

2235
03:14:12,270 --> 03:14:15,024
有八种表述涵盖了大部分数据库问题。
Eight phrasings covering most database questions.

2236
03:14:15,264 --> 03:14:19,184
原封不动地迁移 Oracle 应用意味着使用 RDS。
Migrating an Oracle application unchanged means RDS.

2237
03:14:19,566 --> 03:14:23,716
单位数毫秒级的键值查询意味着 Dynamo DB。
Key value lookups at single digit milliseconds means Dynamo DB.

2238
03:14:24,464 --> 03:14:28,292
对历史数据进行商业智能分析意味着 Redshift。
Business intelligence over historical data means redshift.

2239
03:14:28,814 --> 03:14:31,204
推荐引擎意味着 Neptune。
A recommendation engine means Neptune.

2240
03:14:31,886 --> 03:14:34,628
现有的 MongoDB 工作负载意味着 Document DB。
An existing MongoDB workload means Document DB.

2241
03:14:34,864 --> 03:14:38,224
重复读取导致数据库过载意味着 ElastiCache。
Repeated reads overloading a database means Elasticash.

2242
03:14:38,384 --> 03:14:41,700
能够承受可用区故障意味着多可用区（多可用区）。
Surviving an availability zone failure means multi-AZ.

2243
03:14:42,958 --> 03:14:46,784
而报告查询导致应用程序变慢意味着只读副本。
And reporting queries slowing the application means read replicas.

2244
03:14:48,494 --> 03:14:49,956
实战案例 1。
Worked scenario 1.

2245
03:14:50,414 --> 03:14:56,384
一家公司在 Amazon RDS for Postgres 上运行关键的订单处理系统。
A company runs a critical order processing system on Amazon RDS for Postgres.

2246
03:14:57,294 --> 03:15:03,332
一个可用区故障导致数据库中断两小时，导致订单停止。
An availability zone disruption made the database unreachable for two hours halting orders.

2247
03:15:04,304 --> 03:15:12,580
该公司希望即使单个区域不可用时，数据库仍能继续提供请求，并实现自动故障转移。
The company wants the database to keep serving requests if a single zone becomes unavailable, with failover happening automatically.

2248
03:15:13,582 --> 03:15:14,980
它应该配置什么？
What should it configure?

2249
03:15:15,822 --> 03:15:16,900
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

2250
03:15:23,072 --> 03:15:24,420
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

2251
03:15:24,672 --> 03:15:33,220
选项 A 确实很有诱惑力，因为只读副本确实会在另一个可用区放一份副本，听起来像是解决了可用区故障问题。
Option A is genuinely tempting because a read replica does put a copy in another availability zone, which sounds like it addresses zone failure.

2252
03:15:33,966 --> 03:15:34,916
但有两个点让它不成立。
Two things kill it.

2253
03:15:35,374 --> 03:15:38,628
复制是异步的，所以副本可能会有延迟。
The replication is asynchronous, so the replica may lag.

2254
03:15:39,470 --> 03:15:45,316
而且提升主库是手动操作，而要求里说故障转移必须是自动的。
And promoting it is a manual action, whereas the requirement says failover must happen automatically.

2255
03:15:45,632 --> 03:15:53,380
这一个副词就决定了题目答案。当两个选项都涉及在别处放置副本时，要仔细阅读要求中是“自动”还是“手动”。
That single adverb decides the question. Read the requirement for automatic against manual whenever both options place a copy elsewhere.

2256
03:15:55,054 --> 03:15:56,164
案例 1。
Worked scenario.

2257
03:15:57,152 --> 03:16:06,916
2. 同一个订单处理数据库现在具备高可用性，但财务团队开始在工作日对它运行大量的报表查询。
2. The same order processing database is now highly available, but the finance team has begun running large reporting queries against it during the working day.

2258
03:16:07,822 --> 03:16:12,132
每当这些报告运行时，订单处理的速度就会明显变慢。
Order processing has become noticeably slower whenever those reports run.

2259
03:16:12,942 --> 03:16:15,872
这些报表可以容忍数据延迟几秒钟。
The reports can tolerate data a few seconds out of date.

2260
03:16:16,112 --> 03:16:17,312
公司应该怎么做？
What should the company do?

2261
03:16:17,614 --> 03:16:18,628
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

2262
03:16:24,782 --> 03:16:29,508
答案是 B，而且这故意选用了和案例 1 相同的数据库。
The answer is B, and this is deliberately the same database as scenario 1.

2263
03:16:30,030 --> 03:16:32,740
同样的系统，不同的问题，不同的答案。
Same system, different problem, different answer.

2264
03:16:33,390 --> 03:16:36,452
那里的问题是应对故障，所以用多可用区。
There the problem was surviving failure, so multi-AZ.

2265
03:16:37,390 --> 03:16:42,372
这里的问题是处理带有写入操作的读负载，所以用只读副本。
Here the problem is red load computing with writes, so read replicas.

2266
03:16:43,182 --> 03:16:47,140
注意关于“容忍数据延迟几秒”的那句话。
Notice the sentence about tolerating data a few seconds out of date.

2267
03:16:47,534 --> 03:16:50,436
这句话的存在是为了让异步复制变得可行。
That exists to make asynchronous replication acceptable.

2268
03:16:52,014 --> 03:16:55,952
它的出现是一个强烈的暗示，说明题目意在考察只读副本。
And its presence is a strong hint that read replicas are intended.

2269
03:16:57,262 --> 03:16:58,564
案例 3。
Verb scenario 3.

2270
03:16:58,958 --> 03:17:07,172
一家零售商希望通过寻找购买了相似组合商品的客户，然后沿着这些联系点向外延伸几步，来推荐产品。
A retailer wants to suggest products by finding customers who bought similar combinations of items, then following those connections, several steps outward.

2271
03:17:07,630 --> 03:17:11,268
这些查询是关于商品和客户如何相互连接的。
The queries are about how items and customers connect to one another.

2272
03:17:12,206 --> 03:17:17,156
现有的关系型查询在执行此类操作时需要多次连接，并且变得太慢了。
Existing relational queries doing this require many joins and have become too slow.

2273
03:17:17,518 --> 03:17:19,712
哪种数据库是为这种情况设计的？
Which database is designed for this?

2274
03:17:20,078 --> 03:17:21,188
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

2275
03:17:27,312 --> 03:17:29,232
答案是 C。
The answer is C.

2276
03:17:30,894 --> 03:17:33,604
有三个信号指向图形数据库。
Three signals point at a graph database.

2277
03:17:34,112 --> 03:17:36,484
查询内容是关于事物如何连接。
The queries are about how things connect.

2278
03:17:36,752 --> 03:17:39,492
它们会沿着联系点向外延伸几步。
They follow connections several steps outward.

2279
03:17:39,952 --> 03:17:47,908
而且关系型版本需要多次连接且太慢，而这正是图形数据库存在的意义所在。
And the relational version needs many joins and is too slow, which is precisely the problem graph databases exist to solve.

2280
03:17:48,526 --> 03:17:54,148
仅凭“推荐引擎”这个词通常就足够让你选择 Neptune 了。
The phrase recommendation engine alone is usually enough to reach for Neptune.

2281
03:17:54,606 --> 03:18:00,004
但这里的场景也描述了遍历模式，这是更核心的原因。
But here the scenario also describes the traversal pattern, which is the more honest reason.

2282
03:18:01,678 --> 03:18:03,332
做题场景 4。
Worked scenario 4.

2283
03:18:04,302 --> 03:18:08,196
一个新闻网站在 Amazon RDS 中存储文章。
A news website stores articles in Amazon RDS.

2284
03:18:08,974 --> 03:18:17,636
90% 的数据库读取请求都是针对那 20 篇热门文章，每小时重复请求数千次，导致数据库压力巨大。
90% of database reads are requests for the same 20 popular articles, repeated thousands of times an hour, and the database is struggling.

2285
03:18:18,222 --> 03:18:19,908
这些文章很少更改。
The articles change rarely.

2286
03:18:20,814 --> 03:18:24,100
降低数据库负载最合适的方法是什么？
What is the most appropriate way to reduce database load?

2287
03:18:25,070 --> 03:18:26,340
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

2288
03:18:32,430 --> 03:18:33,792
答案是 B。
The answer is B.

2289
03:18:34,352 --> 03:18:41,380
把它和场景 2 做个对比，因为两者都描述了读取负载过载导致数据库压力大，但答案不同。
Compare this with scenario 2 because both describe read load overwhelming a database and the answers differ.

2290
03:18:41,998 --> 03:18:47,396
在那个案例中，读取的是大量多变的报表查询，这正是只读副本擅长处理的。
There, the reads were large varied reporting queries, which a replica handles well.

2291
03:18:48,078 --> 03:18:54,020
而这里的读取是相同的，即每小时请求数千次的 20 个项目，且这些项目很少更改。
Here the reads are the same, 20 items requested thousands of times an hour, and the items rarely change.

2292
03:18:54,702 --> 03:18:56,196
这就是缓存的特征。
That is the cache signature.

2293
03:18:56,750 --> 03:19:00,388
重复性高且低波动性意味着弹性哈希。
Repetition and low volatility together mean elastic hash.

2294
03:19:01,422 --> 03:19:03,844
多变的查询意味着只读副本。
Varied queries mean read replicas.

2295
03:19:05,518 --> 03:19:06,916
做题场景 5。
Work scenario 5.

2296
03:19:07,598 --> 03:19:11,812
一家游戏公司需要存储玩家资料和会话状态。
A gaming company needs to store player profiles and session state.

2297
03:19:12,192 --> 03:19:19,524
它预期用户量会从数千人不可预测地增长到数百万，并需要稳定的单位数毫秒级读取。
It expects unpredictable growth from thousands to millions of players and needs consistent single digit millisecond reads.

2298
03:19:20,014 --> 03:19:23,044
它不想管理服务器或规划容量。
It does not want to manage servers or plan capacity.

2299
03:19:24,014 --> 03:19:28,676
每个资料都通过玩家标识符检索，不需要复杂的连接。
Each profile is retrieved by player identifier with no complex joints.

2300
03:19:29,806 --> 03:19:31,556
它应该使用哪种数据库？
Which database should it use?

2301
03:19:32,398 --> 03:19:33,700
停下来思考一下。
Pause and decide.

2302
03:19:39,822 --> 03:19:47,364
答案是 C，这个场景堆叠了四个 DynamoDB 的信号，方便你练习同时识别这些特征。
The answer is C, and this scenario stacks four dynamo DB signals so you can practice recognizing them together.

2303
03:19:48,462 --> 03:19:50,756
面向百万用户的不可预测增长。
Unpredictable growth to millions.

2304
03:19:52,494 --> 03:19:55,556
稳定的单位数毫秒级读取。
Consistent single-digit millisecond reads.

2305
03:19:56,238 --> 03:19:59,300
无需管理服务器，也不需要规划容量。
No servers to manage and no capacity planning.

2306
03:20:00,302 --> 03:20:03,684
以及通过单一标识符检索且无连接。
And retrieval by a single identifier with no joints.

2307
03:20:04,622 --> 03:20:10,340
选项 B 是最接近的干扰项，因为 Aurora 无服务器确实可以自动扩展。
Option B is the closest miss because Aurora serverless does scale automatically.

2308
03:20:11,118 --> 03:20:12,932
但它仍然是一个关系型引擎。
But it is still a relational engine.

2309
03:20:13,390 --> 03:20:17,604
而最后一句话告诉你，关系型功能将无法被利用。
And the last sentence tells you the relational features would go unused.

2310
03:20:19,246 --> 03:20:22,596
总结一下，先判断是否是关系型，再看具体形态。
To recap, ask relational first, then shape.

2311
03:20:23,278 --> 03:20:25,572
多可用区对应的是可用性。
Multi-availability zone is availability.

2312
03:20:25,998 --> 03:20:30,596
而只读副本对应的是性能，自动故障转移是区分这两者的关键点。
While red replicas are performance, an automatic failover is the deciding word between them.

2313
03:20:31,758 --> 03:20:34,437
重复相同的读取意味着弹性缓存，
Repeated identical reads means elastic cache,

2314
03:20:35,438 --> 03:20:38,500
而多样化的高强度读取意味着只读副本。
while varied heavy reads means red replicas.

2315
03:20:39,342 --> 03:20:44,880
为应用程序提供服务意味着 DynamoDB，而回答业务问题意味着 Redshift。
Serving an application means DynamoDB while answering a business question means red shift.

2316
03:20:45,040 --> 03:20:52,932
Aurora 只兼容 MySQL 或 Postgres。所以 Oracle 和 SQL Server 意味着标准 RDS。
And Aurora is MySQL or Postgres compatible only. So Oracle and SQL server means standard RDS.

2317
03:20:53,280 --> 03:20:56,036
下一模块：网络和内容分发。
Next module, networking and content delivery.

2318
03:20:57,550 --> 03:21:01,156
在题库分析中，网络占 19%。
Networking accounted for 19% of the bank analysis.

2319
03:21:01,838 --> 03:21:09,188
这里有八个实战案例，因为题目考查的是精确的辨析，而不是单纯知道某个服务的功能。
It has eight worked scenarios here because the questions turn on precise distinctions rather than on knowing what a service does.

2320
03:21:09,774 --> 03:21:14,148
两个服务可能都能让你连接到 AWS，但只有一个符合要求。
Two services can both connect you to AWS and only one fits the requirement.

2321
03:21:15,822 --> 03:21:17,636
这个模块涵盖三个问题。
This module answers three questions.

2322
03:21:17,920 --> 03:21:25,892
流量从哪里进入你的环境（即网关和子网）？什么决定流量是否被允许（即安全组和网络 ACL）？
Where does traffic enter your environment, which is gateways and subnets? What decides whether traffic is allowed, which is security groups and network?

2323
03:21:27,342 --> 03:21:28,228
网络 ACL。
SELs.

2324
03:21:29,230 --> 03:21:35,332
还有，如何让远方的用户访问到内容（即 CloudFront、Route 53 和 Global Accelerator）？
And how does traffic reach users who are far away, which is CloudFront, Route 53, and Global Accelerator?

2325
03:21:36,622 --> 03:21:40,708
这里的几乎每一道题都属于这三个中的其中一个。
Almost every question here belongs to exactly one of those three.

2326
03:21:42,446 --> 03:21:48,804
VPC 是 AWS 云中逻辑隔离的区域，你可以在其中控制网络布局。
AVPC is a logically isolated section of the AWS cloud where you control the network layout.

2327
03:21:49,280 --> 03:21:58,180
VPC 属于一个区域，其中的每个子网属于一个可用区，这是决定题目答案的关键细节。
AVPC belongs to one region and each subnet within it belongs to one availability zone, which is a detail that decides questions.

2328
03:21:59,840 --> 03:22:03,236
路由表决定从子网发出的流量去往何处。
Root tables decide where traffic from a subnet is sent.

2329
03:22:04,078 --> 03:22:15,364
VPC 本身不收费，但其中的某些组件，比如 NAT 网关，是收费的。而且除非你刻意配置，否则 VPC 内部的任何内容都无法从互联网访问。
The VPC itself costs nothing, though some components inside it, such as NAT gateways, do. And nothing inside a VPC is reachable from the internet unless you deliberately arrange it.

2330
03:22:16,974 --> 03:22:20,484
这个区别比大家想象的要简单。
This distinction is simpler than people expect.

2331
03:22:20,880 --> 03:22:28,804
如果路由表将发往互联网的流量发送到互联网网关，那么该子网就是公有的；否则就是私有的。
A subnet is public if its root table sends internet-bound traffic to an internet gateway and private if it does not.

2332
03:22:29,280 --> 03:22:31,076
这就是全部区别。
That is the entire difference.

2333
03:22:31,680 --> 03:22:37,220
公有子网包含负载均衡器、NAT 网关和堡垒机。
Public subnets hold load balancers, NAT gateways and bastion hosts.

2334
03:22:38,080 --> 03:22:45,828
私有子网包含应用服务器和数据库，它们只能通过 NAT 网关访问外网。
Private subnets hold application servers and databases, which reach the internet outbound only through a NAT gateway.

2335
03:22:46,222 --> 03:22:49,060
这两类子网在其他方面没有区别。
Nothing else about the two kinds of subnet differs.

2336
03:22:50,542 --> 03:23:02,640
互联网网关允许 VPC 和互联网之间的双向流量。NAT 网关允许私有资源访问外网，同时阻止任何入站流量。
An Internet gateway allows two-way traffic between a VPC and the Internet. A NAT gateway lets private resources reach the internet outbound while blocking anything inbound.

2337
03:23:02,800 --> 03:23:06,724
它位于公有子网中，而私有子网的流量会路由到它。
It sits in a public subnet with the private subnet routing to it.

2338
03:23:07,182 --> 03:23:11,972
NAT 网关按小时和处理的 GB 数计费。
NAT gateways are charged per hour and per gigabyte processed.

2339
03:23:12,430 --> 03:23:14,404
所以它们也会出现在成本相关的题目中。
So they turn up in cost questions too.

2340
03:23:15,214 --> 03:23:22,720
并且注意，NAT 网关不是安全控制手段。它允许出站流量，而不是过滤流量。
And note that a NAT gateway is not a security control. It permits outbound traffic rather than filtering it.

2341
03:23:24,046 --> 03:23:37,540
VPC 的核心在于这一点。附加到实例网络接口的“安全组”是有状态的，因此回程流量会自动允许，且只包含允许规则。
The VPC classic and worth holding precisely. Security groups attached to an instance's network interface are stateful, so return traffic is allowed automatically and have allow rules only.

2342
03:23:38,830 --> 03:23:42,080
“网络ACL”是附加到子网的，并且是无状态的。
Network ACS attached to a subnet and are stateless.

2343
03:23:42,240 --> 03:23:44,800
所以回程流量需要专门的规则。
So return traffic needs its own rule.

2344
03:23:45,326 --> 03:23:50,884
它们包含允许和拒绝规则，按编号顺序评估，有两个分隔符。
They have both allow and deny rules evaluated in numbered order, two separators.

2345
